INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('invention-of-the-wheel','Invention of the Wheel',-3500,'Middle East','The wheel and plough are developed in Mesopotamia, transforming agriculture, transportation, and trade across the ancient world. The sail appears in Egypt around the same period, enabling maritime commerce along the Nile and beyond. Together these three inventions lay the practical foundation for complex civilization and long-distance exchange.','medium',9,NULL,NULL,NULL,0);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('sumerian-writing','Invention of Sumerian Writing',-3200,'Middle East','The Sumerians of ancient Mesopotamia develop cuneiform, the world''s earliest writing system, initially used for recording trade transactions on clay tablets. This invention enables the transmission of complex knowledge, law, and literature across generations and marks the beginning of recorded history.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,1);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('first-cities-mesopotamia','First Cities Founded in Mesopotamia',-3000,'Middle East','The first true cities emerge in Sumer, the southern region of Mesopotamia, with Uruk growing into the world''s largest settlement with a population in the tens of thousands. These urban centers develop specialized labor, centralized administration, monumental architecture, and complex trade networks stretching across the ancient Near East. The Sumerian city-state becomes the template for human political and social organization.','medium',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,2);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('indus-valley-begins','Indus Valley Civilization Begins',-2600,'South Asia','One of the world''s earliest urban civilizations emerges in the Indus River valley, featuring advanced city planning, drainage systems, and trade networks. Cities like Mohenjo-daro and Harappa flourish with populations in the tens of thousands.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,3);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('egyptian-pyramids-built','Great Pyramid of Giza Built',-2560,'Africa','The Great Pyramid of Giza is constructed as a tomb for Pharaoh Khufu, requiring an estimated 2.3 million stone blocks and decades of labor. It stands as the tallest man-made structure in the world for nearly four millennia and remains one of the seven wonders of the ancient world.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,4);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('code-of-hammurabi','Code of Hammurabi Established',-1754,'Middle East','Babylonian king Hammurabi promulgates one of the earliest and most complete written legal codes, covering commerce, property, family, and criminal law. The code, inscribed on a stone stele, introduces the principle of presumption of innocence and establishes the idea of law as a public institution.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,5);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('phoenician-alphabet-invented','Phoenician Alphabet Invented',-1600,'Middle East','The Phoenicians develop the first widely used alphabetic writing system, consisting of 22 consonant letters derived from earlier Semitic scripts used in the Sinai Peninsula. Unlike the complex syllabic systems of Mesopotamia and Egypt, the alphabet''s simplicity allows merchants and administrators to learn it rapidly, and it spreads across the Mediterranean world through Phoenician trade networks. Nearly all modern alphabets, including Greek, Latin, Arabic, and Hebrew, descend from this Phoenician innovation.','hard',9,NULL,NULL,NULL,6);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('fall-of-troy','Fall of Troy',-1200,'Europe','The city of Troy, located in present-day northwest Turkey, falls to a coalition of Greek forces after a legendary ten-year siege, according to ancient tradition immortalized in Homer''s Iliad. The Trojan horse — a giant wooden horse concealing Greek soldiers — becomes one of history''s most enduring stories of deception in warfare. Archaeological excavations at Hisarlik confirm a real Bronze Age city was violently destroyed around this period, lending historical weight to the legend.','easy',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,7);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-mahabharata','Battle of Kurukshetra',-1000,'South Asia','The legendary war described in the Mahabharata epic, fought between the Pandavas and Kauravas on the plains of Kurukshetra. The conflict forms the backdrop for the Bhagavad Gita and remains central to Hindu philosophy and culture.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,8);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('greek-olympics-ancient','Ancient Olympic Games Established',-776,'Europe','The ancient Olympic Games are held for the first time at Olympia in ancient Greece as a religious festival honoring Zeus, featuring athletic and chariot racing competitions. The games are held every four years for over a millennium and become the inspiration for the modern Olympic movement.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,9);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('founding-of-rome','Founding of Rome',-753,'Europe','According to Roman tradition, the city of Rome is founded by Romulus on the Palatine Hill, marking the beginning of a civilization that will shape Western history for over a millennium. The city grows from a small settlement of Latin and Sabine peoples into the heart of a vast empire.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,10);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('ironworking-spreads','Ironworking Spreads Across the Old World',-670,'Global','Iron smelting technology, first developed in Anatolia around 1200 BC, spreads widely across Europe, Asia, and Africa during the early first millennium BC. Iron''s abundance and superior hardness compared to bronze democratize the production of agricultural tools and weapons, reshaping economies, armies, and societies across three continents. The Iron Age marks a fundamental turning point in human technological development, enabling more productive farming, more lethal warfare, and larger political structures.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,11);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('babylonian-conquest-jerusalem','Babylonian Conquest of Jerusalem',-588,'Middle East','King Nebuchadnezzar II of Babylon conquers Jerusalem, destroys Solomon''s Temple, and deports much of the Jewish population to Babylon in what becomes known as the Babylonian captivity. The exile profoundly reshapes Jewish theology and identity, accelerating the development of strict monotheism and the compilation of the Hebrew Bible. The event is foundational to the history of Judaism, Christianity, and Islam, and the longing to return to Jerusalem becomes a defining element of Jewish culture.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,12);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('thales-solar-eclipse','Thales Predicts a Solar Eclipse',-585,'Europe','The Greek philosopher Thales of Miletus successfully predicts a solar eclipse, marking one of the first recorded instances of scientific reasoning applied to natural phenomena rather than divine intervention. Thales seeks material and natural explanations for the world around him, establishing the foundational attitude that underpins Western science and philosophy. Ancient tradition credits him as the first philosopher, the originator of a tradition of rational inquiry that runs through Socrates, Plato, and Aristotle.','hard',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,13);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('birth-of-buddha','Birth of Siddhartha Gautama',-563,'South Asia','Siddhartha Gautama is born in Lumbini into a royal family of the Shakya clan. He would later renounce his privileged life and attain enlightenment, becoming the Buddha and founding one of the world''s major religions.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,14);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('birth-of-confucius','Birth of Confucius',-551,'East Asia','Kong Qiu, known to the world as Confucius, is born in the state of Lu in present-day Shandong, China. His teachings on ethics, social harmony, filial piety, and good governance — collected by his disciples in the Analects — shape Chinese civilization for over two millennia. Confucianism becomes the dominant philosophical and political framework across East Asia, profoundly influencing law, education, family structure, and governance from China to Korea, Japan, and Vietnam.','easy',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,15);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('cyrus-founds-persian-empire','Cyrus the Great Founds the Persian Empire',-550,'Middle East','Cyrus II of Persia defeats the Median, Lydian, and Babylonian kingdoms in quick succession to establish the Achaemenid Empire, the largest empire the world had yet seen, stretching from the Aegean Sea to the Indus River. Renowned for tolerating the customs and religions of conquered peoples, Cyrus permits the Jewish exiles in Babylon to return to their homeland and rebuild their temple, an act celebrated in the Hebrew Bible. The Cyrus Cylinder, recording his policies, is often cited as one of humanity''s earliest declarations of human rights.','medium',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,16);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('roman-republic-founded','Roman Republic Established',-509,'Europe','The Romans expel their last king Tarquin the Proud and establish a republic governed by elected consuls and the Senate. The Roman Republic''s system of checks and balances and mixed constitution becomes an enduring model for later democracies and republican governments.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,17);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('greek-democracy-athens','Athenian Democracy Established',-508,'Europe','Cleisthenes introduces democratic reforms in Athens, establishing a system of governance in which citizens participate directly in decision-making through the assembly. Often called the ''Father of Democracy,'' his reforms create the world''s first democratic political system.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,18);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-marathon','Battle of Marathon',-490,'Europe','A small Athenian army defeats a much larger Persian force at Marathon, halting the first Persian invasion of Greece. The victory becomes a defining moment of Greek identity and the legend of a messenger running to Athens to announce the victory gives birth to the modern marathon race.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,19);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('hippocrates-medicine','Hippocrates Founds Rational Medicine',-400,'Europe','Hippocrates of Kos establishes medicine as a rational discipline separate from superstition and religion, emphasizing observation, diagnosis, and prognosis. His approach, recorded in the Hippocratic Corpus, forms the foundation of Western medical practice, and the Hippocratic Oath remains a touchstone of medical ethics.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,20);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('socrates-execution','Execution of Socrates',-399,'Europe','The philosopher Socrates is condemned to death by an Athenian jury on charges of impiety and corrupting the youth, choosing to drink hemlock rather than flee. His execution, recorded by his student Plato, becomes the defining martyr story of Western philosophy and raises enduring questions about truth, justice, and civil disobedience.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,21);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('platos-academy-founded','Plato Founds the Academy',-387,'Europe','Plato establishes the Academy in Athens, often considered the first institution of higher learning in the Western world, where philosophy, mathematics, and science are taught. It attracts scholars from across the Greek world and operates for nearly nine centuries, shaping the development of Western intellectual tradition.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,22);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('alexander-conquests','Alexander the Great''s Conquests Begin',-334,'Europe','Alexander III of Macedonia crosses into Asia and begins a decade of military campaigns that will create one of history''s largest empires, stretching from Greece to northwestern India. His conquests spread Greek culture across the ancient world and usher in the Hellenistic period.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,23);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('alexander-founds-alexandria','Alexander the Great Founds Alexandria',-332,'Africa','After conquering Egypt from the Persians, Alexander the Great founds the city of Alexandria on the Mediterranean coast, envisioning a great center of Hellenistic culture and commerce linking Greece with Egypt. The city grows into one of the ancient world''s largest metropolises and home to the legendary Library of Alexandria, an institution that attracts scholars from across the known world and preserves the accumulated knowledge of antiquity. Alexandria remains the intellectual capital of the Mediterranean world for centuries after Alexander''s death.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,24);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-gaugamela','Battle of Gaugamela',-331,'Middle East','Alexander the Great decisively defeats the Persian King Darius III at Gaugamela in present-day Iraq, effectively ending the Achaemenid Persian Empire despite being significantly outnumbered. Alexander''s oblique advance and the disciplined Macedonian phalanx shatter the Persian army, opening the road to Babylon, Persepolis, and the East. The battle marks the decisive replacement of Persian hegemony in the Near East with Hellenistic Greek culture, reshaping the civilizations of three continents.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,25);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('death-of-alexander','Death of Alexander the Great',-323,'Middle East','Alexander the Great dies in Babylon at the age of 32, possibly from typhoid fever compounded by heavy drinking, though the cause remains debated. Having built the largest empire the world had yet seen — stretching from Greece to the borders of India — he leaves no clear successor, reportedly saying the empire should go ''to the strongest.'' His death triggers the Wars of the Diadochi, in which his generals carve up the empire into rival Hellenistic kingdoms and spread Greek culture from Egypt to Central Asia.','easy',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,26);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('ashoka-becomes-emperor','Ashoka Becomes Mauryan Emperor',-268,'South Asia','Ashoka ascends to the throne of the Mauryan Empire, which at its height spans most of the Indian subcontinent. His reign would become one of the most significant in Indian history due to his later conversion to Buddhist principles of nonviolence.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,27);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('punic-wars','Punic Wars Between Rome and Carthage',-264,'Europe','Rome and the North African city-state of Carthage fight three devastating wars over more than a century for dominance of the western Mediterranean. The wars culminate in the complete destruction of Carthage and establish Rome as the unchallenged master of the Mediterranean world.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,28);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('ashoka-converts-to-buddhism','Ashoka Converts to Buddhism',-260,'South Asia','Horrified by the devastation caused by the Kalinga War, Ashoka embraces Buddhism and adopts a policy of nonviolence and dharma. He erects pillars and edicts across his empire promoting Buddhist values, transforming Indian governance.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,29);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('eratosthenes-measures-earth','Eratosthenes Measures the Earth''s Circumference',-240,'Africa','The Greek mathematician and librarian Eratosthenes calculates the circumference of the Earth by measuring the difference in the angle of the sun''s shadow between Alexandria and Syene at the summer solstice, deducing that the two cities are separated by about one-fiftieth of the full circle. His result of approximately 40,000 kilometers is remarkably close to the modern measurement. The achievement stands as one of antiquity''s greatest scientific accomplishments, demonstrating the power of mathematical reasoning applied to physical observation.','hard',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,30);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('qin-unification-china','Qin Dynasty Unifies China',-221,'East Asia','Qin Shi Huangdi defeats all rival Warring States and unifies China for the first time under a single emperor, establishing the Qin dynasty. He standardizes weights, measures, writing, and currency across the empire and begins construction of the Great Wall of China.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,31);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('great-wall-china','Construction of the Great Wall of China Begins',-215,'East Asia','Emperor Qin Shi Huangdi orders the connection and extension of existing northern walls to create a unified defensive barrier against nomadic invasions. The Great Wall, extended and rebuilt by successive dynasties especially the Ming, becomes one of history''s greatest engineering achievements.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,32);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('silk-road-opens','Silk Road Trade Route Opens',-130,'East Asia','Han dynasty emperor Wudi sends envoy Zhang Qian westward, opening sustained trade connections between China, Central Asia, and eventually the Mediterranean world. The Silk Road carries not only silk and spices but ideas, religions, technologies, and diseases across continents for centuries.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,33);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('first-triumvirate','First Triumvirate Formed',-60,'Europe','Julius Caesar, Pompey the Great, and Marcus Crassus form an informal political alliance known as the First Triumvirate, effectively dominating Roman politics and marginalizing the Senate. The alliance allows Caesar to secure the consulship and a military command in Gaul, where he spends the next decade building the veteran army that will carry him to supreme power. The Triumvirate marks the beginning of the end for the Roman Republic, setting in motion the events that lead to civil war and the age of emperors.','hard',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,34);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('caesar-crosses-rubicon','Caesar Crosses the Rubicon',-49,'Europe','Julius Caesar leads his battle-hardened army across the Rubicon river into Italy, violating Roman law that forbade generals from bringing troops into the Republic''s heartland. The act, accompanied by the famous phrase ''the die is cast,'' triggers a civil war that will ultimately destroy the Roman Republic. Caesar''s crossing has become a lasting metaphor for any irrevocable decision that commits one fully to a course of action.','easy',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,35);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('julius-caesar-assassination','Julius Caesar Assassinated',-44,'Europe','Roman dictator Julius Caesar is stabbed to death by a group of senators including Brutus and Cassius on the steps of the Senate on the Ides of March. His assassination plunges Rome into civil war and ultimately leads to the transformation of the Republic into the Roman Empire.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,36);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('augustus-first-emperor','Augustus Becomes First Roman Emperor',-27,'Europe','Octavian, nephew of Julius Caesar, receives the title Augustus from the Roman Senate, marking the beginning of the Roman Empire and the end of the Republic. His long and stable reign inaugurates the Pax Romana, two centuries of relative peace across the vast Roman world.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,37);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('pax-romana','Pax Romana Begins',-27,'Europe','The accession of Augustus initiates the Pax Romana, roughly two centuries of relative peace and stability across the Roman Empire during which trade, law, and culture flourish. The period sees the construction of roads, aqueducts, and monumental architecture that will shape European civilization for millennia.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,38);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('birth-of-jesus','Birth of Jesus of Nazareth',-4,'Middle East','Jesus of Nazareth is born in the Roman province of Judea, an event that marks year one of the Christian calendar and the origin point of the world''s largest religion. His teachings of love, forgiveness, and salvation would transform the spiritual and cultural landscape of human civilization.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,39);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('crucifixion-of-jesus','Crucifixion of Jesus',29,'Middle East','Jesus of Nazareth is executed by crucifixion under the Roman prefect Pontius Pilate in Jerusalem, an event recorded in both Christian scripture and Roman historical sources. His followers'' belief in his subsequent resurrection becomes the central doctrine of Christianity, transforming a small Jewish sect into a religion that spreads across the Roman Empire and eventually to every corner of the world. The crucifixion and its theological interpretation remain the defining moment of the Christian faith, observed by over two billion people today.','easy',9,NULL,NULL,NULL,40);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('great-fire-of-rome','Great Fire of Rome',64,'Europe','A devastating fire sweeps through Rome for six days, destroying or severely damaging ten of the city''s fourteen districts and leaving hundreds of thousands homeless. Emperor Nero, almost certainly absent when the fire began, is later accused by rumor and legend of starting it himself — a charge almost certainly false. The disaster gives Nero the opportunity to rebuild much of Rome in a grander style and leads to the first major Roman persecution of Christians, whom he scapegoats for the catastrophe.','medium',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,41);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('eruption-of-vesuvius','Eruption of Mount Vesuvius',79,'Europe','Mount Vesuvius erupts catastrophically, burying the Roman cities of Pompeii and Herculaneum under meters of volcanic ash and pyroclastic material and killing thousands within hours. The disaster is vividly described by Pliny the Younger in letters that become the first detailed eyewitness accounts of a volcanic eruption. The remarkably preserved ruins, rediscovered and excavated from the eighteenth century onward, provide an unparalleled snapshot of daily life in the Roman world.','easy',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,42);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('paper-invented-china','Paper Invented in China',105,'East Asia','Cai Lun, a court official of the Eastern Han dynasty, refines and standardizes the process of making paper from bark, hemp, rags, and fishing nets, presenting his improved method to the emperor. Paper rapidly replaces more expensive and cumbersome writing materials such as silk and bamboo strips. The invention spreads westward via the Silk Road over subsequent centuries, transforming record-keeping, administration, literature, and communication across Eurasia.','medium',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,43);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('hadrians-wall','Hadrian''s Wall Construction Begins',122,'Europe','The Roman Emperor Hadrian orders the construction of a defensive wall stretching coast to coast across northern Britain, from the Solway Firth to the River Tyne, to control movement between Roman Britain and the unconquered tribes of Caledonia. The wall is the most heavily fortified frontier in the entire Roman Empire, lined with forts, milecastles, and turrets garrisoned by tens of thousands of soldiers. It remains the best-preserved Roman military structure in the world and a UNESCO World Heritage Site.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,44);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('maya-classic-period','Maya Classic Period',250,'Americas','The Maya civilization enters its Classic Period, building monumental city-states like Tikal and Palenque with sophisticated writing, calendars, and astronomical observations. Maya mathematics independently develops the concept of zero and their calendar system achieves remarkable precision.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,45);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('christianity-roman-empire','Edict of Milan: Christianity Legalized',313,'Europe','Emperor Constantine issues the Edict of Milan, legalizing Christianity throughout the Roman Empire and ending decades of persecution of Christians. Constantine''s personal conversion and this decree set in motion the transformation of the Roman Empire into a Christian state.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,46);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('gupta-empire-founded','Gupta Empire Founded',320,'South Asia','Chandragupta I establishes the Gupta Empire in northern India, inaugurating a period often called the Golden Age of India. Under Gupta rule, advances in mathematics, astronomy, literature, and the arts would flourish across the subcontinent.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,47);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('constantinople-founded','Constantinople Founded',324,'Europe','Emperor Constantine the Great dedicates his new capital at the ancient Greek city of Byzantium, renaming it Constantinople in his own honor and investing it with the institutions and architectural splendor of a new Rome. Strategically positioned at the crossroads of Europe and Asia controlling the Bosphorus strait, the city becomes the wealthiest and most powerful city in the Christian world for over a thousand years. As the capital of the Byzantine Empire, Constantinople preserves Roman law and Greek learning through the medieval period until its fall to the Ottoman Turks in 1453.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,48);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('nalanda-university-founded','Nalanda University Founded',427,'South Asia','Nalanda is established as one of the world''s first residential universities in Bihar, attracting scholars from across Asia. At its peak, it housed thousands of students and monks studying a curriculum spanning Buddhist philosophy, logic, grammar, and medicine.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,49);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('attila-hun-invasions','Attila the Hun Invades Europe',450,'Europe','Attila leads the Hunnic Empire in devastating raids into the Eastern and Western Roman Empire, earning the epithet ''Scourge of God'' for his destruction of cities and countryside. Though stopped at the Battle of the Catalaunian Plains, his invasions accelerate the fragmentation of the Western Roman Empire.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,50);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('fall-of-roman-empire-west','Fall of the Western Roman Empire',476,'Europe','The last Western Roman Emperor, Romulus Augustulus, is deposed by the Germanic chieftain Odoacer, marking the conventional end of the Western Roman Empire and the beginning of the Middle Ages. The fall reshapes Europe into a mosaic of Germanic kingdoms with profound consequences for civilization.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,51);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('aryabhata-heliocentric','Aryabhata Proposes Earth''s Rotation',499,'South Asia','The Indian mathematician and astronomer Aryabhata publishes the Aryabhatiya, proposing that the Earth rotates on its axis and calculating the approximate value of pi. His work establishes foundational concepts in Indian mathematics and astronomy.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,52);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('birth-of-muhammad','Birth of Muhammad',570,'Middle East','Muhammad ibn Abdullah is born in Mecca, in the Arabian Peninsula, into the Quraysh tribe, the guardians of the Kaaba. He would receive his first divine revelation at the age of forty, beginning the delivery of the message that becomes the Quran. As the founder of Islam, Muhammad''s life and teachings shape one of the world''s largest religions and transform the political, cultural, and spiritual landscape of the Middle East, Africa, and far beyond.','easy',9,NULL,NULL,NULL,53);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('harsha-reign-begins','Harsha''s Reign Begins',606,'South Asia','Harshavardhana becomes ruler of a large empire centered at Kannauj, uniting much of northern India after the fall of the Gupta Empire. His reign is noted for religious tolerance, support of Buddhist and Hindu scholarship, and diplomatic exchanges with China.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,54);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('founding-of-islam','Muhammad Receives First Revelation',610,'Middle East','The Prophet Muhammad receives the first revelation of the Quran in the Cave of Hira near Mecca, which marks the beginning of Islam. Over the following decades, his preaching gives rise to a new monotheistic religion that will reshape the spiritual, political, and cultural landscape of the world.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,55);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('hijra','The Hijra: Muhammad Migrates to Medina',622,'Middle East','Facing persecution from the Quraysh in Mecca, Muhammad and his followers migrate to the city of Medina in an event known as the Hijra. In Medina, Muhammad establishes the first Muslim community, drafts the Constitution of Medina creating a political-religious framework for governance, and begins building the mosque that becomes the model for Islamic worship. The year of the Hijra is taken as Year One of the Islamic lunar calendar, marking it as the defining moment in the founding of Islam as both a faith and a political community.','medium',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,56);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('invention-of-zero','Invention of Zero in India',628,'South Asia','Indian mathematician Brahmagupta formalizes the rules for arithmetic operations involving zero in his work Brahmasphutasiddhanta, treating zero as a number in its own right for the first time. This revolutionary concept, combined with the Hindu-Arabic numeral system, becomes foundational to all of modern mathematics and computing.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,57);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('arab-traders-kerala','Arab Traders Arrive in Kerala',629,'South Asia','Arab traders establish early Muslim communities on the Malabar Coast, initiating a long history of Islamic influence in Kerala. According to tradition, the Cheraman Perumal mosque built during this period is one of the oldest mosques in Asia.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,58);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('islamic-caliphate-expands','Islamic Caliphate Expands Across Arabia',632,'Middle East','Following the death of the Prophet Muhammad, Abu Bakr becomes the first caliph and launches military campaigns that rapidly expand Islamic rule across Arabia and beyond. Within a century, the Caliphate stretches from Spain to Central Asia, one of the fastest imperial expansions in history.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,59);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('moors-invade-spain','Moors Invade Spain',711,'Europe','A Muslim army under Tariq ibn Ziyad crosses the Strait of Gibraltar — a name derived from ''Jabal al-Tariq,'' or ''Rock of Tariq'' — and defeats the Visigothic King Roderic, rapidly overrunning most of the Iberian Peninsula. The resulting Muslim territory of Al-Andalus becomes a center of Islamic culture, science, and philosophy, transmitting Greek and Arabic knowledge to medieval Europe through translations in Toledo and Cordoba. The Moorish presence in Spain lasts nearly eight centuries until the final Reconquista in 1492.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,60);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('woodblock-printing-china','Woodblock Printing Invented in China',730,'East Asia','Woodblock printing is developed in Tang dynasty China, enabling text and images carved in relief on wooden blocks to be reproduced cheaply and repeatedly on paper. The technology enables the mass production of Buddhist texts, government documents, and eventually paper money, dramatically increasing access to information and accelerating literacy. Woodblock printing spreads across East Asia before Bi Sheng''s invention of movable type three centuries later further refines the process.','hard',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,61);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-tours','Battle of Tours',732,'Europe','Frankish leader Charles Martel defeats an advancing Muslim army at Tours in central France, halting the northward expansion of the Umayyad Caliphate into Western Europe. Many historians regard this battle as decisive in preserving Christianity as the dominant religion of Europe.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,62);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('islamic-golden-age','Islamic Golden Age Begins',786,'Middle East','The reign of Harun al-Rashid and the establishment of the House of Wisdom in Baghdad inaugurates a golden age of Islamic science, mathematics, philosophy, and medicine. Scholars translate and extend Greek knowledge while making original contributions in algebra, optics, astronomy, and medicine.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,63);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('viking-raids-begin','Viking Age Begins',793,'Europe','Norse warriors raid the monastery of Lindisfarne on the English coast in one of the first recorded Viking attacks, inaugurating the Viking Age. Over the following centuries, Norsemen range from Newfoundland to Russia, Constantinople to North Africa, as traders, settlers, and raiders reshaping European history.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,64);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('charlemagne-crowned-emperor','Charlemagne Crowned Holy Roman Emperor',800,'Europe','Pope Leo III crowns Charlemagne, King of the Franks, as Holy Roman Emperor on Christmas Day in St. Peter''s Basilica, creating a new imperial power in Western Europe. Charlemagne''s reign unites much of Western Europe, promotes literacy and education, and shapes the political and cultural identity of medieval Europe.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,65);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('gunpowder-invented','Gunpowder Invented in China',850,'East Asia','Chinese alchemists experimenting with elixirs of immortality discover the explosive properties of a mixture of sulfur, charcoal, and saltpeter, inventing gunpowder. The discovery revolutionizes warfare when it reaches Europe centuries later, making medieval fortifications obsolete and transforming military tactics worldwide.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,66);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('kievan-rus-founded','Founding of Kievan Rus',882,'Europe','The Varangian prince Oleg captures Kiev and makes it the capital of a new state uniting the East Slavic and Norse trading communities along the Dnieper river route connecting Scandinavia to Byzantium. Kievan Rus becomes the first major East Slavic political entity, laying the cultural, religious, and political foundations for the later nations of Russia, Ukraine, and Belarus. Its adoption of Orthodox Christianity from Byzantium in 988 shapes Eastern European civilization for centuries.','hard',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,67);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('chola-rajaraja-peak','Chola Dynasty Reaches Its Peak',985,'South Asia','Rajaraja I ascends to the Chola throne and expands the dynasty into a maritime empire dominating South India and parts of Southeast Asia. He commissions the great Brihadeeswarar temple at Thanjavur, a masterpiece of Dravidian architecture.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,68);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('viking-exploration-north-america','Vikings Reach North America',1000,'Americas','Leif Erikson leads a Norse expedition that establishes a settlement at L''Anse aux Meadows in what is now Newfoundland, Canada, nearly five centuries before Columbus. Archaeological evidence confirms this as the first known European contact with the Americas.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,69);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('mahmud-ghazni-somnath','Mahmud of Ghazni Raids Somnath',1026,'South Asia','Sultan Mahmud of Ghazni leads one of his many raids into the Indian subcontinent, sacking the wealthy Somnath temple on the Gujarat coast. The raid becomes a defining moment in the history of Muslim-Hindu relations on the subcontinent.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,70);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('printing-movable-type-china','Bi Sheng Invents Movable Type in China',1040,'East Asia','Bi Sheng of the Song dynasty invents movable type printing using ceramic characters, four centuries before Gutenberg''s press in Europe. The technology enables the mass production of books and spreads literacy and knowledge across China and East Asia.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,71);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('great-schism','Great Schism Divides Christianity',1054,'Europe','The Pope in Rome and the Patriarch of Constantinople mutually excommunicate each other, formalizing the split of Christianity into the Roman Catholic and Eastern Orthodox churches. The division, rooted in centuries of theological disagreements over papal authority, the nature of the Holy Spirit, and the use of images in worship, proves permanent and is never healed. It reshapes the religious map of Europe and contributes to the divergent political and cultural development of Western and Eastern European civilizations.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,72);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-hastings','Battle of Hastings',1066,'Europe','William, Duke of Normandy, defeats King Harold II at the Battle of Hastings and becomes King of England, initiating the Norman Conquest. This transformative event reshapes English language, culture, and governance through the fusion of Norman French and Anglo-Saxon traditions.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,73);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('university-of-bologna-founded','University of Bologna Founded',1088,'Europe','The University of Bologna is established in Italy, becoming the oldest continuously operating university in the Western world, initially focused on the systematic study of Roman law. It attracts students from across Europe seeking formal legal training and establishes the model of a secular institution dedicated to higher learning with recognized degrees and faculties. The university movement rapidly spreads, with Oxford, Paris, Cambridge, and dozens of other institutions founded over the following two centuries, fundamentally reshaping European intellectual life.','hard',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,74);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('first-crusade','First Crusade Launched',1096,'Middle East','Pope Urban II calls for a Christian military campaign to recapture Jerusalem from Muslim rule, launching the First Crusade. Armies of knights and peasants march across Europe and the Middle East, culminating in the brutal conquest of Jerusalem, and initiating two centuries of crusading warfare.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,75);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('invention-of-compass','Magnetic Compass Developed in China',1100,'East Asia','Chinese navigators begin using magnetic compasses for maritime navigation during the Song dynasty, revolutionizing sea travel by enabling reliable orientation regardless of weather or visibility. The compass spreads to the Islamic world and Europe within centuries, enabling the Age of Exploration.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,76);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('genghis-khan-unifies-mongols','Genghis Khan Unifies the Mongols',1206,'East Asia','Temujin is proclaimed Genghis Khan (''Universal Ruler'') at a great assembly of Mongol chieftains after uniting the warring steppe tribes under his command. He goes on to launch the conquests that create the largest contiguous land empire in history, though at the cost of catastrophic destruction across Eurasia.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,77);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('magna-carta','Magna Carta Signed',1215,'Europe','English King John is forced by rebellious barons to seal the Magna Carta at Runnymede, establishing for the first time that the king was subject to the rule of law. The document becomes a cornerstone of constitutional governance and influences legal systems around the world.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,78);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('marco-polo-china','Marco Polo Travels to China',1271,'East Asia','Marco Polo departs Venice on a journey that takes him to the court of Kublai Khan in China, where he spends seventeen years observing Mongol and Chinese civilization. His memoir inspires generations of European explorers, including Christopher Columbus, and sparks European fascination with the riches of Asia.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,79);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('mongol-empire-peak','Mongol Empire Reaches Greatest Extent',1279,'East Asia','Under Kublai Khan, the Mongol Empire reaches its greatest territorial extent, becoming the largest contiguous land empire in history spanning from the Pacific Ocean to Eastern Europe. The Pax Mongolica facilitates unprecedented trade and cultural exchange across Eurasia along the Silk Road.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,80);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-bannockburn','Battle of Bannockburn',1314,'Europe','Scottish forces under King Robert the Bruce decisively defeat the much larger English army of Edward II near Stirling Castle, securing Scottish independence from English domination. The battle is the high point of the First War of Scottish Independence and remains the defining moment of Scottish national identity, still commemorated today. Although the formal recognition of Scottish independence required the Treaty of Edinburgh-Northampton fourteen years later, Bannockburn effectively ends England''s attempt to absorb Scotland.','hard',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,81);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('black-death-arrives-china','Black Death Spreads from Central Asia',1331,'East Asia','Bubonic plague devastates parts of China and Central Asia under Mongol rule before spreading westward along trade routes. The disease, carried by fleas on rats, ultimately reaches Europe via Crimea and kills an estimated 75-200 million people across Eurasia.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,82);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('vijayanagara-empire-founded','Vijayanagara Empire Founded',1336,'South Asia','Harihara I and Bukka Raya I establish the Vijayanagara Empire in the Deccan, which becomes a major Hindu kingdom resisting the Sultanates of the north. The empire''s capital at Hampi grows into one of the largest cities in the world during its peak.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,83);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('hundred-years-war','Hundred Years War',1337,'Europe','England and France enter a prolonged series of conflicts over the French throne lasting over a century, featuring legendary battles at Crécy and Agincourt and the emergence of Joan of Arc. The war forges distinct French and English national identities and ends with England''s expulsion from France.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,84);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('black-death-europe','Black Death Strikes Europe',1347,'Europe','The bubonic plague arrives in Sicily from Crimea and rapidly spreads across Europe, killing an estimated one-third to one-half of the European population within a few years. The catastrophic loss reshapes European society by disrupting feudal systems, labor markets, and the Church''s authority.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,85);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('ming-dynasty-founded','Ming Dynasty Founded in China',1368,'East Asia','Zhu Yuanzhang expels the Mongol Yuan dynasty and establishes the Ming dynasty, restoring Han Chinese rule to China. The Ming period sees the rebuilding of the Great Wall, the construction of the Forbidden City, and the remarkable maritime expeditions of Zheng He across Asia and Africa.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,86);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('timur-sacks-delhi','Timur Sacks Delhi',1398,'South Asia','Timur, the Central Asian conqueror known in the West as Tamerlane, leads his army into the Indian subcontinent and sacks Delhi, massacring much of its population and stripping the city of its accumulated wealth. The Delhi Sultanate never fully recovers from the blow, plunging northern India into a century of fragmentation and instability. Timur''s campaign represents one of the most destructive military incursions in Indian history and reshapes the subcontinent''s political landscape, indirectly creating the conditions for the later Mughal conquest.','medium',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,87);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('renaissance-begins-florence','Renaissance Begins in Florence',1401,'Europe','A cultural and intellectual movement centered in Florence begins reviving interest in classical Greek and Roman art, philosophy, and science, with patronage from wealthy families like the Medici. The Renaissance produces extraordinary achievements in painting, sculpture, architecture, and literature that fundamentally reshape Western culture.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,88);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('zheng-he-voyages','Zheng He''s Great Maritime Voyages',1405,'East Asia','Chinese admiral Zheng He leads the first of seven massive naval expeditions visiting Southeast Asia, India, the Persian Gulf, and the East African coast with a fleet dwarfing contemporary European ships. The voyages showcase Ming China''s power and facilitate diplomatic and trade relations across the Indian Ocean world.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,89);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('age-of-exploration-portugal','Portugal Opens African Coastal Trade',1415,'Africa','Portugal''s conquest of Ceuta and Prince Henry the Navigator''s systematic sponsorship of African coastal exploration launches the European Age of Exploration. Portuguese navigators gradually map the West African coast, establishing trade posts and introducing European maritime expansion that will reshape global history.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,90);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('joan-of-arc-burned','Joan of Arc Executed',1431,'Europe','Joan of Arc, the teenage peasant girl who led French armies to pivotal victories claiming divine guidance, is burned at the stake by English-allied Burgundians after being convicted of heresy. Posthumously rehabilitated and eventually canonized, she becomes France''s patron saint and a symbol of national resistance.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,91);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('gutenberg-printing-press','Gutenberg Invents Printing Press',1440,'Europe','Johannes Gutenberg develops the movable-type printing press in Mainz, Germany, enabling the mass production of books for the first time in Europe. The invention revolutionizes the spread of knowledge, fuels the Renaissance and Reformation, and is considered one of the most transformative technologies in history.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,92);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('aztec-empire-peak','Aztec Empire Reaches Its Peak',1440,'Americas','Under Moctezuma I, the Aztec Triple Alliance expands rapidly to control much of Mesoamerica, extracting tribute from hundreds of subject peoples. Tenochtitlan, built on an island in Lake Texcoco, becomes one of the largest cities in the world with a population rivaling contemporary European capitals.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,93);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('fall-of-constantinople','Fall of Constantinople',1453,'Middle East','Ottoman Sultan Mehmed II captures Constantinople after a two-month siege, ending the Byzantine Empire and marking the fall of the last vestige of the Roman Empire. The conquest transforms the city into Istanbul, the new Ottoman capital, and is often cited as the end of the Middle Ages.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,94);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('guru-nanak-born','Guru Nanak Born',1469,'South Asia','Guru Nanak, the founder of Sikhism, is born in the Punjab region. His teachings emphasizing equality, monotheism, and service to humanity attract followers from both Hindu and Muslim communities and give rise to a new religious tradition.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,95);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('renaissance-da-vinci','Leonardo da Vinci Active',1490,'Europe','Leonardo da Vinci produces his most celebrated works and notebooks during this period, combining mastery of painting with scientific investigation of anatomy, engineering, and natural phenomena. His breadth of genius — from the Last Supper to designs for flying machines — epitomizes the Renaissance ideal of the universal man.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,96);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('columbus-reaches-americas','Columbus Reaches the Americas',1492,'Americas','Christopher Columbus, sailing under Spanish patronage, lands in the Bahamas, initiating sustained contact between Europe and the Americas. His voyages begin the Columbian Exchange, a massive transfer of plants, animals, diseases, and cultures that permanently transforms both hemispheres.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,97);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('vasco-da-gama-india-route','Vasco da Gama Opens Sea Route to India',1498,'South Asia','Portuguese explorer Vasco da Gama completes the first direct sea voyage from Europe to India by sailing around Africa, arriving at Calicut on the Kerala coast. The discovery of this sea route breaks the Arab monopoly on Asian trade and inaugurates the Portuguese Maritime Empire.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,98);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('renaissance-michelangelo','Michelangelo Paints the Sistine Chapel',1508,'Europe','Michelangelo spends four years painting the iconic ceiling of the Sistine Chapel in the Vatican, depicting scenes from Genesis in an unprecedented display of artistic mastery and physical endurance. The work, including the famous ''Creation of Adam,'' stands as one of the supreme achievements of Western art.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,99);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('protestant-reformation','Protestant Reformation Begins',1517,'Europe','Martin Luther posts his Ninety-Five Theses on the door of a church in Wittenberg, challenging corrupt practices in the Catholic Church and igniting the Protestant Reformation. The movement permanently fractures Western Christianity, sparks religious wars, and reshapes European culture and politics.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,100);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('magellan-circumnavigation','First Circumnavigation of the Globe',1519,'Global','Ferdinand Magellan leads an expedition that becomes the first to circumnavigate the globe, though Magellan himself is killed in the Philippines. The voyage, completed by Sebastian Elcano, definitively proves the spherical nature of Earth and vastly expands European geographic knowledge.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,101);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('spanish-conquest-mexico','Spanish Conquest of the Aztec Empire',1519,'Americas','Hernán Cortés leads a Spanish expedition that, with the aid of indigenous allies and devastating diseases, overthrows the Aztec Empire and its emperor Moctezuma within two years. The conquest of Mexico opens the way for Spanish colonization of the Americas and the destruction of Mesoamerican civilizations.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,102);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('first-battle-of-panipat','First Battle of Panipat',1526,'South Asia','Babur defeats Ibrahim Lodi of the Delhi Sultanate at Panipat, using artillery to decisive effect for the first time in Indian warfare. This battle marks the end of the Delhi Sultanate and the beginning of Mughal rule over the Indian subcontinent.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,103);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('babur-founds-mughal-empire','Babur Founds the Mughal Empire',1526,'South Asia','Following his victory at Panipat, Babur establishes the Mughal Empire, which will eventually become one of the most powerful and culturally rich empires in Indian history. Babur is also remembered as a poet and memoirist through his autobiography, the Baburnama.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,104);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('conquest-of-peru-inca','Spanish Conquest of the Inca Empire',1532,'Americas','Francisco Pizarro and a small band of Spanish conquistadors capture and eventually execute the Inca emperor Atahualpa, initiating the conquest of the Inca Empire in South America. Disease and internal divisions help the Spanish rapidly dismantle one of history''s largest and most sophisticated empires.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,105);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('humayun-defeated-kanauj','Humayun Defeated at Kanauj',1540,'South Asia','The Afghan chieftain Sher Shah Suri defeats Mughal emperor Humayun at the Battle of Kanauj, forcing him into a fifteen-year exile. Sher Shah''s brief reign introduces administrative and revenue reforms that would later be adopted and expanded by Akbar.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,106);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('copernicus-heliocentric','Copernicus Publishes Heliocentric Theory',1543,'Europe','Nicolaus Copernicus publishes his theory that Earth and other planets orbit the Sun, directly challenging the prevailing geocentric model supported by the Church. The Copernican Revolution triggers a fundamental shift in scientific thinking and sets the stage for the broader Scientific Revolution.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,107);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('portuguese-arrive-japan','Portuguese Arrive in Japan',1543,'East Asia','Portuguese traders shipwrecked on the island of Tanegashima introduce firearms to Japan, transforming Japanese warfare and accelerating political change. The arrival begins a period of contact that brings Christianity, new technologies, and trade goods to Japan while exposing it to European influence.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,108);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('second-battle-of-panipat','Second Battle of Panipat',1556,'South Asia','The young Mughal emperor Akbar, guided by regent Bairam Khan, defeats the Hindu general Hemu at Panipat, consolidating Mughal control over northern India. This battle ensures the survival of the Mughal Empire after the tumultuous reign of Humayun.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,109);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('shakespeare-born','William Shakespeare Born',1564,'Europe','William Shakespeare is born in Stratford-upon-Avon, England, in the same year that Michelangelo dies, as if the torch of Renaissance genius passes between them. Over his career he writes 37 plays and 154 sonnets that explore the full range of human experience — ambition, jealousy, love, power, and mortality — with unprecedented psychological depth and linguistic brilliance. His works, from Hamlet and King Lear to A Midsummer Night''s Dream and The Tempest, remain the most performed and studied literary works in history.','easy',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,110);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('mughal-akbar-administration','Akbar Establishes Mansabdari System',1571,'South Asia','Emperor Akbar introduces the Mansabdari system, a unified administrative and military ranking structure that integrates Mughal and Rajput nobles into a single imperial hierarchy. This administrative innovation provides the organizational backbone of the Mughal Empire at its height.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,111);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-haldighati','Battle of Haldighati',1576,'South Asia','Maharana Pratap of Mewar battles the Mughal forces led by Man Singh at Haldighati in a fierce but inconclusive engagement. Though Pratap''s forces are outnumbered and he retreats, he becomes a symbol of Rajput resistance to Mughal dominance.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,112);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('akbar-din-i-ilahi','Akbar Proclaims Din-i-Ilahi',1582,'South Asia','Emperor Akbar establishes Din-i-Ilahi, a syncretic religious movement blending elements of Islam, Hinduism, Zoroastrianism, and other faiths. Though it attracts few followers, it exemplifies Akbar''s policy of religious tolerance and his attempt to unify his diverse empire.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,113);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('spanish-armada-defeated','Spanish Armada Defeated',1588,'Europe','The English fleet and stormy weather destroy the Spanish Armada sent by King Philip II to invade England, marking a turning point in European naval dominance. The defeat weakens Spanish imperial power and accelerates England''s rise as a major maritime and colonial power.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,114);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('renaissance-shakespeare','Shakespeare Writes His Greatest Works',1600,'Europe','William Shakespeare writes his greatest tragedies including Hamlet, Othello, King Lear, and Macbeth during the height of his creative powers. His works explore the full range of human experience with unparalleled psychological depth and linguistic richness, shaping the English language and world literature.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,115);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('east-india-company-founded','East India Company Founded',1600,'Europe','Queen Elizabeth I grants a royal charter to the East India Company, giving it a monopoly on English trade with the East Indies and the power to wage war and make treaties. Initially focused on spices and textiles, the company gradually transforms into a political and military power, eventually governing large swaths of South Asia directly on behalf of the British Crown. The East India Company becomes the world''s most powerful private enterprise and the primary instrument of British colonialism in Asia, ruling India for over 250 years.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,116);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('death-of-elizabeth-i','Death of Elizabeth I',1603,'Europe','Queen Elizabeth I of England dies at Richmond Palace after a reign of nearly 45 years, ending the Tudor dynasty that had shaped England since 1485. Her reign, celebrated as the Elizabethan era, saw England emerge as a major European power, the flourishing of literature and theatre under Shakespeare and Marlowe, and the beginnings of English overseas expansion. She is succeeded by James VI of Scotland, who unites the English and Scottish crowns as James I, beginning the Stuart era and moving England toward the constitutional conflicts of the following century.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,117);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('galileo-telescope','Galileo Turns Telescope to the Heavens',1609,'Europe','Galileo Galilei uses an improved telescope to make detailed astronomical observations including the moons of Jupiter and the phases of Venus, providing powerful evidence for the Copernican heliocentric model. His findings bring him into conflict with the Catholic Church but fundamentally advance astronomy.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,118);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('thirty-years-war','Thirty Years War Begins',1618,'Europe','A conflict beginning with a Protestant rebellion in Bohemia draws most of Europe''s major powers into a devastating war fought primarily on German soil. The war, ending three decades later with the Peace of Westphalia, reshapes the European political order, establishes state sovereignty, and kills millions.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,119);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('pilgrims-land-plymouth','Pilgrims Land at Plymouth',1620,'North America','The Mayflower arrives at Plymouth, Massachusetts, carrying 102 passengers — mostly English Separatists seeking religious freedom from the Church of England — after a grueling ten-week voyage. Before landing, the male passengers sign the Mayflower Compact, one of the first governing documents in the New World establishing self-rule by consent of the governed. The Plymouth Colony becomes a founding symbol of American identity, democratic values, and the tradition of seeking religious freedom that draws millions of immigrants to North America.','easy',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,120);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('taj-mahal-construction-begins','Construction of the Taj Mahal Begins',1632,'South Asia','Emperor Shah Jahan commissions the Taj Mahal in Agra as a mausoleum for his beloved wife Mumtaz Mahal, who died in childbirth. The monument, completed roughly twenty years later, is considered one of the finest examples of Mughal architecture and a UNESCO World Heritage Site.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,121);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('galileo-inquisition','Galileo Faces the Inquisition',1633,'Europe','The Roman Inquisition puts Galileo Galilei on trial for supporting the Copernican heliocentric theory in his Dialogue, forcing him to recant under threat of torture. His trial becomes the defining symbol of the conflict between religious authority and scientific inquiry.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,122);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('english-civil-war','English Civil War',1642,'Europe','Conflict between King Charles I and Parliament erupts into civil war, with Oliver Cromwell''s New Model Army defeating royalist forces. The war leads to the execution of Charles I, the short-lived Commonwealth republic, and ultimately establishes the principle of parliamentary sovereignty in England.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,123);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('signing-of-treaty-westphalia','Peace of Westphalia Signed',1648,'Europe','The Peace of Westphalia ends the Thirty Years War and the Eighty Years War, establishing the principle of state sovereignty and non-interference in other states'' internal affairs. The settlement is often considered the foundation of the modern international system of nation-states.','hard',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,124);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('execution-of-charles-i','Execution of Charles I',1649,'Europe','King Charles I of England is tried for treason by a specially convened Parliamentary court and executed by beheading outside the Banqueting House in London. This unprecedented act — the public trial and execution of a reigning monarch by his own subjects — sends shockwaves across Europe and fundamentally alters the relationship between the Crown and Parliament. England briefly becomes a Commonwealth republic under Oliver Cromwell before the monarchy is restored eleven years later, but the episode permanently establishes the principle that the king is not above the law.','medium',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,125);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('hobbes-leviathan','Hobbes Publishes Leviathan',1651,'Europe','Thomas Hobbes publishes Leviathan, arguing that without government human life would be ''solitary, poor, nasty, brutish, and short,'' and that people rationally surrender some freedoms to a sovereign authority in exchange for security and order. The work establishes the social contract as a foundational concept of modern political philosophy, providing a secular rather than divine basis for political authority. Hobbes''s framework, developed and challenged by Locke and Rousseau, shapes all subsequent thinking about the relationship between individuals, society, and the state.','hard',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,126);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('english-restoration','English Monarchy Restored',1660,'Europe','Charles II enters London in triumph, restoring the monarchy after eleven years of Puritan Commonwealth rule following his father''s execution. The Restoration brings a cultural renaissance in England — theaters reopen, the arts flourish, and the court becomes a center of wit and libertinism after the austerity of Cromwellian rule. The period also sees the founding of the Royal Society, cementing England''s place at the forefront of the Scientific Revolution.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,127);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('great-plague-london','Great Plague of London',1665,'Europe','The last major outbreak of bubonic plague in England strikes London, killing an estimated 100,000 people — roughly a quarter of the city''s population — in less than eighteen months. The epidemic forces King Charles II and his court to flee the capital, disrupting trade and governance. The Great Fire of London the following year inadvertently helps end the epidemic by destroying much of the overcrowded, rat-infested housing in which the disease spread most readily.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,128);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('great-fire-london','Great Fire of London',1666,'Europe','A fire starting in a bakery on Pudding Lane sweeps through the medieval City of London for three days, destroying over 13,000 houses, 87 churches including the old St Paul''s Cathedral, and the city''s commercial heart. Despite the enormous destruction, few deaths are confirmed, and the fire inadvertently helps end the bubonic plague ravaging the city by destroying rat-infested slums. Architect Christopher Wren leads the rebuilding effort, creating the iconic new St Paul''s Cathedral and transforming London into a more modern, fire-resistant city.','easy',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,129);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('shivaji-crowned-chhatrapati','Shivaji Crowned as Chhatrapati',1674,'South Asia','Shivaji Bhonsale is crowned Chhatrapati at Raigad Fort, formally establishing the Maratha Kingdom as an independent sovereign state. His guerrilla warfare tactics and administrative innovations created a powerful Hindu empire that would eventually challenge Mughal dominance.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,130);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('newton-laws-of-motion','Newton Publishes Laws of Motion',1687,'Europe','Isaac Newton publishes Principia Mathematica, laying out his three laws of motion and universal law of gravitation, unifying terrestrial and celestial mechanics. This monumental work forms the foundation of classical physics and remains one of the most influential scientific texts ever written.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,131);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('glorious-revolution','Glorious Revolution in England',1688,'Europe','King James II of England is overthrown and replaced by William of Orange in a largely bloodless coup that establishes constitutional monarchy and parliamentary supremacy. The subsequent Bill of Rights limits royal power and guarantees parliamentary privileges, shaping the British democratic tradition.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,132);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('mughal-empire-zenith-aurangzeb','Mughal Empire Reaches Maximum Extent',1707,'South Asia','Emperor Aurangzeb''s death marks both the maximum territorial extent of the Mughal Empire and the beginning of its rapid decline. His costly Deccan campaigns, religious intolerance, and the power of regional rulers exhaust the empire''s resources and trigger the fragmentation that allows the British East India Company to expand.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,133);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('act-of-union-1707','Act of Union Creates Great Britain',1707,'Europe','The Acts of Union unite the kingdoms of England and Scotland into a single Kingdom of Great Britain with one Parliament sitting at Westminster, ending over seven centuries of separate Scottish statehood. The union, controversial in Scotland and achieved partly through political pressure and financial incentives, creates the political entity that will dominate global trade, science, and empire over the following two centuries. Great Britain''s combined resources and political stability underpin the Industrial Revolution and the expansion of a British Empire that at its height covers a quarter of the world''s land surface.','medium',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,134);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('euler-konigsberg-bridges','Euler Solves the Königsberg Bridge Problem',1735,'Europe','The Swiss mathematician Leonhard Euler proves that it is impossible to walk through the city of Königsberg crossing each of its seven bridges exactly once, in the process founding the mathematical field of graph theory. By abstracting the city''s geography into nodes and edges, Euler creates a new framework for analyzing connectivity and networks that has no precedent. The paper is considered the first work in graph theory and topology and becomes foundational to modern network analysis, computer science, logistics, and the study of social networks.','hard',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,135);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('trans-atlantic-slave-trade-peak','Peak of the Transatlantic Slave Trade',1750,'Africa','The transatlantic slave trade reaches its peak volume in the mid-eighteenth century, with over 80,000 Africans forcibly transported to the Americas annually. The trade, which forcibly displaced an estimated 12 million Africans across three centuries, represents one of history''s greatest human catastrophes and shapes the demographic and cultural landscape of the Americas.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,136);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-plassey','Battle of Plassey',1757,'South Asia','Robert Clive of the British East India Company defeats the Nawab of Bengal, Siraj ud-Daulah, at Plassey through a combination of military force and strategic treachery. This decisive battle marks the beginning of British political control over India.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,137);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('industrial-revolution-textile','Industrial Revolution Transforms Britain',1760,'Europe','Britain leads a transformation from manual craft production to machine-based manufacturing in factories, dramatically increasing industrial output and triggering mass urbanization. The Industrial Revolution creates new social classes, alters working conditions, and sets the template for modern economic development worldwide.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,138);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('east-india-company-bengal','East India Company Assumes Control of Bengal',1765,'South Asia','The British East India Company receives the Diwani rights — the right to collect revenue from Bengal, Bihar, and Orissa — through the Treaty of Allahabad. This marks a decisive shift from a trading company to a governing power controlling vast territories.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,139);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('steam-engine-watt','James Watt Improves the Steam Engine',1769,'Europe','James Watt develops a dramatically improved steam engine with a separate condenser, greatly increasing its efficiency and making it practical for widespread industrial use. His invention becomes the driving force of the Industrial Revolution, powering factories, mines, locomotives, and ships.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,140);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('boston-tea-party','Boston Tea Party',1773,'Americas','American colonists disguised as Mohawk warriors dump 342 chests of British East India Company tea into Boston Harbor in protest of taxation without representation. The dramatic act of defiance galvanizes colonial opposition to British rule and pushes events toward the American Revolution.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,141);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('opium-trade-china-east-india','British East India Company Begins Opium Trade',1773,'East Asia','The British East India Company establishes a monopoly on opium production in Bengal and begins exporting it to China, creating a highly profitable trade that generates millions of addicts. The resulting trade imbalance and Chinese attempts to suppress the trade lead to the Opium Wars.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,142);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('american-revolution','American Revolution',1776,'Americas','The thirteen American colonies declare independence from British rule and fight a revolutionary war, producing the Declaration of Independence and a new republican government. The revolution establishes the United States and becomes a model for democratic revolutions worldwide.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,143);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('american-declaration','Declaration of Independence Signed',1776,'Americas','The Continental Congress adopts the Declaration of Independence, drafted primarily by Thomas Jefferson, proclaiming the thirteen colonies'' separation from Britain and articulating the Enlightenment principles of natural rights and government by consent. The document becomes one of history''s most influential political texts.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,144);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('wealth-of-nations-published','Adam Smith Publishes The Wealth of Nations',1776,'Europe','Scottish economist Adam Smith publishes An Inquiry into the Nature and Causes of the Wealth of Nations on the same day the American colonies declare independence, laying the foundations of modern economic theory. Smith argues that free markets, driven by individual self-interest and coordinated by the ''invisible hand'' of price signals, generate prosperity more efficiently than state direction of the economy. The book becomes the foundational text of classical economics, its ideas shaping capitalist policy from the Industrial Revolution to the present day.','medium',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,145);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('american-war-independence-ends','Treaty of Paris Ends American Revolution',1783,'Americas','Britain signs the Treaty of Paris recognizing American independence and ceding vast territories east of the Mississippi River to the new United States. The treaty marks the successful conclusion of the American Revolution and creates the foundation for American westward expansion.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,146);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('founding-of-united-states','United States Constitution Ratified',1788,'Americas','The United States ratifies its Constitution, establishing a federal republic with separation of powers, a system of checks and balances, and protections for individual rights. The Constitution becomes one of the most influential governing documents in history, serving as a model for democratic constitutions worldwide.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,147);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('french-revolution','French Revolution',1789,'Europe','The French monarchy is overthrown in a sweeping revolution driven by Enlightenment ideals of liberty and equality, leading to radical political transformation, the execution of the king, and a Reign of Terror. The revolution reverberates across Europe and reshapes modern political thought around liberty, nationalism, and democracy.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,148);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('french-revolution-storming-bastille','Storming of the Bastille',1789,'Europe','Parisian revolutionaries storm the Bastille prison fortress on July 14th, freeing political prisoners and seizing weapons in the opening act of the French Revolution. The storming becomes the defining symbol of the revolution and is still commemorated annually as France''s national holiday.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,149);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('french-revolution-declaration','Declaration of the Rights of Man',1789,'Europe','France''s National Assembly adopts the Declaration of the Rights of Man and of the Citizen, establishing principles of individual liberty, equality before the law, and popular sovereignty. The document becomes a foundational text of modern democracy and human rights, influencing constitutions and declarations worldwide.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,150);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('haitian-revolution','Haitian Revolution',1791,'Americas','Enslaved people in the French colony of Saint-Domingue launch a massive uprising that becomes the only successful slave revolution in history, leading to the creation of Haiti as the world''s first Black republic. The revolution terrifies slaveholding nations and becomes a global symbol of Black freedom.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,151);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('abolition-slavery-france','France Abolishes Slavery',1794,'Europe','The French National Convention abolishes slavery in all French territories, making France the first European colonial power to do so, largely driven by the slave uprising in Saint-Domingue. The decree is later reversed by Napoleon but eventually reinstated permanently.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,152);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('first-vaccine-smallpox','Smallpox Vaccine Invented',1796,'Europe','Edward Jenner demonstrates that inoculation with cowpox material protects against smallpox, developing the world''s first vaccine. His discovery saves hundreds of millions of lives and establishes the principle of vaccination that underlies all modern immunology.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,153);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('tipu-sultan-killed','Tipu Sultan Falls at Seringapatam',1799,'South Asia','Tipu Sultan, the ''Tiger of Mysore'' and one of India''s most formidable opponents of British expansion, is killed defending his capital Seringapatam. His defeat ends the Kingdom of Mysore as a significant power and opens much of southern India to British control.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,154);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('napoleonic-wars','Napoleonic Wars Begin',1803,'Europe','Napoleon Bonaparte wages a series of military campaigns that bring most of Europe under French control and permanently reshape the continent''s political map. The wars spread revolutionary ideals across Europe, stimulate nationalism, and cause unprecedented destruction before Napoleon''s final defeat at Waterloo.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,155);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-trafalgar','Battle of Trafalgar',1805,'Europe','The British Royal Navy under Admiral Horatio Nelson defeats the combined French and Spanish fleets off Cape Trafalgar in southern Spain, securing British naval supremacy for over a century. Nelson is mortally wounded aboard his flagship HMS Victory at the moment of his greatest triumph, dying with the words ''Thank God I have done my duty'' and becoming one of Britain''s most celebrated national heroes. The battle ensures Napoleon can never invade Britain and establishes the maritime foundation for the British Empire''s global reach.','easy',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,156);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('abolition-slavery-britain','Britain Abolishes the Slave Trade',1807,'Europe','The British Parliament passes the Slave Trade Act, abolishing the transatlantic slave trade in the British Empire after decades of campaigning by abolitionists led by William Wilberforce. The law marks a turning point in the global fight against slavery, though slavery itself continues in British colonies for another generation.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,157);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('latin-american-independence','Latin American Independence Movements',1810,'Americas','Inspired by the American and French revolutions and weakened Spanish imperial control, independence movements erupt across Latin America. Led by figures like Simón Bolívar and José de San Martín, most of Spanish America achieves independence over the following two decades, fundamentally redrawing the political map.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,158);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('napoleon-defeat-waterloo','Battle of Waterloo',1815,'Europe','Napoleon Bonaparte is defeated decisively by the Duke of Wellington and Prussian forces at Waterloo in Belgium, ending his Hundred Days return to power. His final exile to Saint Helena ends the Napoleonic era and ushers in the Concert of Europe that shapes the continent for a generation.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,159);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('greek-independence','Greek War of Independence',1821,'Europe','Greek patriots launch a war of independence against Ottoman rule, drawing romanticist support from Europe and eventually winning international recognition for an independent Greek state. The struggle inspires nationalist movements across Europe and marks the beginning of the Ottoman Empire''s long decline.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,160);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('first-steam-railway','First Public Steam Railway Opens',1825,'Europe','George Stephenson''s Stockton and Darlington Railway opens in northern England, becoming the first public railway to use steam locomotives to carry passengers and freight on a regular commercial service. The success of the line launches the railway age, with networks expanding rapidly across Britain and then the world, transforming the cost and speed of overland transport beyond anything previously imaginable. Cheap, fast railways reshape economies, settlement patterns, and the conduct of warfare, accelerating the Industrial Revolution and binding global trade together.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,161);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('great-reform-act','Great Reform Act Passed in Britain',1832,'Europe','The Great Reform Act is passed by the British Parliament after fierce political struggle, abolishing the notorious ''rotten boroughs'' — constituencies with tiny electorates controlled by wealthy patrons — and extending the vote to a significant portion of the male middle class. Though far from establishing full democracy, the Act breaks the landed aristocracy''s monopoly on political representation and establishes the principle that Parliament should broadly reflect the population. It sets Britain on the gradual path toward universal suffrage, completed nearly a century later.','hard',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,162);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('queen-victoria-accession','Queen Victoria Ascends to the Throne',1837,'Europe','Eighteen-year-old Victoria becomes Queen of the United Kingdom following the death of her uncle William IV, beginning a reign of 63 years that makes her the longest-serving British monarch up to that point. The Victorian era sees Britain at the height of its imperial power, governing roughly a quarter of the world''s land and population, while at home rapid industrialization, social reform movements, scientific advances, and the gradual expansion of democratic rights transform British society. Victoria herself becomes a symbol of moral authority and imperial confidence across the English-speaking world.','easy',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,163);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('opium-wars-china','First Opium War',1839,'East Asia','Britain goes to war against China after the Chinese government attempts to stop the lucrative British opium trade, decisively defeating the Qing forces. The resulting Treaty of Nanking forces China to cede Hong Kong and open ports to trade, beginning a century of humiliation for China.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,164);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('chinese-opium-ban','Lin Zexu Destroys Opium in Canton',1839,'East Asia','Imperial Commissioner Lin Zexu seizes and destroys over 20,000 chests of opium from British merchants in Canton, in a dramatic demonstration of Chinese resistance to the drug trade. Britain responds by launching the First Opium War, setting in motion China''s century of humiliation.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,165);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('first-use-of-anesthesia','First Use of Surgical Anesthesia',1844,'North America','American dentist Horace Wells pioneers the use of nitrous oxide for tooth extraction without pain, and within two years William Morton''s public demonstration of ether anesthesia at Massachusetts General Hospital confirms and spreads the breakthrough worldwide. The ability to render patients unconscious during operations transforms surgery from an ordeal of conscious agony — endured as briefly as possible — into a methodical, precise discipline. Anesthesia is widely regarded as one of the greatest gifts of medicine, enabling procedures that save countless millions of lives.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,166);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('revolutions-of-1848','Revolutions Sweep Across Europe',1848,'Europe','A wave of liberal and nationalist revolutions erupts across Europe, toppling or threatening governments in France, the German states, the Austrian Empire, Italy, and beyond in the space of weeks. Driven by demands for constitutional government, national self-determination, and economic reform, the uprisings briefly overthrow many ancien régime governments before being crushed by conservative military force. The revolutions accelerate nationalist movements across Europe, hasten the decline of the old dynastic order, and are accompanied by Marx and Engels''s Communist Manifesto, published the same year.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,167);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('crimean-war','Crimean War',1853,'Europe','Russia goes to war with the Ottoman Empire over influence in the Holy Land and access to the Black Sea, drawing in Britain, France, and Sardinia on the Ottoman side in the first major European conflict since the Napoleonic Wars. The Crimean War becomes notable for the nursing reforms of Florence Nightingale, which lay the foundations of modern professional nursing, and for the catastrophic Charge of the Light Brigade, immortalized by Tennyson. The war ends Russian expansion toward the Mediterranean and marks the beginning of modern military logistics, journalism, and battlefield medicine.','medium',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,168);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('opium-war-second','Second Opium War',1856,'East Asia','Britain and France wage a second war against China, ultimately sacking Beijing and burning the Summer Palace, forcing China to sign the Convention of Peking granting further trading concessions. The conflict deepens China''s century of humiliation and further weakens the Qing dynasty.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,169);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('indian-rebellion-1857','First Indian War of Independence',1857,'South Asia','Indian soldiers in the British East India Company''s army mutiny at Meerut, sparking a widespread uprising across northern and central India against British rule. Though the rebellion is eventually suppressed, it leads to the dissolution of the East India Company and direct Crown rule over India.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,170);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('darwin-evolution','Darwin Publishes Theory of Evolution',1859,'Europe','Charles Darwin publishes On the Origin of Species, introducing the theory of evolution by natural selection and explaining the diversity of life on Earth through common ancestry. The theory revolutionizes biology and profoundly challenges religious accounts of creation, sparking debate that continues to this day.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,171);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('first-oil-well','First Commercial Oil Well Drilled',1859,'North America','Edwin Drake successfully drills the first commercial oil well near Titusville, Pennsylvania, striking oil at a depth of 21 meters and triggering an oil rush across the region. The discovery marks the beginning of the modern petroleum industry, enabling oil to be extracted, refined, and sold at scale for the first time. Cheap petroleum powers the second Industrial Revolution, fuels the age of automobiles and aviation, and makes oil the central commodity of the global economy and of geopolitics throughout the twentieth century.','medium',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,172);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('american-civil-war','American Civil War',1861,'Americas','The United States erupts into civil war when eleven Southern states secede over the issue of slavery and form the Confederate States of America. After four years of devastating conflict, the Union is preserved, slavery is abolished through the Thirteenth Amendment, and the nation''s social order is fundamentally transformed.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,173);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('emancipation-proclamation','Emancipation Proclamation Issued',1863,'North America','President Abraham Lincoln issues the Emancipation Proclamation, declaring all enslaved people in states in rebellion against the Union to be free. Though initially limited in immediate practical effect — applying only to areas not yet under Union control — the proclamation fundamentally transforms the Civil War from a conflict to preserve the Union into a war for human freedom, giving it a powerful moral dimension. It paves the way for the Thirteenth Amendment, which permanently abolished slavery throughout the United States two years later.','easy',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,174);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('abolition-slavery-us','Abolition of Slavery in the United States',1865,'Americas','The Thirteenth Amendment to the US Constitution is ratified, formally abolishing slavery throughout the United States at the end of the Civil War. The amendment liberates approximately four million enslaved people and begins the complex and often violent process of Reconstruction in the American South.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,175);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('lincoln-assassination','Assassination of Abraham Lincoln',1865,'North America','President Abraham Lincoln is shot by Confederate sympathizer John Wilkes Booth at Ford''s Theatre in Washington, D.C., dying the following morning just days after the Confederate surrender ends the Civil War. Lincoln''s death robs the nation of the leader best positioned to pursue a reconciliatory Reconstruction of the defeated South. The assassination leaves reunification in less capable hands, with consequences — particularly for the rights of newly freed Black Americans — that shape American society for generations.','easy',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,176);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('meiji-restoration-japan','Meiji Restoration in Japan',1868,'East Asia','Emperor Meiji is restored to power, ending the feudal Tokugawa shogunate and launching Japan''s rapid modernization. Japan adopts Western technology, institutions, and military organization at an extraordinary pace, transforming from a feudal society into a modern industrial and military power within a generation.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,177);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('suez-canal-opens','Suez Canal Opens',1869,'Africa','The Suez Canal, connecting the Mediterranean Sea to the Red Sea through Egypt, opens after ten years of construction, dramatically shortening sea routes between Europe and Asia. The canal becomes one of the world''s most strategically important waterways and a flashpoint of imperial rivalry.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,178);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('gandhi-born','Mahatma Gandhi Born',1869,'South Asia','Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi is born in Porbandar, Gujarat, into a merchant-caste family. He will grow up to lead India''s independence movement through nonviolent resistance, profoundly influencing civil rights leaders worldwide including Martin Luther King Jr. and Nelson Mandela.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,179);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('unification-germany','German Unification',1871,'Europe','Otto von Bismarck orchestrates the unification of the German states under Prussian leadership following victory in the Franco-Prussian War, creating the German Empire. The new power fundamentally alters the balance of power in Europe and sets in motion forces that will lead to two world wars.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,180);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('telephone-invented','Telephone Invented',1876,'Americas','Alexander Graham Bell makes the first successful voice telephone call, opening an era of instant long-distance communication. His invention rapidly transforms business, society, and personal relationships across the globe and lays the groundwork for all modern telecommunications.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,181);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('cricket-test-first','First Test Cricket Match',1877,'Oceania','The first official Test cricket match is played between Australia and England at the Melbourne Cricket Ground, with Australia winning by 45 runs. Test cricket, played over five days, becomes the pinnacle of the sport and a cultural institution across the British Commonwealth.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,182);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('zulu-war','Anglo-Zulu War',1879,'Africa','British forces invade the Zulu Kingdom and suffer a catastrophic defeat at Isandlwana, one of the worst British military disasters in colonial history, before eventually defeating the Zulus. The war ends the independent Zulu Kingdom and marks Britain''s determination to consolidate control of southern Africa.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,183);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('krakatoa-erupts','Krakatoa Erupts',1883,'Southeast Asia','The volcanic island of Krakatoa in the Dutch East Indies erupts in one of the most powerful volcanic events in recorded history, generating explosions heard nearly 5,000 kilometers away and sending a tsunami that kills over 36,000 people on the coasts of Java and Sumatra. The enormous quantities of ash and sulfur dioxide ejected into the upper atmosphere lower global temperatures for several years, producing vivid crimson sunsets that inspire artists worldwide, including possibly Edvard Munch''s The Scream. Krakatoa''s eruption is the first natural disaster to be reported globally in near-real time via the telegraph network.','medium',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,184);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('colonial-africa-berlin','Berlin Conference Divides Africa',1884,'Africa','European powers meet at the Berlin Conference to regulate the colonization of Africa, effectively dividing the continent among themselves with little regard for existing ethnic or political boundaries. The resulting borders, drawn by European diplomats, create lasting instability and conflict that reverberates across Africa today.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,185);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('indian-national-congress-founded','Indian National Congress Founded',1885,'South Asia','The Indian National Congress is established in Bombay as a platform for educated Indians to discuss political issues and present demands to the British government. It would evolve into the primary vehicle for the Indian independence movement under leaders like Gandhi and Nehru.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,186);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('partition-of-africa-colonial','Congo Free State Atrocities',1885,'Africa','King Leopold II of Belgium claims the Congo as his personal property and institutes a brutal forced labor system to harvest rubber and ivory, killing an estimated ten million Congolese. The atrocities, exposed by journalists and activists, spark one of history''s first international human rights campaigns.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,187);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('ramanujan-born','Srinivasa Ramanujan Born',1887,'South Asia','Srinivasa Ramanujan, one of history''s greatest mathematical geniuses, is born in Erode, Tamil Nadu. With almost no formal training, he would make extraordinary contributions to number theory, infinite series, and continued fractions, collaborating with G.H. Hardy at Cambridge.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,188);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('tesla-ac-electricity','Tesla Demonstrates Alternating Current',1888,'Americas','Nikola Tesla demonstrates the practical viability of alternating current electrical systems, which can transmit power over long distances far more efficiently than Edison''s direct current. Backed by George Westinghouse, AC eventually wins the War of Currents and becomes the global standard for electrical power.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,189);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('japan-meiji-constitution','Meiji Constitution Adopted in Japan',1889,'East Asia','Japan adopts its first modern constitution, establishing a constitutional monarchy with an elected parliament (Diet) while maintaining imperial sovereignty. The constitution formalizes Japan''s transformation into a modern state and lays the groundwork for its rise as a major world power.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,190);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('suffrage-new-zealand','New Zealand Grants Women the Vote',1893,'Oceania','New Zealand becomes the first self-governing country in the world to grant all women the right to vote, following a petition campaign led by Kate Sheppard. The achievement provides inspiration and a model for suffrage movements in other countries worldwide.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,191);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('marconi-invents-radio','Marconi Demonstrates Wireless Telegraphy',1895,'Europe','Italian inventor Guglielmo Marconi successfully demonstrates wireless telegraphy over increasing distances, building on the theoretical foundations of Maxwell and Hertz to create the first practical radio communication system. Within years he sends signals across the Atlantic Ocean, and the technology is rapidly adopted for maritime communication, military operations, and eventually mass broadcasting. Radio transforms how information is transmitted, making possible the broadcast media that define twentieth-century public life and culture.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,192);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('x-rays-discovered','X-Rays Discovered',1895,'Europe','German physicist Wilhelm Röntgen discovers X-rays while experimenting with cathode ray tubes, producing the first X-ray image — a photograph of his wife''s hand with her wedding ring clearly visible — and publishing his findings to astonished scientific and public audiences. The discovery spreads around the world within months and is immediately applied in hospitals for diagnosing fractures and internal conditions previously invisible to physicians. X-rays revolutionize medicine and open the field of radiation physics that leads to further discoveries including radioactivity, the atomic nucleus, and the foundations of quantum mechanics.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,193);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('modern-olympics-founded','Modern Olympic Games Founded',1896,'Europe','Pierre de Coubertin revives the Olympic Games in Athens with athletes from 14 nations competing in the first modern Olympiad. The Games grow from a small international competition into the world''s premier sporting event, watched by billions and imbued with ideals of international peace and friendship.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,194);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('curie-radioactivity','Marie Curie Discovers Radioactivity Properties',1898,'Europe','Marie Curie and her husband Pierre isolate the radioactive elements polonium and radium, pioneering the study of radioactivity and its medical applications. Marie Curie becomes the first woman to win a Nobel Prize and the only person to win it in two different sciences, transforming physics and medicine.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,195);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('south-african-boer-war','South African Boer War',1899,'Africa','Britain goes to war against the Boer republics of the Transvaal and Orange Free State in South Africa to secure control of the gold and diamond fields. The conflict introduces concentration camps to the modern lexicon and results in British annexation of the Boer republics, eventually leading to the Union of South Africa.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,196);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('australia-federation','Federation of Australia',1901,'Oceania','Six self-governing British colonies unite to form the Commonwealth of Australia, adopting a federal constitution that balances state and national powers. Australia''s federation creates one of the world''s first democracies with universal male suffrage and establishes a stable nation on a vast continent.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,197);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('wright-brothers-flight','Wright Brothers Achieve Powered Flight',1903,'Americas','Orville Wright pilots the Flyer for a 12-second flight at Kitty Hawk, North Carolina, achieving the world''s first powered, controlled airplane flight. The invention of the airplane revolutionizes transportation, warfare, and commerce in the twentieth century.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,198);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('suffragette-emmeline-pankhurst','Women''s Suffrage Movement Founded in Britain',1903,'Europe','Emmeline Pankhurst founds the Women''s Social and Political Union in Britain, pioneering militant tactics including hunger strikes, demonstrations, and property damage in the campaign for women''s right to vote. The movement''s pressure contributes to women over 30 gaining the vote in Britain fifteen years later.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,199);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('russo-japanese-war','Russo-Japanese War',1904,'East Asia','Japan launches a surprise attack on the Russian naval base at Port Arthur, beginning a war that shocks the world when Japan decisively defeats the Russian Empire on both land and sea. The Japanese victory at the Battle of Tsushima — the most decisive naval battle since Trafalgar — is the first major defeat of a European great power by an Asian nation in the modern era. The war accelerates the Russian domestic unrest that erupts in revolution during the war and signals Japan''s emergence as a major world power, reshaping the balance of power in Asia.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,200);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('partition-of-bengal','Partition of Bengal',1905,'South Asia','British Viceroy Lord Curzon partitions Bengal into Hindu-majority West Bengal and Muslim-majority East Bengal, ostensibly for administrative reasons. The move sparks massive protests and the Swadeshi movement, in which Indians boycott British goods, marking a new phase of nationalist resistance.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,201);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('swadeshi-movement','Swadeshi Movement Launched',1905,'South Asia','In response to the partition of Bengal, Indian nationalists launch the Swadeshi movement, calling for the boycott of British-made goods and the promotion of Indian-made products. The movement spreads nationalist sentiment widely and marks a turning point in the Indian independence struggle.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,202);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('einstein-relativity','Einstein Publishes Theory of Relativity',1905,'Europe','Albert Einstein publishes his Special Theory of Relativity along with three other groundbreaking papers, introducing the famous equation E=mc² and revolutionizing our understanding of space, time, mass, and energy. This miracle year produces discoveries that transform physics and underpin technologies from nuclear energy to GPS.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,203);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('fall-of-qing-dynasty','Fall of the Qing Dynasty',1911,'East Asia','The Xinhai Revolution sweeps away the Qing dynasty, ending over two thousand years of imperial rule in China and establishing the Republic of China. Led by reformists and nationalists inspired by Sun Yat-sen, the revolution abolishes the imperial examination system, the queue hairstyle enforced by the Manchu rulers, and the monarchy itself. The newly established republic is immediately beset by warlordism and political fragmentation, setting the stage for the decades of conflict between Nationalists and Communists that follow.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,204);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('tagore-nobel-prize','Rabindranath Tagore Wins Nobel Prize',1913,'South Asia','Rabindranath Tagore becomes the first non-European to win the Nobel Prize in Literature, awarded for his collection of poems Gitanjali. The honor brings global attention to Bengali literature and to Tagore''s philosophy blending spiritual and humanist themes.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,205);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('world-war-one','World War One Begins',1914,'Europe','The assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand triggers a catastrophic chain of alliances that engulfs Europe in the first truly global war. The conflict kills an estimated 17 million people, topples four empires, redraws the world map, and sets the stage for the even more destructive Second World War.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,206);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('panama-canal-opens','Panama Canal Opens',1914,'Americas','The Panama Canal opens, connecting the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans through the Isthmus of Panama after a decade of American construction following an earlier failed French attempt. The canal revolutionizes global maritime trade by eliminating the long voyage around South America.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,207);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('russian-revolution','Russian Revolution',1917,'Europe','Lenin''s Bolshevik party seizes power in Russia in October, overthrowing the Provisional Government and establishing the world''s first communist state. The revolution leads to a brutal civil war, the murder of the Tsar''s family, and the eventual formation of the Soviet Union.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,208);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('first-world-war-ends','World War One Armistice',1918,'Europe','At the eleventh hour of the eleventh day of the eleventh month, an armistice ends the fighting on the Western Front, concluding the First World War. The war''s end reshapes the world map through the collapse of four empires and sets conditions that lead directly to the Second World War.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,209);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('bolshevik-civil-war','Russian Civil War',1918,'Europe','Following the Bolshevik Revolution, Russia erupts in a devastating civil war between the Bolshevik Red Army and the anti-Bolshevik White forces supported by foreign interventions. The Bolshevik victory consolidates communist rule and leads to the formation of the Soviet Union a few years later.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,210);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('jallianwala-bagh-massacre','Jallianwala Bagh Massacre',1919,'South Asia','British Brigadier General Reginald Dyer orders troops to open fire on a peaceful crowd gathered at Jallianwala Bagh in Amritsar, killing hundreds of civilians. The massacre shocks the nation and world, radicalizing many Indians and galvanizing the independence movement.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,211);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('treaty-of-versailles','Treaty of Versailles Signed',1919,'Europe','The victorious Allied powers sign the Treaty of Versailles with Germany, imposing harsh reparations, territorial losses, and a war guilt clause that humiliates the German nation. The punitive terms generate widespread resentment in Germany and create conditions that facilitate the rise of Adolf Hitler.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,212);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('non-cooperation-movement','Non-Cooperation Movement',1920,'South Asia','Mahatma Gandhi launches the Non-Cooperation Movement, calling on Indians to withdraw from British institutions, return honors, and boycott British goods and courts. It marks the first mass nationalist campaign under Gandhi''s leadership and draws millions into the independence struggle.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,213);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('women-suffrage-us','Women Gain Right to Vote in the United States',1920,'Americas','The Nineteenth Amendment to the US Constitution is ratified, prohibiting the denial of the right to vote based on sex and granting women the right to vote nationwide. The achievement caps decades of suffragette activism and becomes a landmark moment in the global struggle for gender equality.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,214);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('ottoman-empire-falls','Ottoman Empire Falls',1922,'Middle East','The Ottoman Sultanate is formally abolished and Mustafa Kemal Atatürk establishes the Republic of Turkey from the empire''s Anatolian heartland. The fall of the Ottoman Empire reshapes the Middle East, creating new nations from former Ottoman territories and giving rise to conflicts that continue today.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,215);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('turkish-republic-founded','Turkish Republic Founded',1923,'Middle East','Mustafa Kemal Atatürk proclaims the Republic of Turkey from the ruins of the Ottoman Empire, becoming its first president and implementing one of the most sweeping modernization programs in history. Under Atatürk''s direction, Turkey adopts the Latin alphabet, separates religion from the state, grants women the right to vote, replaces Islamic law with European-inspired legal codes, and restructures education and dress along Western lines. The Turkish Republic represents one of the most rapid and radical transformations of a society in the twentieth century.','medium',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,216);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('television-invented','Television Invented',1926,'Europe','Scottish inventor John Logie Baird gives the first public demonstration of a working television system in London, transmitting moving images of human faces using a mechanical scanning system. Though Baird''s mechanical approach is soon superseded by all-electronic television developed by Philo Farnsworth and others, his demonstration proves the concept and launches the race to develop broadcasting. Television becomes the dominant mass medium of the twentieth century, reshaping politics, culture, advertising, and daily life across the world.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,217);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('chinese-civil-war','Chinese Civil War',1927,'East Asia','Conflict between Chiang Kai-shek''s Nationalist Party and Mao''s Communist Party erupts into civil war, interrupted by Japanese invasion before resuming after World War Two. The Communist victory drives the Nationalists to Taiwan and establishes the People''s Republic of China.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,218);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('penicillin-discovered','Penicillin Discovered',1928,'Europe','Scottish bacteriologist Alexander Fleming observes that the mold Penicillium notatum kills bacteria on his culture plate, discovering the first antibiotic. Penicillin''s subsequent development and mass production during World War II saves millions of lives and inaugurates the antibiotic era of medicine.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,219);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('great-depression','Great Depression Begins',1929,'Global','The New York Stock Exchange crashes in October, triggering a global economic depression that causes mass unemployment, widespread poverty, and banking failures across the world. The Great Depression reshapes economic thought, expands the role of government in economies, and creates conditions for the rise of fascism in Europe.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,220);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('gandhi-salt-march','Gandhi''s Salt March',1930,'South Asia','Mahatma Gandhi leads a 240-mile march to the sea at Dandi to make salt in defiance of the British salt tax, launching the Civil Disobedience Movement. The symbolic act captures worldwide attention and inspires mass civil disobedience across India.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,221);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('first-football-world-cup','First FIFA World Cup',1930,'Americas','Uruguay hosts and wins the inaugural FIFA World Cup, defeating Argentina in the final in Montevideo with thirteen nations participating. The tournament grows into the world''s most watched sporting event, with the final drawing television audiences exceeding one billion people.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,222);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('japanese-empire-manchuria','Japan Invades Manchuria',1931,'East Asia','Japan''s Kwantung Army seizes Manchuria in northeastern China following a staged incident, establishing the puppet state of Manchukuo. The invasion exposes the League of Nations'' inability to stop aggression and marks the beginning of Japan''s expansionist campaign across Asia.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,223);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('hitler-rise-chancellor','Hitler Appointed Chancellor of Germany',1933,'Europe','Adolf Hitler is appointed Chancellor of Germany by President Hindenburg, enabling the Nazi Party to rapidly consolidate power through emergency decrees and the elimination of political opposition. Within months, Hitler transforms Germany''s democratic republic into a totalitarian fascist state.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,224);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('long-march-china','The Long March',1934,'East Asia','The Chinese Communist Red Army embarks on a strategic retreat of over 6,000 miles through mountainous terrain to escape Nationalist forces, with Mao Zedong emerging as the dominant leader. The Long March becomes a foundational myth of the Chinese Communist Party and a symbol of revolutionary endurance.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,225);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('rise-of-nazism','Nazi Party Seizes Control of Germany',1934,'Europe','Following President Hindenburg''s death, Hitler merges the offices of Chancellor and President to become absolute ruler, or Fuhrer, of Germany, completing the Nazi seizure of power. The consolidation of totalitarian control enables the subsequent persecution of Jews, political opponents, and minorities.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,226);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('spanish-civil-war','Spanish Civil War',1936,'Europe','General Francisco Franco leads a military uprising against the elected Republican government of Spain, triggering a brutal three-year civil war that draws foreign intervention from Nazi Germany, Fascist Italy, and the Soviet Union. Franco''s victory establishes a fascist dictatorship and the conflict becomes a rehearsal for World War Two.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,227);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('world-war-two','World War Two Begins',1939,'Global','Nazi Germany invades Poland, prompting Britain and France to declare war and beginning the most destructive conflict in human history. The war ultimately involves most of the world''s nations, kills an estimated 70-85 million people, and transforms the global political order.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,228);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-britain','Battle of Britain',1940,'Europe','The Royal Air Force fights off a sustained German Luftwaffe campaign to achieve air superiority over Britain, in the first major campaign fought entirely by air forces. Britain''s victory prevents a German invasion and represents a turning point in World War Two, inspiring Churchill''s famous tribute to ''The Few.''','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,229);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('holocaust','Holocaust',1941,'Europe','Nazi Germany implements the systematic genocide of six million Jews and millions of others including Roma, disabled people, and political opponents across occupied Europe. The Holocaust becomes the defining atrocity of the modern era, leading to the Nuremberg trials, the Genocide Convention, and the founding of Israel.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,230);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('japanese-pearl-harbor','Attack on Pearl Harbor',1941,'East Asia','Japanese naval aircraft launch a surprise attack on the US naval base at Pearl Harbor, Hawaii, sinking or damaging much of the Pacific Fleet. The attack forces the United States to enter World War Two, dramatically altering the global conflict''s outcome.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,231);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('quit-india-movement','Quit India Movement',1942,'South Asia','Mahatma Gandhi launches the Quit India Movement, demanding an immediate end to British rule during World War II with his rallying cry of ''Do or Die.'' The British arrest Gandhi and thousands of Congress leaders, but the movement signifies the final mass push for independence.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,232);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('manhattan-project','Manhattan Project Develops Atomic Bomb',1942,'Americas','The United States launches the Manhattan Project, a massive secret scientific and engineering effort employing over 130,000 people to develop the world''s first nuclear weapons. Led by J. Robert Oppenheimer, the project produces the bombs dropped on Hiroshima and Nagasaki and fundamentally changes warfare and geopolitics.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,233);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('d-day-normandy','D-Day Normandy Landings',1944,'Europe','Allied forces launch the largest seaborne invasion in history on the beaches of Normandy, France, opening the long-awaited Western Front against Nazi Germany. The success of Operation Overlord turns the tide of war in Western Europe and ultimately leads to Germany''s defeat.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,234);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('atomic-bomb-hiroshima','Atomic Bomb Dropped on Hiroshima',1945,'East Asia','The United States drops an atomic bomb on Hiroshima, Japan, instantly killing tens of thousands and exposing hundreds of thousands more to deadly radiation. The use of the weapon — followed days later by a second bomb on Nagasaki — ends World War II and inaugurates the nuclear age.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,235);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('united-nations-founded','United Nations Founded',1945,'Global','Representatives from fifty nations sign the UN Charter in San Francisco, establishing the United Nations as the primary international organization for maintaining peace and cooperation. The UN creates a framework for international law, human rights, and collective security that shapes global governance to this day.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,236);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('end-world-war-two','World War Two Ends',1945,'Global','World War Two concludes with Germany''s unconditional surrender in May and Japan''s surrender in September following the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki. The war''s end reshapes the global order, establishing the United States and Soviet Union as superpowers and laying the groundwork for the Cold War.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,237);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('nuremberg-trials','Nuremberg Trials',1945,'Europe','Allied powers conduct the Nuremberg Trials, prosecuting Nazi leaders for war crimes, crimes against humanity, and crimes against peace, establishing that individuals can be held accountable under international law. The trials create the legal precedent for subsequent international criminal tribunals and the concept of universal human rights.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,238);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('japan-world-war-two-defeat','Japan''s Surrender Ends the Pacific War',1945,'East Asia','Emperor Hirohito announces Japan''s unconditional surrender following the atomic bombings and Soviet declaration of war, ending World War Two in the Pacific. The surrender ceremony aboard the USS Missouri in Tokyo Bay marks the beginning of the American occupation that transforms Japan into a democratic nation.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,239);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('indian-independence','Indian Independence',1947,'South Asia','India gains independence from British rule at midnight on August 15th, with Jawaharlal Nehru delivering his iconic ''Tryst with Destiny'' speech. The moment ends nearly two centuries of colonial rule and creates the world''s largest democracy.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,240);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('partition-india-pakistan','Partition of India and Pakistan',1947,'South Asia','The Indian subcontinent is partitioned into two independent nations — India and Pakistan — along religious lines, accompanied by one of the largest mass migrations in history. An estimated one to two million people die in sectarian violence and over ten million are displaced.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,241);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('cold-war-begins','Cold War Begins',1947,'Global','Increasing tensions between the United States and Soviet Union harden into the Cold War, with President Truman articulating the policy of containment to prevent Soviet expansion. The ideological and geopolitical rivalry between the two superpowers dominates world politics for the next four decades.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,242);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('apartheid-south-africa','Apartheid Established in South Africa',1948,'Africa','The Afrikaner National Party wins elections in South Africa and implements apartheid, a rigid system of racial segregation that strips Black South Africans of political rights and enforces severe discrimination in all aspects of life. The system provokes international condemnation and a powerful internal resistance movement.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,243);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('mahatma-gandhi-assassinated','Mahatma Gandhi Assassinated',1948,'South Asia','Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi, the leader of India''s independence movement and prophet of nonviolent resistance, is shot and killed by Hindu nationalist Nathuram Godse in New Delhi. His assassination shocks the world and threatens to destabilize the newly independent nation.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,244);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('palestine-israel-state','State of Israel Established',1948,'Middle East','David Ben-Gurion proclaims the establishment of the State of Israel in British Mandatory Palestine, immediately triggering a war with neighboring Arab states. The founding of Israel and the displacement of hundreds of thousands of Palestinians creates a conflict that remains unresolved and deeply consequential to this day.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,245);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('chinese-communist-revolution','Chinese Communist Revolution',1949,'East Asia','Mao Zedong proclaims the establishment of the People''s Republic of China after the Communist Party defeats Nationalist forces in the civil war. The revolution transforms the world''s most populous nation, creating a communist state that becomes a major power and reshapes global geopolitics.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,246);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('nato-founded','NATO Founded',1949,'Europe','The North Atlantic Treaty Organization is established by the United States, Canada, and ten Western European nations as a collective defense alliance against Soviet expansion. NATO''s mutual defense commitment shapes the Cold War''s military balance and remains the world''s most powerful military alliance.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,247);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('indian-constitution-adopted','Indian Constitution Adopted',1950,'South Asia','India adopts its constitution on January 26th, becoming a republic and the world''s largest democracy, with B.R. Ambedkar as its chief architect. The constitution enshrines fundamental rights, abolishes untouchability, and establishes a federal democratic framework.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,248);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('korean-war','Korean War',1950,'East Asia','North Korea invades South Korea, drawing in US-led UN forces and later Chinese troops in a conflict that kills millions and ends in a stalemate along the original border. The Korean War establishes the enduring division of the peninsula and becomes the first hot war of the Cold War era.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,249);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('dna-structure-discovered','DNA Double Helix Structure Discovered',1953,'Europe','James Watson and Francis Crick, using X-ray crystallography data from Rosalind Franklin and others, determine the double helix structure of DNA. The discovery reveals the molecular basis of heredity and sparks the genomic revolution in biology and medicine.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,250);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('death-of-stalin','Death of Joseph Stalin',1953,'Europe','Joseph Stalin, the Soviet dictator who transformed the USSR through forced collectivization, industrial crash programs, the Gulag labor camp system, and purges that killed millions, dies of a stroke after nearly three decades in power. His death triggers a power struggle within the Soviet leadership eventually won by Nikita Khrushchev, who denounces Stalin''s crimes in his ''Secret Speech'' three years later and initiates a cautious political ''thaw.'' Stalin''s death marks a significant shift in the Cold War, reducing the acute tensions of his final paranoid years and beginning a gradual, halting reassessment of Soviet policy.','easy',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,251);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('everest-first-ascent','First Ascent of Mount Everest',1953,'South Asia','New Zealander Edmund Hillary and Nepali Sherpa Tenzing Norgay become the first people confirmed to stand on the summit of Mount Everest, the world''s highest peak at 8,849 meters, on May 29. The achievement, announced to the world on the morning of Queen Elizabeth II''s coronation, is celebrated across the British Commonwealth as a triumph of human endurance and teamwork. The ascent transforms mountaineering from an elite pursuit into a global aspiration and makes Everest a symbol of the limits of human ambition.','easy',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,252);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('vietnam-partition','Vietnam Partitioned at the Seventeenth Parallel',1954,'Southeast Asia','Following the decisive French defeat at Dien Bien Phu, the Geneva Accords divide Vietnam at the seventeenth parallel into the communist North and the Western-backed South, pending elections that never occur. The partition plants the seeds of the Vietnam War.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,253);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('french-colonial-algeria','Algerian War of Independence',1954,'Africa','The Algerian National Liberation Front launches an armed insurgency against French colonial rule, beginning an eight-year war that costs an estimated 300,000-1.5 million Algerian lives. Algeria''s eventual independence becomes a landmark moment in the global anti-colonial struggle.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,254);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('suez-crisis','Suez Crisis',1956,'Middle East','Egypt''s President Nasser nationalizes the Suez Canal, provoking a military intervention by Britain, France, and Israel that is quickly reversed under US and Soviet pressure. The crisis marks a decisive end to British and French imperial power and signals the rise of Arab nationalism in the Middle East.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,255);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('sputnik-launch','Sputnik Launched',1957,'Europe','The Soviet Union launches Sputnik 1, the world''s first artificial satellite, into orbit around Earth, shocking the United States and inaugurating the Space Race. Sputnik''s beeping radio signal, audible to amateur radio operators worldwide, demonstrates Soviet technological capability and triggers massive investment in science and education.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,256);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('ghana-independence','Ghana Gains Independence',1957,'Africa','Ghana becomes the first sub-Saharan African country to gain independence from European colonial rule, with Kwame Nkrumah becoming its first Prime Minister. Ghana''s independence inspires independence movements across the continent and marks the beginning of the end of European colonialism in Africa.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,257);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('mao-great-leap-forward','Great Leap Forward in China',1958,'East Asia','Mao Zedong launches the Great Leap Forward, a disastrous campaign to rapidly transform China into a communist industrial state through forced collectivization and backyard steel production. The resulting famine kills between 15 and 55 million people, making it the deadliest famine in history.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,258);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('decolonization-africa','African Decolonization Wave',1960,'Africa','Seventeen African nations gain independence from European colonial powers in a single year, accelerating a broader wave of decolonization across the continent. The independence movements reshape the global political order, giving voice to newly sovereign nations in international forums like the United Nations.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,259);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('apartheid-sharpeville-massacre','Sharpeville Massacre',1960,'Africa','South African police open fire on a crowd of Black protesters demonstrating against the pass laws in Sharpeville, killing 69 people and wounding nearly 200. The massacre shocks the world, leads to international sanctions against South Africa, and transforms the anti-apartheid movement.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,260);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('contraceptive-pill-approved','Oral Contraceptive Pill Approved',1960,'North America','The US Food and Drug Administration approves Enovid, the first oral contraceptive pill, developed from the research of Carl Djerassi and others, for contraceptive use. The Pill gives women unprecedented control over their reproductive choices, separating sex from reproduction in a way that transforms gender roles, family planning, and sexual norms across the developed world. It is widely regarded as one of the most socially transformative innovations of the twentieth century, directly enabling the women''s liberation movement of the 1960s.','medium',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,261);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('space-race-yuri-gagarin','Yuri Gagarin Becomes First Human in Space',1961,'Europe','Soviet cosmonaut Yuri Gagarin completes one orbit of Earth aboard Vostok 1, becoming the first human to travel into space. His flight shocks the United States, accelerates the Space Race, and makes Gagarin an international hero.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,262);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('india-china-war','India-China Border War',1962,'South Asia','China launches a large-scale military offensive against India along their disputed Himalayan border, inflicting a humiliating defeat on Indian forces within a month before declaring a unilateral ceasefire. The conflict reshapes Indian defence policy and sours Sino-Indian relations for decades.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,263);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('cuban-missile-crisis','Cuban Missile Crisis',1962,'Americas','The United States discovers Soviet nuclear missiles in Cuba, leading to a tense thirteen-day standoff between President Kennedy and Premier Khrushchev that brings the world closer to nuclear war than at any other point. The crisis ends with Soviet withdrawal of missiles and becomes the defining moment of Cold War brinkmanship.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,264);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('south-korea-economic-miracle','South Korean Economic Miracle',1962,'East Asia','South Korea launches its first Five-Year Economic Development Plan under President Park Chung-hee, beginning a remarkable transformation from one of the world''s poorest countries into a major industrial power within a generation. The ''Miracle on the Han River'' becomes a model for rapid export-led development.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,265);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('martin-luther-king-speech','Martin Luther King''s March on Washington',1963,'Americas','Martin Luther King Jr. delivers his iconic ''I Have a Dream'' speech to 250,000 people at the Lincoln Memorial during the March on Washington for Jobs and Freedom. The speech becomes one of history''s most celebrated orations and galvanizes support for the Civil Rights Act.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,266);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('jfk-assassination','Assassination of President Kennedy',1963,'North America','President John F. Kennedy is shot and killed while riding in a motorcade through Dealey Plaza in Dallas, Texas, on November 22. The Warren Commission concludes that Lee Harvey Oswald acted alone, though the assassination generates enduring conspiracy theories that have never fully been resolved. Kennedy''s death shocks the world and marks the end of a period of post-war American optimism, transforming American political culture and leaving an indelible mark on the collective memory of a generation.','easy',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,267);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('civil-rights-act-us','US Civil Rights Act',1964,'Americas','President Lyndon B. Johnson signs the Civil Rights Act into law, prohibiting discrimination based on race, color, religion, sex, or national origin in the United States. The landmark legislation, championed by the civil rights movement led by Martin Luther King Jr., dismantles the legal infrastructure of racial segregation.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,268);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('green-revolution-india','Green Revolution in India',1965,'South Asia','India undertakes the Green Revolution, introducing high-yielding crop varieties, chemical fertilizers, and irrigation technology that dramatically increases agricultural output. Led by scientists like M.S. Swaminathan, the program transforms India from a food-deficient nation to one capable of feeding itself.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,269);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('vietnam-war','Vietnam War',1965,'Southeast Asia','The United States escalates military involvement in Vietnam to prevent a communist takeover of South Vietnam, committing ground troops in a conflict that lasts a decade. The war kills millions of Vietnamese and over 58,000 Americans, divides American society, and ends with the fall of Saigon and communist reunification of Vietnam.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,270);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('indo-pak-1965-war','India-Pakistan War over Kashmir',1965,'South Asia','Pakistan launches Operation Gibraltar to infiltrate Jammu and Kashmir, triggering a full-scale war with India that ends in a stalemate and the Tashkent Declaration mediated by the Soviet Union. The war deepens the Kashmir dispute without resolving it.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,271);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('us-civil-rights-march-selma','Selma to Montgomery Marches',1965,'Americas','Civil rights marchers attempting to walk from Selma to Montgomery, Alabama, are violently beaten by police on the Edmund Pettus Bridge on Bloody Sunday, shocking the nation. The marches contribute directly to the passage of the Voting Rights Act, a cornerstone of American civil rights legislation.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,272);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('chinese-cultural-revolution','Chinese Cultural Revolution',1966,'East Asia','Mao Zedong launches the Cultural Revolution to reassert ideological purity and his personal authority, unleashing Red Guards who attack intellectuals, destroy cultural heritage, and purge party officials. The decade-long upheaval causes immense suffering and economic disruption, killing hundreds of thousands and sending millions to labor camps.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,273);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('six-day-war','Six-Day War',1967,'Middle East','Israel launches preemptive air strikes against Egypt, Jordan, and Syria, destroying their air forces on the ground before seizing the Sinai Peninsula, Gaza Strip, West Bank, and Golan Heights in just six days of fighting. The swift and decisive Israeli victory reshapes the map of the Middle East, creating the territorial situation that defines the Israeli-Palestinian conflict to the present day. The war fundamentally alters the regional balance of power, deepens American and Soviet proxy rivalry in the Middle East, and makes the question of Palestinian statehood a central issue of international politics.','medium',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,274);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('moon-landing','Moon Landing',1969,'Americas','NASA astronauts Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin become the first humans to walk on the Moon during the Apollo 11 mission, with Armstrong''s words ''one small step for man'' broadcast to a global audience. The achievement represents the culmination of the Space Race and a triumph of human exploration.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,275);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('bangladesh-liberation-war','Bangladesh Liberation War',1971,'South Asia','East Pakistan, supported by India, fights for and wins independence from Pakistan following a brutal military crackdown by the Pakistani army. The conflict results in massive atrocities, a refugee crisis, and the birth of Bangladesh as a new nation.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,276);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('world-wide-web-invention','First Email Sent',1971,'Americas','Ray Tomlinson sends the first networked email between two computers on ARPANET, using the @ symbol to distinguish the user from the host machine. This invention creates one of the world''s most widely used forms of communication, transforming business, personal communication, and the flow of information.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,277);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('oil-crisis-1973','Oil Crisis of the Middle East',1973,'Middle East','Arab members of OPEC impose an oil embargo on countries supporting Israel in the Yom Kippur War, causing oil prices to quadruple and triggering a global economic crisis. The shock reveals Western economies'' vulnerability to Middle Eastern oil and permanently accelerates interest in energy conservation and alternatives.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,278);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('khmer-rouge-cambodia','Khmer Rouge Takes Power in Cambodia',1975,'Southeast Asia','The Khmer Rouge led by Pol Pot seizes power in Cambodia and launches a radical agrarian revolution, emptying cities and executing intellectuals, ethnic minorities, and perceived enemies. The resulting genocide kills an estimated 1.5 to 2 million people, roughly a quarter of Cambodia''s population.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,279);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('death-of-mao','Death of Mao Zedong',1976,'East Asia','Mao Zedong, the founder and supreme leader of the People''s Republic of China since its founding, dies after three decades of rule that included the Great Leap Forward, the Cultural Revolution, and China''s emergence as a nuclear power. His death triggers a brief power struggle ending in the arrest of the radical Gang of Four and the gradual rise of pragmatist Deng Xiaoping. Mao''s death is pivotal in world history, marking the beginning of China''s transformation from Maoist ideology toward the market-oriented reforms that make it the economic superpower of the twenty-first century.','easy',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,280);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('viking-1-mars','Viking 1 Lands on Mars',1976,'Global','NASA''s Viking 1 spacecraft successfully lands on the Chryse Planitia plain of Mars and transmits the first photographs taken from the surface of another planet, showing a rocky, reddish desert landscape under a salmon-colored sky. The lander conducts biological experiments designed to detect signs of microbial life in the Martian soil, producing ambiguous results that scientists continue to debate. Operating for over six years — far beyond its planned mission — Viking 1 represents humanity''s first sustained robotic presence on another world.','hard',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,281);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('tiananmen-one','Chinese Economic Reforms Begin',1978,'East Asia','Deng Xiaoping consolidates power and launches sweeping economic reforms opening China to foreign investment and market forces while maintaining Communist Party political control. The reforms launch China''s extraordinary economic transformation from a poor agricultural nation into the world''s second-largest economy.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,282);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('iran-islamic-revolution','Iranian Islamic Revolution',1979,'Middle East','Ayatollah Khomeini leads a popular revolution that overthrows the US-backed Shah of Iran and establishes an Islamic Republic. The revolution reshapes Middle Eastern politics, triggers the Iran-Iraq War, and fundamentally alters US-Iran relations with repercussions that extend into the present day.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,283);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('thatcher-becomes-pm','Margaret Thatcher Becomes Prime Minister',1979,'Europe','Margaret Thatcher becomes the United Kingdom''s first female Prime Minister following a decisive Conservative Party victory in the general election, beginning an eleven-year tenure that transforms British politics and economics. Thatcher dismantles much of Britain''s post-war consensus, privatizing state industries, curbing trade union power, and promoting free-market economic policies under the banner of Thatcherism. Her ideological alignment with Ronald Reagan''s parallel program in the United States defines the political economy of the English-speaking world in the 1980s and shifts the center of gravity of Western politics.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,284);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('smallpox-eradicated','Smallpox Eradicated Globally',1980,'Global','The World Health Organization officially declares smallpox eradicated, making it the first and to date only human infectious disease to be eliminated through a deliberate global vaccination campaign. The achievement represents one of public health''s greatest triumphs and saves millions of lives annually.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,285);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('iran-iraq-war','Iran-Iraq War Begins',1980,'Middle East','Iraq, led by Saddam Hussein, invades Iran in a dispute over the Shatt al-Arab waterway and in an attempt to exploit the instability created by Iran''s Islamic Revolution. The resulting war lasts eight years, kills between 500,000 and one million people, and ends in a stalemate with no significant territorial change for either side. The conflict devastates both economies, sees chemical weapons used on a large scale for the first time since World War One, and deepens the Sunni-Shia sectarian fault lines that define Middle Eastern geopolitics.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,286);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('aids-epidemic','AIDS Epidemic Identified',1981,'Americas','The US Centers for Disease Control identifies a mysterious immune deficiency syndrome among gay men, marking the official recognition of the AIDS epidemic. The disease goes on to kill over 35 million people worldwide and transforms global public health, sexuality politics, and medical research.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,287);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('falklands-war','Falklands War',1982,'South America','Argentina invades the British-controlled Falkland Islands in the South Atlantic, prompting Britain under Margaret Thatcher to dispatch a naval task force 13,000 kilometers to retake the remote archipelago. The brief but intense conflict ends in a decisive British military victory after ten weeks of fighting, costing over 900 lives on both sides. The war dramatically boosts Thatcher''s domestic political fortunes, contributes to the collapse of Argentina''s military junta, and reinforces the principle that territorial disputes should not be resolved by force.','medium',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,288);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('india-wins-cricket-world-cup','India Wins the Cricket World Cup',1983,'South Asia','Captained by Kapil Dev, India defeats the dominant West Indies in the Cricket World Cup final at Lord''s in one of the greatest sporting upsets ever. The victory sparks a revolution in Indian cricket and transforms the sport into the nation''s dominant cultural obsession.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,289);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('operation-blue-star','Operation Blue Star',1984,'South Asia','Indian military forces storm the Golden Temple in Amritsar to flush out Sikh militants led by Jarnail Singh Bhindranwale, causing heavy casualties among militants, soldiers, and civilians. The operation deeply wounds Sikh sentiments and has far-reaching political consequences.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,290);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('indira-gandhi-assassination','Assassination of Indira Gandhi',1984,'South Asia','Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi is assassinated by her own Sikh bodyguards in retaliation for Operation Blue Star. Her death triggers widespread anti-Sikh riots across India in which thousands of Sikhs are killed.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,291);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('bhopal-gas-tragedy','Bhopal Gas Tragedy',1984,'South Asia','A catastrophic leak of methyl isocyanate gas from a Union Carbide pesticide plant in Bhopal kills thousands of people immediately and leaves hundreds of thousands with lasting health effects. It remains the world''s worst industrial disaster and a landmark case in corporate accountability.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,292);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('ethiopian-famine','Ethiopian Famine',1984,'Africa','A catastrophic famine kills an estimated one million people in Ethiopia amid civil war and drought, shocking the world through television images and inspiring the Band Aid charity record and Live Aid concerts. The crisis raises awareness of African poverty and stimulates unprecedented international humanitarian aid.','easy',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,293);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('gorbachev-becomes-leader','Gorbachev Becomes Soviet Leader',1985,'Europe','Mikhail Gorbachev becomes General Secretary of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union following the death of Konstantin Chernenko, becoming at 54 the youngest Soviet leader since Stalin. His policies of glasnost (openness) and perestroika (restructuring) are intended to revitalize the stagnating Soviet system but instead unleash forces far beyond his control, leading to the fall of communist governments across Eastern Europe within a few years and ultimately the dissolution of the Soviet Union itself. Gorbachev''s accession is one of the pivotal moments of the Cold War.','medium',8,NULL,NULL,NULL,294);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('chernobyl-disaster','Chernobyl Nuclear Disaster',1986,'Europe','A reactor at the Chernobyl nuclear power plant in Soviet Ukraine explodes and catches fire, releasing radioactive contamination across much of Europe in the worst nuclear accident in history. The disaster kills dozens directly and exposes millions to radiation, accelerates the decline of the Soviet Union, and reshapes global attitudes toward nuclear power.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,295);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('sachin-tendulkar-debut','Sachin Tendulkar''s International Debut',1989,'South Asia','A sixteen-year-old Sachin Tendulkar makes his Test cricket debut against Pakistan, showing remarkable composure in facing fearsome bowling. He goes on to become the highest run-scorer in both Test and One Day International cricket and is widely regarded as the greatest batsman of his era.','easy',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,296);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('berlin-wall-falls','Berlin Wall Falls',1989,'Europe','The East German government opens its borders, leading jubilant crowds to tear down the Berlin Wall that has divided the city for nearly three decades. The event symbolizes the collapse of communism in Eastern Europe and leads directly to German reunification and the end of the Cold War.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,297);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('tiananmen-square','Tiananmen Square Protests',1989,'East Asia','Pro-democracy protesters gather in Tiananmen Square in Beijing for weeks before the Chinese government declares martial law and sends in the military, killing hundreds or possibly thousands in a violent crackdown. The image of a lone man standing before a column of tanks becomes one of the most iconic photographs of the modern era.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,298);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('mandela-freed','Nelson Mandela Released from Prison',1990,'Africa','Nelson Mandela is released from prison after twenty-seven years of incarceration for his anti-apartheid activism, greeted by massive global celebrations. His release marks the beginning of negotiations to end apartheid and ultimately leads to South Africa''s first fully democratic elections four years later.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,299);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('economic-liberalization-india','Economic Liberalization of India',1991,'South Asia','Facing a severe balance-of-payments crisis, Finance Minister Manmohan Singh introduces sweeping economic reforms that liberalize, privatize, and globalize the Indian economy. The reforms dismantle the ''License Raj'' and launch India onto a path of rapid economic growth.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,300);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('rajiv-gandhi-assassination','Assassination of Rajiv Gandhi',1991,'South Asia','Former Indian Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi is assassinated by a suicide bomber linked to the Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam during an election campaign rally in Tamil Nadu. His killing is motivated by India''s military intervention in Sri Lanka''s civil war.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,301);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('dissolution-soviet-union','Dissolution of the Soviet Union',1991,'Europe','The Soviet Union formally dissolves into fifteen independent republics on December 25th, with Mikhail Gorbachev resigning as president. The collapse ends the Cold War and fundamentally reshapes the global political order, leaving the United States as the world''s sole superpower.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,302);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('internet-invented','World Wide Web Invented',1991,'Europe','Tim Berners-Lee at CERN makes the World Wide Web publicly available, creating the system of linked hypertext documents that makes the internet accessible to ordinary users. The web transforms commerce, communication, entertainment, and virtually every aspect of modern civilization.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,303);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('babri-masjid-demolition','Demolition of the Babri Masjid',1992,'South Asia','A crowd of Hindu activists demolishes the Babri Masjid mosque in Ayodhya, claiming the site as the birthplace of Lord Ram. The event triggers widespread Hindu-Muslim riots across India, killing thousands, and sets off a decades-long legal battle culminating in a Supreme Court verdict.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,304);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('rwandan-genocide','Rwandan Genocide',1994,'Africa','Hutu extremists in Rwanda systematically murder an estimated 500,000 to 800,000 Tutsi and moderate Hutu in approximately 100 days, one of history''s fastest genocides. The international community''s failure to intervene becomes a defining moral failure and leads to reforms in international humanitarian law.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,305);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('independence-south-africa','Nelson Mandela Becomes South Africa''s President',1994,'Africa','Nelson Mandela is elected the first Black President of South Africa in the country''s first fully democratic election, marking the official end of the apartheid system. His presidency symbolizes reconciliation and moral leadership, inspiring people around the world in the struggle against racial injustice.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,306);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('collapse-apartheid-negotiations','South Africa''s First Democratic Election',1994,'Africa','South Africa holds its first fully democratic election in which all races can vote, resulting in a historic victory for Nelson Mandela and the African National Congress. The peaceful transition from apartheid to democracy becomes a model for conflict resolution and national reconciliation.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,307);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('amazon-founded','Amazon Founded',1994,'Americas','Jeff Bezos founds Amazon as an online bookstore from his garage in Seattle, launching what will become the world''s largest online retailer and cloud computing provider. Amazon transforms global retail, logistics, and cloud computing while making Bezos one of the wealthiest individuals in history.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,308);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('wto-founded','World Trade Organization Founded',1995,'Global','The World Trade Organization comes into being on January 1, replacing the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade with a permanent institution equipped with binding dispute settlement mechanisms and a mandate to negotiate further trade liberalization. With 123 founding members, the WTO creates the legal framework governing the majority of world trade and becomes the central institution of economic globalization. Its establishment marks the high point of the post-Cold War liberal international order, though it subsequently becomes a focal point of protests against inequality and a target of nationalist backlash.','hard',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,309);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('dolly-sheep-cloned','Dolly the Sheep Cloned',1996,'Europe','Scientists at the Roslin Institute in Edinburgh successfully clone Dolly the sheep from a single adult mammary cell, making her the first mammal ever cloned from an adult somatic cell rather than an embryo. The achievement overturns decades of biological assumptions about cell differentiation and demonstrates that the DNA of a fully specialized adult cell retains the information needed to produce a complete organism. Dolly''s creation ignites intense ethical debate about human cloning and accelerates research into stem cells, regenerative medicine, and the fundamental mechanisms of genetics.','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,310);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('taliban-capture-kabul','Taliban Capture Kabul',1996,'South Asia','The Taliban, a fundamentalist Islamist movement that emerged from the Afghan refugee camps of Pakistan, captures the Afghan capital Kabul, executing the former communist president Najibullah and imposing a strict interpretation of Islamic law across the territory they control. Under Taliban rule, women are barred from education and employment, and cultural sites are destroyed, drawing international condemnation. The Taliban government harbors al-Qaeda, setting the conditions for the September 11 attacks and the US-led invasion of Afghanistan five years later.','medium',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,311);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('hong-kong-handover','Hong Kong Handed Back to China',1997,'East Asia','The United Kingdom transfers sovereignty over Hong Kong to the People''s Republic of China on July 1, ending 156 years of British colonial rule over the territory. Under the principle of ''one country, two systems'' negotiated by Deng Xiaoping and Margaret Thatcher, Hong Kong is to retain its capitalist economy, independent judiciary, and civil liberties for fifty years. The handover marks the symbolic end of the British Empire''s presence in Asia and is a defining moment in China''s national narrative of recovering territories lost during what it calls the ''century of humiliation.''','medium',7,NULL,NULL,NULL,312);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('pokhran-nuclear-tests','Pokhran Nuclear Tests',1998,'South Asia','India conducts a series of nuclear tests in the Pokhran desert in Rajasthan, declaring itself a nuclear weapon state. The tests, code-named Operation Shakti, trigger international sanctions but mark India''s entry into the exclusive club of declared nuclear powers.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,313);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('google-founded','Google Founded',1998,'Americas','Larry Page and Sergey Brin found Google, launching a search engine that organizes the world''s information through its revolutionary PageRank algorithm. Google grows into one of the most powerful technology companies in history, transforming advertising, information access, and the digital economy.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,314);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('space-station-iss','International Space Station Construction Begins',1998,'Global','The first module of the International Space Station is launched, beginning the construction of the largest human-made structure ever placed in orbit. A symbol of post-Cold War cooperation, the ISS involves the US, Russia, Europe, Japan, and Canada in continuous human presence in space.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,315);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('kargil-war','Kargil War',1999,'South Asia','Pakistani soldiers and militants infiltrate the Kargil sector of Jammu and Kashmir, leading to intense high-altitude combat between Indian and Pakistani forces. India successfully recaptures most positions in Operation Vijay, and the conflict remains the only direct war between two nuclear-armed states.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,316);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('gujarat-earthquake','Gujarat Earthquake',2001,'South Asia','A powerful earthquake measuring 7.7 magnitude strikes the Bhuj region of Gujarat on Republic Day, killing around 20,000 people and injuring 167,000. It is one of the deadliest earthquakes in India''s recorded history and causes widespread destruction across the Kutch region.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,317);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('september-11-attacks','September Eleventh Attacks',2001,'Americas','Al-Qaeda terrorists hijack four commercial aircraft, flying two into the World Trade Center in New York, one into the Pentagon, and one crashes in Pennsylvania, killing nearly 3,000 people. The attacks trigger the US War on Terror, reshape global security policy, and fundamentally alter geopolitics.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,318);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('brahmos-missile-india','BrahMos Missile Developed',2001,'South Asia','India and Russia jointly develop and deploy the BrahMos, the world''s fastest supersonic cruise missile, representing a landmark in India''s defense technology capabilities. The missile, named after the Brahmaputra and Moskva rivers, becomes a cornerstone of Indian military modernization.','hard',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,319);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('human-genome-project','Human Genome Project Completed',2003,'Global','An international consortium completes the mapping of the entire human genome, identifying the approximately 20,000-25,000 genes that make up human DNA. The achievement revolutionizes medicine, enabling new approaches to disease diagnosis, treatment, and prevention based on genetic information.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,320);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('space-shuttle-columbia','Space Shuttle Columbia Disaster',2003,'Americas','The Space Shuttle Columbia disintegrates upon reentry into Earth''s atmosphere, killing all seven crew members including India-born astronaut Kalpana Chawla. The accident grounds the shuttle fleet and leads to a comprehensive review of NASA''s safety culture and the eventual retirement of the shuttle program.','easy',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,321);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('indian-ocean-tsunami-india','Indian Ocean Tsunami Strikes India',2004,'South Asia','A massive undersea earthquake off Sumatra triggers a devastating tsunami that strikes Indian coastal regions, killing over 10,000 people in Tamil Nadu, Andhra Pradesh, Kerala, and the Andaman Islands. The disaster prompts major improvements in early warning systems across the Indian Ocean.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,322);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('iphone-launched','iPhone Launched',2007,'Americas','Apple''s Steve Jobs unveils the iPhone, a revolutionary device combining a phone, music player, and internet communicator in a touchscreen package. The smartphone fundamentally transforms communication, commerce, entertainment, and social interaction, spawning a new era of mobile computing.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,323);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('chandrayaan-1-launched','Chandrayaan-1 Launched',2008,'South Asia','India launches Chandrayaan-1, its first lunar probe, marking a major milestone in the nation''s space program. The mission discovers evidence of water molecules on the lunar surface, a significant scientific finding that reshapes understanding of the Moon.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,324);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('mumbai-terrorist-attacks','Mumbai Terrorist Attacks',2008,'South Asia','Pakistani Lashkar-e-Taiba militants carry out a series of coordinated terrorist attacks across Mumbai, targeting the Taj Mahal Palace Hotel, Chhatrapati Shivaji Terminus, and other locations. The three-day siege kills over 160 people and severely strains India-Pakistan relations.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,325);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('global-financial-crisis','Global Financial Crisis',2008,'Global','The collapse of investment bank Lehman Brothers triggers a global financial crisis that causes the worst economic recession since the Great Depression, wiping out trillions in wealth and causing widespread unemployment worldwide. The crisis reshapes global regulation, exposes deep systemic risks in financial markets, and fuels political populism.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,326);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('arab-spring','Arab Spring',2011,'Middle East','A wave of pro-democracy protests and uprisings sweeps across the Arab world, beginning in Tunisia and spreading to Egypt, Libya, Syria, Bahrain, and Yemen. While some countries experience democratic transitions, others descend into civil war, and the movement''s legacy remains deeply contested.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,327);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('osama-bin-laden-killed','Osama bin Laden Killed',2011,'South Asia','US Navy SEALs kill Osama bin Laden in a raid on his compound in Abbottabad, Pakistan, a decade after the September 11 attacks. His death is a symbolic milestone in the US War on Terror though it does not end global jihadist terrorism.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,328);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('nirbhaya-case-protests','Nirbhaya Rape Case and Protests',2012,'South Asia','The brutal gang rape and murder of a young woman on a Delhi bus sparks massive nationwide protests against sexual violence and demands for stronger laws protecting women. The case leads to significant reforms in Indian rape law and raises global awareness about gender-based violence in India.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,329);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('mangalyaan-mars-mission','Mangalyaan Mars Mission',2013,'South Asia','India launches the Mars Orbiter Mission, making it the first Asian nation to reach Mars and the first in the world to do so on its maiden attempt. The mission is completed at a remarkably low cost, demonstrating ISRO''s capability for frugal and efficient space exploration.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,330);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('modi-elected-pm','Narendra Modi Elected as Prime Minister',2014,'South Asia','Narendra Modi of the Bharatiya Janata Party wins a sweeping parliamentary majority, becoming Prime Minister of India with the largest mandate in thirty years. His election is seen as a major shift in Indian politics toward Hindu nationalist governance and pro-business economic reforms.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,331);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('islamic-state-rise','Islamic State Declares Caliphate',2014,'Middle East','The Islamic State (ISIS) declares a caliphate spanning territory across Iraq and Syria, controlling millions of people and shocking the world with its extreme violence and sophisticated propaganda. The group''s rise triggers an international military coalition and a refugee crisis affecting millions.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,332);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('malala-nobel-peace-prize','Malala Yousafzai Wins Nobel Peace Prize',2014,'South Asia','Pakistani activist Malala Yousafzai, who survived a Taliban assassination attempt for her advocacy of girls'' education, becomes the youngest person ever to receive the Nobel Peace Prize. Her story inspires global attention to gender disparities in education in conflict zones.','easy',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,333);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('paris-climate-agreement','Paris Climate Agreement Signed',2015,'Global','Nearly every nation signs the Paris Agreement committing to limit global warming to well below 2°C above pre-industrial levels and pursue efforts to limit warming to 1.5°C. The landmark accord represents the first universal commitment to addressing climate change but faces implementation challenges.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,334);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('demonetization-india','Demonetization in India',2016,'South Asia','Prime Minister Narendra Modi announces the sudden withdrawal of all 500 and 1000 rupee banknotes, declaring them invalid overnight in a move aimed at curbing black money and corruption. The decision causes widespread disruption and long queues at banks while remaining highly controversial in its economic impact.','easy',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,335);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('gst-implemented-india','GST Implemented in India',2017,'South Asia','India replaces a complex web of central and state taxes with a unified Goods and Services Tax, the most ambitious tax reform since independence. The GST aims to create a single national market and reduce tax evasion, though its implementation causes initial disruption for businesses.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,336);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('chandrayaan-2-launched','Chandrayaan-2 Launched',2019,'South Asia','India launches Chandrayaan-2 with an orbiter, lander, and rover aimed at the lunar south pole. Though the Vikram lander crashes during descent, the orbiter continues to function and provides valuable data, keeping alive India''s ambitions for a soft lunar landing.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,337);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('caa-protests-india','Citizenship Amendment Act Protests',2019,'South Asia','India passes the Citizenship Amendment Act granting citizenship to non-Muslim refugees from three neighboring countries, sparking widespread protests over fears of religious discrimination. The demonstrations, including the prolonged Shaheen Bagh sit-in led by Muslim women, become the largest civil protest movement in years.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,338);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('black-holes-confirmed','First Black Hole Image Captured',2019,'Global','The Event Horizon Telescope Collaboration releases the first direct image of a black hole''s event horizon in galaxy M87, providing visual confirmation of one of physics'' most extraordinary theoretical predictions. The image, produced by linking radio telescopes across the globe, marks a triumph of international scientific cooperation.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,339);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('covid-lockdown-india','COVID Lockdown in India',2020,'South Asia','Prime Minister Modi announces a sudden nationwide lockdown within hours notice to contain the COVID-19 pandemic, triggering a massive humanitarian crisis as millions of migrant workers attempt to walk home to their villages. India endures one of the world''s strictest lockdowns while managing the economic and public health fallout.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,340);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('covid-19-pandemic','COVID-19 Global Pandemic',2020,'Global','A novel coronavirus identified in Wuhan, China spreads globally to become a devastating pandemic that kills millions, halts economies, and transforms daily life worldwide. The crisis accelerates vaccine development using mRNA technology and triggers profound debates about public health, inequality, and global preparedness.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,341);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('chandrayaan-3-lunar-landing','Chandrayaan-3 Lunar Landing',2023,'South Asia','India''s Chandrayaan-3 successfully lands near the lunar south pole, making India the fourth country to achieve a soft lunar landing and the first to land near the south pole. The mission discovers evidence of sulfur and other elements in the lunar soil, generating major scientific interest.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,342);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('david-captures-jerusalem','King David Captures Jerusalem',-1000,'Middle East','According to biblical tradition, King David captures the Jebusite city of Jerusalem and makes it the capital of a united Israelite kingdom. Jerusalem becomes the political and religious centre of the Israelites, a status that later shapes its importance for Judaism, Christianity and Islam.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('ptolemaic-dynasty-founded','Ptolemy I Becomes Pharaoh of Egypt',-305,'Africa','Ptolemy, one of Alexander the Great''s generals, declares himself king of Egypt and founds the Ptolemaic dynasty. His Greek-speaking dynasty rules Egypt from Alexandria for nearly three centuries, ending with Cleopatra VII.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-zama','Battle of Zama',-202,'Africa','The Roman general Scipio Africanus defeats Hannibal near Zama in North Africa, ending the Second Punic War. Carthage gives up its fleet and overseas territories, leaving Rome the dominant power in the western Mediterranean.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('caesar-invades-britain','Julius Caesar Invades Britain',-55,'Europe','Julius Caesar leads the first Roman military expedition across the English Channel to Britain, returning with a larger force the following year. He does not conquer the island, but his campaigns draw Britain into the Roman world; full conquest comes under Claudius nearly a century later.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('second-triumvirate','Second Triumvirate Formed',-43,'Europe','Mark Antony, Octavian and Marcus Aemilius Lepidus form the Second Triumvirate, a legally sanctioned dictatorship of three men, after Julius Caesar''s assassination. They purge their opponents, including Cicero, and defeat Caesar''s assassins, but the rivalry between Antony and Octavian later ends the Republic.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('jin-reunifies-china','Jin Dynasty Reunifies China',280,'East Asia','The Western Jin dynasty conquers the state of Wu, ending the Three Kingdoms period and reuniting China under Emperor Wu (Sima Yan). The unity is short-lived: within decades civil war and invasions split northern and southern China again.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('huns-arrive-in-europe','Huns Arrive in Europe',375,'Europe','The Huns, nomadic horsemen from the steppes, overwhelm the Ostrogoths and drive the Visigoths across the Danube into the Roman Empire. The upheaval sets off the great migrations that help bring down the Western Roman Empire.','hard',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('chandragupta-ii-vikramaditya','Chandragupta II Vikramaditya Takes the Throne',375,'South Asia','Chandragupta II, remembered by the title Vikramaditya, becomes emperor of the Gupta Empire. His reign extends Gupta power across northern and western India and is associated with a flowering of Sanskrit literature, art and science.','hard',4,'approximate range',1,'c. 375-380',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('benedictine-order-founded','Founding of the Benedictine Order',529,'Europe','Benedict of Nursia establishes the monastery of Monte Cassino in Italy, where he writes the Rule that becomes the model for Western monastic life. Benedictine monasteries go on to preserve learning and shape religious life across medieval Europe.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('death-of-muhammad','Death of the Prophet Muhammad',632,'Middle East','The Prophet Muhammad dies in Medina, having united much of the Arabian Peninsula under Islam. The dispute over his succession, beginning with the choice of Abu Bakr as the first caliph, later shapes the division between Sunni and Shia Muslims.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('mihira-bhoja-kannauj','Mihira Bhoja Becomes King of Kannauj',836,'South Asia','Mihira Bhoja ascends the throne of the Gurjara-Pratihara dynasty, ruling from Kannauj. Over a long reign he makes the Pratiharas one of the leading powers of northern India and a barrier against Arab expansion from Sindh.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('mahmud-of-ghazni-accession','Mahmud of Ghazni Takes Power',998,'South Asia','Mahmud becomes ruler of the Ghaznavid state in present-day Afghanistan and builds an empire stretching from eastern Iran to the Punjab. His repeated raids into northern India bring enormous wealth to his capital at Ghazni.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('tower-of-london-begun','Construction of the Tower of London Begins',1078,'Europe','William the Conqueror begins building the White Tower in London, a stone keep meant to dominate the city after the Norman Conquest. It grows into the Tower of London, serving over the centuries as royal palace, prison, armoury and home of the Crown Jewels.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('university-of-paris-founded','Philip II Grants the University of Paris a Royal Charter',1200,'Europe','King Philip II (Philip Augustus) grants a royal charter to the masters and students of Paris, placing them under royal protection. Their guild had grown up over several decades around the cathedral school of Notre-Dame, and the University of Paris becomes the leading centre of theology and philosophy in medieval Europe.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('qutb-ud-din-aibak-delhi','Qutb ud-Din Aibak Founds the Delhi Sultanate',1206,'South Asia','After the death of Muhammad of Ghor, his former slave general Qutb ud-Din Aibak takes power in northern India and becomes the first sultan of Delhi. His Mamluk, or Slave, dynasty begins more than three centuries of sultanate rule.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('razia-sultana-accession','Razia Sultana Takes the Throne of Delhi',1236,'South Asia','Razia, daughter of Sultan Iltutmish, becomes ruler of the Delhi Sultanate, the only woman ever to hold its throne. She governs actively and appears in public in male dress, but opposition from the Turkic nobility leads to her overthrow and death within four years.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('alauddin-khalji-accession','Alauddin Khalji Becomes Sultan of Delhi',1296,'South Asia','Alauddin Khalji seizes the throne of Delhi after having his uncle, Sultan Jalaluddin, killed. He repels repeated Mongol invasions, introduces strict price controls and land-revenue reforms, and extends the sultanate''s power deep into southern India.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('muhammad-bin-tughlaq-accession','Muhammad bin Tughlaq Becomes Sultan',1325,'South Asia','Muhammad bin Tughlaq becomes sultan of Delhi. A learned but erratic ruler, he is remembered for ambitious schemes that failed, including moving the capital to Daulatabad in the Deccan and issuing a token copper currency.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('firuz-shah-tughlaq-accession','Firuz Shah Tughlaq Becomes Sultan',1351,'South Asia','Firuz Shah Tughlaq succeeds his cousin Muhammad bin Tughlaq as sultan of Delhi. His long reign is remembered for public works such as canals, new towns and the Feroz Shah Kotla citadel, even as the sultanate''s power declines.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('babur-ruler-of-ferghana','Babur Becomes Ruler of Ferghana',1494,'South Asia','Babur, a Timurid prince descended from both Timur and Genghis Khan, inherits the small kingdom of Ferghana in Central Asia at about the age of eleven. Repeatedly driven from his homeland, he eventually turns south and founds the Mughal Empire in India.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('first-portable-watches','Peter Henlein Makes the First Portable Watch',1508,'Europe','The Nuremberg locksmith Peter Henlein, traditionally credited as the inventor, builds small timepieces driven by a coiled steel mainspring instead of heavy falling weights. These ''Nuremberg eggs'' are worn as pendants or carried in pouches, since pockets are not yet common, and begin the shift towards personal timekeeping.','medium',3,'approximate range',1,'c. 1505–1510',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('humayun-succeeds-babur','Humayun Succeeds Babur',1530,'South Asia','Babur, founder of the Mughal Empire, dies in Agra and is succeeded by his son Humayun. Humayun inherits a young, unsettled empire and soon faces challenges from his own brothers and from the Afghan leader Sher Shah Suri.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('humayun-recaptures-delhi','Humayun Recaptures Delhi',1555,'South Asia','After fifteen years in exile, Humayun returns with Persian help, defeats the Suri dynasty and retakes Delhi, restoring Mughal rule. He dies months later after a fall on the steps of his library, leaving the throne to his young son Akbar.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('death-of-akbar','Death of Akbar',1605,'South Asia','Akbar the Great dies at Agra after nearly fifty years on the throne, having built the Mughal Empire into the dominant power of the subcontinent. His son Salim succeeds him as the emperor Jahangir.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('martyrdom-of-guru-arjan','Execution of Guru Arjan',1606,'South Asia','Guru Arjan, the fifth Sikh Guru and compiler of the Adi Granth, is arrested on the orders of the Mughal emperor Jahangir and dies in custody after refusing to convert to Islam. Remembered as the first Sikh martyr, his death leads his successor to militarise the Sikh community.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('jahangir-marries-nur-jahan','Jahangir Marries Nur Jahan',1611,'South Asia','The Mughal emperor Jahangir marries Mehr-un-Nissa, who receives the title Nur Jahan, ''Light of the World''. She becomes the most powerful woman in Mughal history, issuing coins and orders in her own name as real power passes to her in Jahangir''s later years.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('death-of-jahangir','Death of Jahangir',1627,'South Asia','The Mughal emperor Jahangir dies while travelling back from Kashmir. After a brief succession struggle his son Khurram takes the throne as Shah Jahan, the emperor who will build the Taj Mahal.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('birth-of-shivaji','Birth of Shivaji',1630,'South Asia','Shivaji Bhonsle is born at the hill fort of Shivneri near Pune. He grows up to challenge the Mughal Empire and the Deccan sultanates, and is later crowned Chhatrapati of a new Maratha kingdom.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('execution-of-guru-tegh-bahadur','Execution of Guru Tegh Bahadur',1675,'South Asia','Guru Tegh Bahadur, the ninth Sikh Guru, is publicly executed in Delhi on the orders of the Mughal emperor Aurangzeb after refusing to convert to Islam. Sikhs remember him for defending freedom of religion, including that of Kashmiri Hindus.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-blenheim','Battle of Blenheim',1704,'Europe','An Anglo-Austrian army under the Duke of Marlborough and Prince Eugene of Savoy crushes a Franco-Bavarian force at Blenheim in Bavaria. The victory saves Vienna, knocks Bavaria out of the War of the Spanish Succession and ends the image of French invincibility.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('death-of-guru-gobind-singh','Death of Guru Gobind Singh',1708,'South Asia','Guru Gobind Singh, the tenth Sikh Guru and founder of the Khalsa, dies at Nanded in the Deccan after being attacked. Before his death he declares that the line of human Gurus ends and that the scripture, the Guru Granth Sahib, will be the Sikhs'' eternal Guru.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('nadir-shah-sacks-delhi','Nadir Shah Sacks Delhi',1739,'South Asia','Nadir Shah of Persia defeats the Mughal army at Karnal and sacks Delhi, massacring thousands of its inhabitants. He carries off enormous treasure, including the Peacock Throne and the Koh-i-Noor diamond, exposing the weakness of the declining Mughal Empire.','hard',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-buxar','Battle of Buxar',1764,'South Asia','East India Company troops under Hector Munro defeat the combined forces of the Nawab of Bengal, the Nawab of Awadh and the Mughal emperor Shah Alam II. The victory leads to the Treaty of Allahabad, which gives the Company the right to collect revenue in Bengal, Bihar and Orissa.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('second-anglo-mysore-war','Second Anglo-Mysore War Begins',1780,'South Asia','Hyder Ali of Mysore invades the Carnatic and inflicts a heavy defeat on East India Company forces at Pollilur. The war continues under his son Tipu Sultan after Hyder''s death and ends with the Treaty of Mangalore, which restores the pre-war borders.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('lewis-and-clark-expedition','Lewis and Clark Expedition',1804,'Americas','Meriwether Lewis and William Clark lead the Corps of Discovery up the Missouri River and across the Rocky Mountains to the Pacific coast, guided in part by the Shoshone woman Sacagawea. The expedition maps newly acquired western lands and strengthens American claims to the Pacific Northwest.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('death-of-napoleon','Death of Napoleon',1821,'Europe','Napoleon Bonaparte dies in exile on the remote South Atlantic island of Saint Helena, where the British have held him since Waterloo. His legend, and the legal reforms of the Napoleonic Code, long outlive him.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('indian-removal-act','Indian Removal Act',1830,'Americas','President Andrew Jackson signs the Indian Removal Act, authorising the forced relocation of Native American nations from the southeastern United States to lands west of the Mississippi. The removals that follow, including the Cherokee ''Trail of Tears'', cost thousands of lives.','hard',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('alaska-purchase','United States Buys Alaska',1867,'Americas','The United States buys Alaska from the Russian Empire for 7.2 million dollars, in a deal negotiated by Secretary of State William Seward. Mocked at the time as ''Seward''s Folly'', the purchase ends Russia''s presence in North America and later proves rich in gold and oil.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('stanley-finds-livingstone','Stanley Finds Livingstone',1871,'Africa','The journalist Henry Morton Stanley, sent by the New York Herald, finds the missing Scottish missionary and explorer David Livingstone at Ujiji on Lake Tanganyika. His reported greeting, ''Dr. Livingstone, I presume?'', becomes one of the most famous lines in the history of exploration.','medium',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-little-bighorn','Battle of the Little Bighorn',1876,'Americas','Lakota Sioux and Northern Cheyenne warriors led by Sitting Bull and Crazy Horse destroy Lieutenant Colonel George Custer''s detachment of the 7th Cavalry in Montana. The victory is short-lived: the US Army responds with an intensified campaign that forces the Plains nations onto reservations.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('edison-light-bulb','Edison Demonstrates the Light Bulb',1879,'Americas','Thomas Edison and his team at Menlo Park demonstrate a long-lasting incandescent lamp with a carbon filament. Edison''s work on bulbs, and on the power stations to supply them, helps bring electric light into homes and cities around the world.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('benz-motorwagen','Benz Builds the First Practical Automobile',1885,'Europe','Karl Benz builds his three-wheeled Patent-Motorwagen in Mannheim, powered by a petrol engine of his own design, and patents it early the following year. It is widely regarded as the first practical automobile and begins a transformation of transport, cities and industry.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('spanish-american-war','Spanish–American War',1898,'Americas','After the battleship USS Maine explodes in Havana harbour, the United States goes to war with Spain over Cuba. In a few months of fighting the US defeats Spain and gains Puerto Rico, Guam and the Philippines, emerging as a colonial power in the Pacific and the Caribbean.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('eisenhower-elected','Eisenhower Elected US President',1952,'Americas','Dwight D. Eisenhower, the general who commanded Allied forces in Europe during the Second World War, wins the US presidential election for the Republicans. His two terms see the end of the Korean War, the start of the Interstate Highway System and a deepening Cold War.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('france-first-nuclear-test','France Tests Its First Atomic Bomb',1960,'Europe','France explodes its first nuclear device, code-named Gerboise Bleue, in the Algerian Sahara and becomes the world''s fourth nuclear power. The test reflects President de Gaulle''s determination to give France a nuclear deterrent independent of the United States.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('formation-of-malaysia','Federation of Malaysia Formed',1963,'Southeast Asia','Malaya joins with Singapore, Sabah and Sarawak to form the Federation of Malaysia under Prime Minister Tunku Abdul Rahman. The new state faces armed ''Confrontation'' from Indonesia, and Singapore leaves the federation within two years.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('partial-test-ban-treaty','Partial Nuclear Test Ban Treaty Signed',1963,'Global','The United States, the Soviet Union and Britain sign a treaty in Moscow banning nuclear weapons tests in the atmosphere, in outer space and under water. Signed months after the Cuban Missile Crisis, it is the first major arms-control agreement of the Cold War.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('cosmic-microwave-background','Cosmic Microwave Background Discovered',1964,'Americas','Arno Penzias and Robert Wilson of Bell Labs detect a faint microwave signal coming evenly from every direction in the sky. It turns out to be radiation left over from the early universe, providing strong evidence for the Big Bang theory and later earning them a Nobel Prize.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('singapore-independence','Singapore Becomes Independent',1965,'Southeast Asia','Singapore is separated from the Federation of Malaysia and becomes a sovereign city-state, with Lee Kuan Yew as prime minister. Despite having few natural resources, it grows into one of the world''s wealthiest trading hubs.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('death-of-churchill','Death of Winston Churchill',1965,'Europe','Sir Winston Churchill, Britain''s prime minister for most of the Second World War, dies in London at the age of ninety. He is given a state funeral, an honour rarely granted to anyone outside the royal family.','easy',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('jimmy-carter-elected','Jimmy Carter Elected US President',1976,'Americas','Jimmy Carter, a former peanut farmer and governor of Georgia, defeats Gerald Ford in the first presidential election after the Watergate scandal. His presidency brings the Camp David Accords but also economic troubles and the Iran hostage crisis.','easy',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('khmer-rouge-overthrown','Khmer Rouge Driven from Phnom Penh',1979,'Southeast Asia','Vietnamese forces, together with Cambodian rebels opposed to Pol Pot, capture Phnom Penh and drive the Khmer Rouge from power. A Vietnamese-backed government takes over, while the Khmer Rouge retreat to the jungle and fight on for nearly two decades.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('bhutto-executed','Zulfikar Ali Bhutto Executed',1979,'South Asia','Zulfikar Ali Bhutto, Pakistan''s former prime minister and founder of the Pakistan People''s Party, is hanged after a disputed murder trial under the military government of General Zia-ul-Haq. His death makes him a martyr to his supporters, and his daughter Benazir later leads the party.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('us-invasion-of-grenada','United States Invades Grenada',1983,'Americas','After a coup in which Grenada''s prime minister Maurice Bishop is killed, US forces invade the small Caribbean island in Operation Urgent Fury. The intervention, condemned by the UN General Assembly, removes the military government within days.','easy',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('palestinian-declaration-of-independence','Palestinian Declaration of Independence',1988,'Middle East','Meeting in Algiers, the Palestine National Council led by Yasser Arafat proclaims an independent State of Palestine. The declaration implicitly accepts a two-state solution and is soon recognised by many countries, though the territory remains under Israeli occupation.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('spitak-earthquake','Spitak Earthquake in Armenia',1988,'Europe','A powerful earthquake devastates northern Soviet Armenia, destroying the town of Spitak and much of Leninakan and killing tens of thousands of people. For the first time, the Soviet Union openly accepts large-scale aid from the West.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('zia-ul-haq-killed','Zia-ul-Haq Killed in Plane Crash',1988,'South Asia','General Muhammad Zia-ul-Haq, Pakistan''s military ruler since he overthrew Zulfikar Ali Bhutto, dies when his plane crashes near Bahawalpur, along with the US ambassador. Elections later that year bring Benazir Bhutto to power.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('namibia-independence-process','Namibia Becomes Independent',1990,'Africa','Namibia becomes independent after seven decades of South African rule and a long liberation struggle led by SWAPO. UN-supervised elections bring SWAPO to power, and its leader Sam Nujoma becomes the first president, making Namibia one of the last African colonies to gain independence.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('india-rejects-ctbt','India Refuses to Sign the Test Ban Treaty',1996,'South Asia','India refuses to sign the Comprehensive Nuclear-Test-Ban Treaty, objecting that it does not commit the nuclear powers to disarmament, and blocks its adoption at the Conference on Disarmament. The treaty is instead adopted through the UN General Assembly; two years later India carries out nuclear tests.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('sheikh-hasina-first-term','Sheikh Hasina Becomes Prime Minister',1996,'South Asia','Sheikh Hasina, leader of the Awami League and daughter of Bangladesh''s founding leader Sheikh Mujibur Rahman, becomes prime minister for the first time. She goes on to become the country''s longest-serving head of government.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('kofi-annan-secretary-general','Kofi Annan Chosen as UN Secretary-General',1996,'Global','The Ghanaian diplomat Kofi Annan is appointed Secretary-General of the United Nations, the first to rise from within the UN''s own staff. He later shares the Nobel Peace Prize with the UN for work on peace and human rights.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('suharto-resigns','Suharto Resigns',1998,'Southeast Asia','Indonesian President Suharto resigns after more than three decades in power, following the Asian financial crisis, mass protests and riots. His fall opens the Reformasi era of democratic reform in the world''s largest Muslim-majority country.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('clinton-impeached','Bill Clinton Impeached',1998,'Americas','The US House of Representatives impeaches President Bill Clinton on charges of perjury and obstruction of justice arising from his affair with Monica Lewinsky. The Senate acquits him early the following year and he completes his second term.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('kosovo-war-ends','Yugoslavia Accepts Kosovo Peace Plan',1999,'Europe','After eleven weeks of NATO air strikes, Yugoslav President Slobodan Milošević accepts an international peace plan and withdraws Serbian forces from Kosovo. A NATO-led force and a UN administration take over the province, which later declares independence.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('kilby-first-integrated-circuit','Kilby Builds the First Integrated Circuit',1958,'Americas','Jack Kilby of Texas Instruments demonstrates the first working integrated circuit, built on a single piece of germanium that carries a transistor, resistors and a capacitor. Putting a whole circuit on one chip points the way to the modern microchip, and Kilby later receives the Nobel Prize in Physics for it.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('noyce-silicon-chip','Noyce Invents the Silicon Chip',1959,'Americas','Robert Noyce of Fairchild Semiconductor independently invents the monolithic integrated circuit in silicon, using Jean Hoerni''s planar process to build and connect all the components within one flat chip. The design can be mass-produced and becomes the basis of virtually every microchip since, powering the computer age.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('maurya-empire-founded','Chandragupta Maurya Founds the Maurya Empire',-320,'South Asia','Chandragupta Maurya, guided by his adviser Chanakya, overthrows the Nanda dynasty of Magadha and founds the Maurya Empire, ruling from Pataliputra. He goes on to unite most of the Indian subcontinent for the first time and to push back the Greek successors of Alexander.','medium',5,'approximate',1,'c. 320 BCE',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('battle-of-the-hydaspes','Battle of the Hydaspes',-326,'South Asia','Alexander the Great crosses into the Punjab and defeats King Porus at the Hydaspes (Jhelum) River in a hard-fought battle against war elephants. Soon afterwards his exhausted army refuses to march further east, and Alexander turns back at the limit of his conquests.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('arab-conquest-of-sindh','Arab Conquest of Sindh',712,'South Asia','The young Umayyad general Muhammad bin Qasim conquers Sindh, defeating its king, Dahir. The conquest brings the first lasting Muslim rule to the Indian subcontinent and links the region to the wider Islamic world.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('second-battle-of-tarain','Second Battle of Tarain',1192,'South Asia','Muhammad of Ghor defeats the Rajput king Prithviraj Chauhan at Tarain, reversing his own defeat on the same field the year before. The victory opens northern India to Ghurid rule and leads directly to the founding of the Delhi Sultanate.','hard',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('kepler-laws-planetary-motion','Kepler Publishes His Laws of Planetary Motion',1609,'Europe','Johannes Kepler publishes Astronomia nova, showing that the planets move in ellipses rather than perfect circles and sweep out equal areas in equal times. His laws, completed by a third a decade later, lay the foundation for Newton''s theory of gravity.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('aurangzeb-becomes-emperor','Aurangzeb Becomes Mughal Emperor',1658,'South Asia','After defeating his brothers in a war of succession, Aurangzeb takes the Mughal throne and imprisons his father, Shah Jahan, in Agra Fort. His long reign carries the empire to its greatest size but also strains it through constant warfare and religious conflict.','hard',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('third-battle-of-panipat','Third Battle of Panipat',1761,'South Asia','The Afghan ruler Ahmad Shah Durrani defeats a large Maratha army at Panipat, in one of the largest and bloodiest battles of its time. The defeat halts Maratha expansion into northern India and leaves a power vacuum that the East India Company later fills.','hard',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('great-bengal-famine','Great Bengal Famine',1770,'South Asia','Drought and crop failure, made far worse by East India Company revenue demands, cause a catastrophic famine in Bengal. Estimates of the death toll vary widely, up to 10 million people, and the disaster fuels criticism of Company rule in Britain.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('lee-surrenders-appomattox','Lee Surrenders at Appomattox',1865,'Americas','Confederate General Robert E. Lee surrenders the Army of Northern Virginia to Union General Ulysses S. Grant at Appomattox Court House in Virginia. The surrender effectively ends the American Civil War; five days later President Lincoln is assassinated.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('amundsen-south-pole','Amundsen Reaches the South Pole',1911,'Antarctica','The Norwegian explorer Roald Amundsen and his team become the first people to reach the South Pole, travelling with skis and sled dogs. Robert Falcon Scott''s British party arrives five weeks later and dies on the return journey.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('league-of-nations-founded','League of Nations Founded',1920,'Global','The League of Nations, created by the peace settlement after the First World War, comes into being with the aim of preventing future wars through collective security. Weakened by the absence of the United States, it fails to stop the aggression that leads to the Second World War.','easy',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('discovery-of-pluto','Discovery of Pluto',1930,'Americas','Clyde Tombaugh at the Lowell Observatory in Arizona discovers Pluto by comparing photographs of the night sky taken days apart. Counted as the ninth planet for decades, it is later reclassified as a dwarf planet.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('germany-invades-soviet-union','Germany Invades the Soviet Union',1941,'Europe','Nazi Germany and its allies launch Operation Barbarossa, the largest invasion in history, breaking the pact between Hitler and Stalin. The Eastern Front becomes the deadliest theatre of the Second World War, and Germany''s defeat there proves decisive.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('yom-kippur-war','Yom Kippur War',1973,'Middle East','Egypt and Syria launch a surprise attack on Israel on the Jewish holy day of Yom Kippur. Israel recovers and pushes back, but the war shakes confidence on both sides, triggers an Arab oil embargo and opens the way to peace between Egypt and Israel.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('camp-david-accords','Camp David Accords',1978,'Middle East','Egyptian President Anwar Sadat and Israeli Prime Minister Menachem Begin, hosted by US President Jimmy Carter, agree a framework for peace at Camp David. It leads to a peace treaty the following year, making Egypt the first Arab state to recognise Israel.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('gulf-war','Gulf War',1991,'Middle East','A US-led coalition authorised by the United Nations launches Operation Desert Storm to drive Iraqi forces out of Kuwait, which Saddam Hussein had invaded the previous summer. A weeks-long air campaign and a brief ground war liberate Kuwait.','medium',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('bandung-conference','Bandung Conference',1955,'Southeast Asia','Leaders of twenty-nine newly independent Asian and African countries, including Nehru, Sukarno, Nasser and Zhou Enlai, meet in Bandung, Indonesia. They call for an end to colonialism and for cooperation outside the Cold War blocs, laying the groundwork for the Non-Aligned Movement.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('dalai-lama-flees-to-india','Dalai Lama Flees to India',1959,'East Asia','After a failed Tibetan uprising against Chinese rule in Lhasa, the fourteenth Dalai Lama escapes across the Himalayas to India. He sets up a government in exile at Dharamsala, while Tibet remains under the control of the People''s Republic of China.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('indonesia-proclaims-independence','Indonesia Proclaims Independence',1945,'Southeast Asia','Days after Japan''s surrender, Sukarno and Mohammad Hatta proclaim the independence of Indonesia from the Netherlands. Four years of armed and diplomatic struggle follow before the Dutch finally recognise the new republic.','hard',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('burma-independence','Burma Gains Independence',1948,'Southeast Asia','Burma becomes independent from Britain as the Union of Burma and chooses to leave the Commonwealth. Its independence leader, Aung San, had been assassinated months earlier, and the new state soon faces ethnic insurgencies and, later, military rule.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('ceylon-independence','Ceylon Gains Independence',1948,'South Asia','Ceylon becomes independent from Britain as a dominion within the Commonwealth, with D. S. Senanayake as its first prime minister. The island later becomes a republic and takes the name Sri Lanka.','hard',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('assassination-of-sheikh-mujib','Assassination of Sheikh Mujibur Rahman',1975,'South Asia','Sheikh Mujibur Rahman, the founding leader of Bangladesh, is assassinated with most of his family in a military coup in Dhaka. Two of his daughters survive because they are abroad, one of them Sheikh Hasina, who later becomes prime minister.','medium',4,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('death-of-shivaji','Death of Shivaji',1680,'South Asia','Shivaji, founder of the Maratha kingdom, dies at his hill fort of Raigad. His son Sambhaji succeeds him and continues the long struggle against the Mughal emperor Aurangzeb.','hard',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('jfk-elected','John F. Kennedy Elected US President',1960,'Americas','John F. Kennedy narrowly defeats Richard Nixon after the first televised presidential debates, becoming the youngest person ever elected US president and the first Catholic. His short presidency spans the Bay of Pigs, the Cuban Missile Crisis and the start of the race to the Moon.','easy',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('reagan-elected','Ronald Reagan Elected US President',1980,'Americas','The former actor and California governor Ronald Reagan defeats Jimmy Carter in a landslide. His presidency brings tax cuts, a military build-up and a harder line against the Soviet Union, followed by arms-control deals with Gorbachev.','easy',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES('george-hw-bush-elected','George H. W. Bush Elected US President',1988,'Americas','Vice President George H. W. Bush defeats Michael Dukakis to succeed Ronald Reagan. His single term sees the end of the Cold War, the reunification of Germany and the Gulf War.','easy',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','invention-of-the-wheel',0,'{"id": "invention-of-the-wheel", "name": "Invention of the Wheel", "year": -3500, "categories": ["Science", "Culture"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["wheel invented", "plough invented", "Mesopotamia wheel", "first wheel", "sail invented", "wheel and plow"], "description": "The wheel and plough are developed in Mesopotamia around 3500 BC, transforming agriculture, transportation, and trade across the ancient world. The sail appears in Egypt around the same period, enabling maritime commerce along the Nile and beyond. Together these three inventions lay the practical foundation for complex civilization and long-distance exchange.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 9}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','sumerian-writing',1,'{"id": "sumerian-writing", "name": "Invention of Sumerian Writing", "year": -3200, "categories": ["Culture", "Technology"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["cuneiform writing", "Mesopotamia writing", "oldest writing system", "Uruk tablets"], "description": "The Sumerians of ancient Mesopotamia develop cuneiform, the world''s earliest writing system, initially used for recording trade transactions on clay tablets. This invention enables the transmission of complex knowledge, law, and literature across generations and marks the beginning of recorded history.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','first-cities-mesopotamia',2,'{"id": "first-cities-mesopotamia", "name": "First Cities Founded in Mesopotamia", "year": -3000, "categories": ["Culture", "Social"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Sumer cities", "Uruk", "first urban civilization", "Sumerian cities", "cradle of civilization", "first city-states"], "description": "The first true cities emerge in Sumer, the southern region of Mesopotamia, with Uruk growing into the world''s largest settlement with a population in the tens of thousands. These urban centers develop specialized labor, centralized administration, monumental architecture, and complex trade networks stretching across the ancient Near East. The Sumerian city-state becomes the template for human political and social organization.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 8}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','indus-valley-begins',3,'{"id": "indus-valley-begins", "name": "Indus Valley Civilization Begins", "year": -2600, "categories": ["Culture", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Harappan civilization", "Mohenjo-daro", "Harappa", "IVC"], "description": "One of the world''s earliest urban civilizations emerges in the Indus River valley, featuring advanced city planning, drainage systems, and trade networks. Cities like Mohenjo-daro and Harappa flourish with populations in the tens of thousands.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','egyptian-pyramids-built',4,'{"id": "egyptian-pyramids-built", "name": "Great Pyramid of Giza Built", "year": -2560, "categories": ["Culture", "Arts"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Khufu pyramid", "Cheops pyramid", "Giza pyramids", "seven wonders ancient world"], "description": "The Great Pyramid of Giza is constructed as a tomb for Pharaoh Khufu, requiring an estimated 2.3 million stone blocks and decades of labor. It stands as the tallest man-made structure in the world for nearly four millennia and remains one of the seven wonders of the ancient world.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','code-of-hammurabi',5,'{"id": "code-of-hammurabi", "name": "Code of Hammurabi Established", "year": -1754, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Babylonian law", "Hammurabi laws", "eye for an eye", "ancient law code"], "description": "Babylonian king Hammurabi promulgates one of the earliest and most complete written legal codes, covering commerce, property, family, and criminal law. The code, inscribed on a stone stele, introduces the principle of presumption of innocence and establishes the idea of law as a public institution.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','phoenician-alphabet-invented',6,'{"id": "phoenician-alphabet-invented", "name": "Phoenician Alphabet Invented", "year": -1600, "categories": ["Culture", "Science"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["first alphabet", "alphabet invented", "Canaanite alphabet", "Proto-Sinaitic script", "writing system", "consonantal alphabet"], "description": "The Phoenicians develop the first widely used alphabetic writing system, consisting of 22 consonant letters derived from earlier Semitic scripts used in the Sinai Peninsula. Unlike the complex syllabic systems of Mesopotamia and Egypt, the alphabet''s simplicity allows merchants and administrators to learn it rapidly, and it spreads across the Mediterranean world through Phoenician trade networks. Nearly all modern alphabets, including Greek, Latin, Arabic, and Hebrew, descend from this Phoenician innovation.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 9}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','fall-of-troy',7,'{"id": "fall-of-troy", "name": "Fall of Troy", "year": -1200, "categories": ["War", "Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Trojan War ends", "Trojan horse", "Iliad", "Homer", "sack of Troy", "Troy destroyed", "Helen of Troy"], "description": "The city of Troy, located in present-day northwest Turkey, falls to a coalition of Greek forces after a legendary ten-year siege, according to ancient tradition immortalized in Homer''s Iliad. The Trojan horse — a giant wooden horse concealing Greek soldiers — becomes one of history''s most enduring stories of deception in warfare. Archaeological excavations at Hisarlik confirm a real Bronze Age city was violently destroyed around this period, lending historical weight to the legend.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','battle-of-mahabharata',8,'{"id": "battle-of-mahabharata", "name": "Battle of Kurukshetra", "year": -1000, "categories": ["War", "Religion", "Culture"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Mahabharata war", "Kurukshetra war", "Pandava vs Kaurava"], "description": "The legendary war described in the Mahabharata epic, fought between the Pandavas and Kauravas on the plains of Kurukshetra. The conflict forms the backdrop for the Bhagavad Gita and remains central to Hindu philosophy and culture.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','greek-olympics-ancient',9,'{"id": "greek-olympics-ancient", "name": "Ancient Olympic Games Established", "year": -776, "categories": ["Sports", "Culture", "Religion"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Olympia games", "Greek athletics", "ancient Greece sports", "Zeus festival"], "description": "The ancient Olympic Games are held for the first time at Olympia in ancient Greece as a religious festival honoring Zeus, featuring athletic and chariot racing competitions. The games are held every four years for over a millennium and become the inspiration for the modern Olympic movement.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','founding-of-rome',10,'{"id": "founding-of-rome", "name": "Founding of Rome", "year": -753, "categories": ["Politics", "Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Romulus Remus", "Roman foundation", "Seven Hills Rome", "Latin kingdom"], "description": "According to Roman tradition, the city of Rome is founded by Romulus on the Palatine Hill, marking the beginning of a civilization that will shape Western history for over a millennium. The city grows from a small settlement of Latin and Sabine peoples into the heart of a vast empire.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','ironworking-spreads',11,'{"id": "ironworking-spreads", "name": "Ironworking Spreads Across the Old World", "year": -670, "categories": ["Science", "Culture"], "region": "World", "aliases": ["Iron Age", "iron smelting", "iron tools", "iron weapons", "metallurgy", "iron technology", "iron age begins"], "description": "Iron smelting technology, first developed in Anatolia around 1200 BC, spreads widely across Europe, Asia, and Africa during the early first millennium BC. Iron''s abundance and superior hardness compared to bronze democratize the production of agricultural tools and weapons, reshaping economies, armies, and societies across three continents. The Iron Age marks a fundamental turning point in human technological development, enabling more productive farming, more lethal warfare, and larger political structures.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','babylonian-conquest-jerusalem',12,'{"id": "babylonian-conquest-jerusalem", "name": "Babylonian Conquest of Jerusalem", "year": -588, "categories": ["War", "Religion"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Nebuchadnezzar Jerusalem", "Babylonian exile", "destruction of Solomon''s Temple", "Jewish exile", "Captivity in Babylon", "First Temple destroyed"], "description": "King Nebuchadnezzar II of Babylon conquers Jerusalem, destroys Solomon''s Temple, and deports much of the Jewish population to Babylon in what becomes known as the Babylonian captivity. The exile profoundly reshapes Jewish theology and identity, accelerating the development of strict monotheism and the compilation of the Hebrew Bible. The event is foundational to the history of Judaism, Christianity, and Islam, and the longing to return to Jerusalem becomes a defining element of Jewish culture.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','thales-solar-eclipse',13,'{"id": "thales-solar-eclipse", "name": "Thales Predicts a Solar Eclipse", "year": -585, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Thales of Miletus", "first philosopher", "Greek philosophy begins", "eclipse prediction", "pre-Socratic philosophy", "natural philosophy"], "description": "The Greek philosopher Thales of Miletus successfully predicts a solar eclipse, marking one of the first recorded instances of scientific reasoning applied to natural phenomena rather than divine intervention. Thales seeks material and natural explanations for the world around him, establishing the foundational attitude that underpins Western science and philosophy. Ancient tradition credits him as the first philosopher, the originator of a tradition of rational inquiry that runs through Socrates, Plato, and Aristotle.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','birth-of-buddha',14,'{"id": "birth-of-buddha", "name": "Birth of Siddhartha Gautama", "year": -563, "categories": ["Religion"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Buddha born", "Gautama Buddha", "Prince Siddhartha", "founder of Buddhism"], "description": "Siddhartha Gautama is born in Lumbini into a royal family of the Shakya clan. He would later renounce his privileged life and attain enlightenment, becoming the Buddha and founding one of the world''s major religions.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','birth-of-confucius',15,'{"id": "birth-of-confucius", "name": "Birth of Confucius", "year": -551, "categories": ["Religion", "Culture"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Kongzi", "Kong Qiu", "Confucianism founder", "Chinese philosopher born", "Analects", "Chinese philosophy"], "description": "Kong Qiu, known to the world as Confucius, is born in the state of Lu in present-day Shandong, China. His teachings on ethics, social harmony, filial piety, and good governance — collected by his disciples in the Analects — shape Chinese civilization for over two millennia. Confucianism becomes the dominant philosophical and political framework across East Asia, profoundly influencing law, education, family structure, and governance from China to Korea, Japan, and Vietnam.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 8}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','cyrus-founds-persian-empire',16,'{"id": "cyrus-founds-persian-empire", "name": "Cyrus the Great Founds the Persian Empire", "year": -550, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Achaemenid Empire", "Persian Empire founded", "Cyrus the Great", "Cyrus cylinder", "first Persian Empire", "Persia rises"], "description": "Cyrus II of Persia defeats the Median, Lydian, and Babylonian kingdoms in quick succession to establish the Achaemenid Empire, the largest empire the world had yet seen, stretching from the Aegean Sea to the Indus River. Renowned for tolerating the customs and religions of conquered peoples, Cyrus permits the Jewish exiles in Babylon to return to their homeland and rebuild their temple, an act celebrated in the Hebrew Bible. The Cyrus Cylinder, recording his policies, is often cited as one of humanity''s earliest declarations of human rights.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 8}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','roman-republic-founded',17,'{"id": "roman-republic-founded", "name": "Roman Republic Established", "year": -509, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Roman Republic", "Lucius Brutus", "Tarquin expelled", "consul system Rome"], "description": "The Romans expel their last king Tarquin the Proud and establish a republic governed by elected consuls and the Senate. The Roman Republic''s system of checks and balances and mixed constitution becomes an enduring model for later democracies and republican governments.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','greek-democracy-athens',18,'{"id": "greek-democracy-athens", "name": "Athenian Democracy Established", "year": -508, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Cleisthenes reforms", "birth of democracy", "Athenian constitution", "Greek democracy"], "description": "Cleisthenes introduces democratic reforms in Athens, establishing a system of governance in which citizens participate directly in decision-making through the assembly. Often called the ''Father of Democracy,'' his reforms create the world''s first democratic political system.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','battle-of-marathon',19,'{"id": "battle-of-marathon", "name": "Battle of Marathon", "year": -490, "categories": ["War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Greek Persian war", "Miltiades victory", "Persian invasion Greece", "Marathon run origin"], "description": "A small Athenian army defeats a much larger Persian force at Marathon, halting the first Persian invasion of Greece. The victory becomes a defining moment of Greek identity and the legend of a messenger running to Athens to announce the victory gives birth to the modern marathon race.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','hippocrates-medicine',20,'{"id": "hippocrates-medicine", "name": "Hippocrates Founds Rational Medicine", "year": -400, "categories": ["Medicine", "Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Father of Medicine", "Greek medicine", "Hippocratic oath", "scientific medicine begins"], "description": "Hippocrates of Kos establishes medicine as a rational discipline separate from superstition and religion, emphasizing observation, diagnosis, and prognosis. His approach, recorded in the Hippocratic Corpus, forms the foundation of Western medical practice, and the Hippocratic Oath remains a touchstone of medical ethics.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','socrates-execution',21,'{"id": "socrates-execution", "name": "Execution of Socrates", "year": -399, "categories": ["Culture", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Socrates trial", "Socrates hemlock", "Athenian philosopher death", "Plato teacher"], "description": "The philosopher Socrates is condemned to death by an Athenian jury on charges of impiety and corrupting the youth, choosing to drink hemlock rather than flee. His execution, recorded by his student Plato, becomes the defining martyr story of Western philosophy and raises enduring questions about truth, justice, and civil disobedience.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','platos-academy-founded',22,'{"id": "platos-academy-founded", "name": "Plato Founds the Academy", "year": -387, "categories": ["Culture", "Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Athens Academy", "Plato school", "first university Europe", "philosophy school"], "description": "Plato establishes the Academy in Athens, often considered the first institution of higher learning in the Western world, where philosophy, mathematics, and science are taught. It attracts scholars from across the Greek world and operates for nearly nine centuries, shaping the development of Western intellectual tradition.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','alexander-conquests',23,'{"id": "alexander-conquests", "name": "Alexander the Great''s Conquests Begin", "year": -334, "categories": ["War", "Politics", "Exploration"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Alexander Macedonia", "Hellenistic conquests", "Persian empire defeated", "Alexandria founded"], "description": "Alexander III of Macedonia crosses into Asia and begins a decade of military campaigns that will create one of history''s largest empires, stretching from Greece to northwestern India. His conquests spread Greek culture across the ancient world and usher in the Hellenistic period.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','alexander-founds-alexandria',24,'{"id": "alexander-founds-alexandria", "name": "Alexander the Great Founds Alexandria", "year": -332, "categories": ["Politics", "Culture"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Alexandria founded", "Alexandria Egypt", "Library of Alexandria", "Hellenistic Egypt", "Alexander in Egypt", "Alexandria city"], "description": "After conquering Egypt from the Persians, Alexander the Great founds the city of Alexandria on the Mediterranean coast, envisioning a great center of Hellenistic culture and commerce linking Greece with Egypt. The city grows into one of the ancient world''s largest metropolises and home to the legendary Library of Alexandria, an institution that attracts scholars from across the known world and preserves the accumulated knowledge of antiquity. Alexandria remains the intellectual capital of the Mediterranean world for centuries after Alexander''s death.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','battle-of-gaugamela',25,'{"id": "battle-of-gaugamela", "name": "Battle of Gaugamela", "year": -331, "categories": ["War"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Alexander defeats Darius", "Darius III defeated", "fall of Persian Empire", "Battle of Arbela", "331 BC battle", "end of Achaemenid Empire"], "description": "Alexander the Great decisively defeats the Persian King Darius III at Gaugamela in present-day Iraq, effectively ending the Achaemenid Persian Empire despite being significantly outnumbered. Alexander''s oblique advance and the disciplined Macedonian phalanx shatter the Persian army, opening the road to Babylon, Persepolis, and the East. The battle marks the decisive replacement of Persian hegemony in the Near East with Hellenistic Greek culture, reshaping the civilizations of three continents.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','death-of-alexander',26,'{"id": "death-of-alexander", "name": "Death of Alexander the Great", "year": -323, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Alexander dies", "Alexander the Great dies", "death in Babylon", "Wars of the Diadochi", "Macedonian empire collapses", "successor wars"], "description": "Alexander the Great dies in Babylon at the age of 32, possibly from typhoid fever compounded by heavy drinking, though the cause remains debated. Having built the largest empire the world had yet seen — stretching from Greece to the borders of India — he leaves no clear successor, reportedly saying the empire should go ''to the strongest.'' His death triggers the Wars of the Diadochi, in which his generals carve up the empire into rival Hellenistic kingdoms and spread Greek culture from Egypt to Central Asia.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 8}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','ashoka-becomes-emperor',27,'{"id": "ashoka-becomes-emperor", "name": "Ashoka Becomes Mauryan Emperor", "year": -268, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Ashoka the Great", "Maurya emperor", "Ashoka accession"], "description": "Ashoka ascends to the throne of the Mauryan Empire, which at its height spans most of the Indian subcontinent. His reign would become one of the most significant in Indian history due to his later conversion to Buddhist principles of nonviolence.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','punic-wars',28,'{"id": "punic-wars", "name": "Punic Wars Between Rome and Carthage", "year": -264, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Hannibal Alps", "Carthage Rome war", "Third Punic War", "Scipio Africanus"], "description": "Rome and the North African city-state of Carthage fight three devastating wars over more than a century for dominance of the western Mediterranean. The wars culminate in the complete destruction of Carthage and establish Rome as the unchallenged master of the Mediterranean world.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','ashoka-converts-to-buddhism',29,'{"id": "ashoka-converts-to-buddhism", "name": "Ashoka Converts to Buddhism", "year": -260, "categories": ["Religion", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Ashoka embraces Buddhism", "Kalinga war aftermath", "Ashoka edicts"], "description": "Horrified by the devastation caused by the Kalinga War, Ashoka embraces Buddhism and adopts a policy of nonviolence and dharma. He erects pillars and edicts across his empire promoting Buddhist values, transforming Indian governance.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','eratosthenes-measures-earth',30,'{"id": "eratosthenes-measures-earth", "name": "Eratosthenes Measures the Earth''s Circumference", "year": -240, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Eratosthenes", "Earth''s circumference calculated", "Greek geography", "Alexandria scientist", "ancient astronomy", "round Earth measurement"], "description": "The Greek mathematician and librarian Eratosthenes calculates the circumference of the Earth by measuring the difference in the angle of the sun''s shadow between Alexandria and Syene at the summer solstice, deducing that the two cities are separated by about one-fiftieth of the full circle. His result of approximately 40,000 kilometers is remarkably close to the modern measurement. The achievement stands as one of antiquity''s greatest scientific accomplishments, demonstrating the power of mathematical reasoning applied to physical observation.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','qin-unification-china',31,'{"id": "qin-unification-china", "name": "Qin Dynasty Unifies China", "year": -221, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Qin Shi Huangdi", "First Emperor China", "Warring States ends", "Chinese unification"], "description": "Qin Shi Huangdi defeats all rival Warring States and unifies China for the first time under a single emperor, establishing the Qin dynasty. He standardizes weights, measures, writing, and currency across the empire and begins construction of the Great Wall of China.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','great-wall-china',32,'{"id": "great-wall-china", "name": "Construction of the Great Wall of China Begins", "year": -215, "categories": ["Technology", "Politics", "War"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Chinese wall built", "Qin wall", "northern frontier wall", "world''s longest wall"], "description": "Emperor Qin Shi Huangdi orders the connection and extension of existing northern walls to create a unified defensive barrier against nomadic invasions. The Great Wall, extended and rebuilt by successive dynasties especially the Ming, becomes one of history''s greatest engineering achievements.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','silk-road-opens',33,'{"id": "silk-road-opens", "name": "Silk Road Trade Route Opens", "year": -130, "categories": ["Exploration", "Culture", "Technology"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Han dynasty trade", "China trade routes", "spice route", "Zhang Qian expedition"], "description": "Han dynasty emperor Wudi sends envoy Zhang Qian westward, opening sustained trade connections between China, Central Asia, and eventually the Mediterranean world. The Silk Road carries not only silk and spices but ideas, religions, technologies, and diseases across continents for centuries.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','first-triumvirate',34,'{"id": "first-triumvirate", "name": "First Triumvirate Formed", "year": -60, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Caesar Pompey Crassus", "Roman triumvirate", "Julius Caesar alliance", "Roman Republic crisis", "60 BC Rome", "three men rule Rome"], "description": "Julius Caesar, Pompey the Great, and Marcus Crassus form an informal political alliance known as the First Triumvirate, effectively dominating Roman politics and marginalizing the Senate. The alliance allows Caesar to secure the consulship and a military command in Gaul, where he spends the next decade building the veteran army that will carry him to supreme power. The Triumvirate marks the beginning of the end for the Roman Republic, setting in motion the events that lead to civil war and the age of emperors.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','caesar-crosses-rubicon',35,'{"id": "caesar-crosses-rubicon", "name": "Caesar Crosses the Rubicon", "year": -49, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Rubicon river", "Roman Civil War begins", "alea iacta est", "the die is cast", "Caesar vs Pompey", "49 BC Rome"], "description": "Julius Caesar leads his battle-hardened army across the Rubicon river into Italy, violating Roman law that forbade generals from bringing troops into the Republic''s heartland. The act, accompanied by the famous phrase ''the die is cast,'' triggers a civil war that will ultimately destroy the Roman Republic. Caesar''s crossing has become a lasting metaphor for any irrevocable decision that commits one fully to a course of action.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','julius-caesar-assassination',36,'{"id": "julius-caesar-assassination", "name": "Julius Caesar Assassinated", "year": -44, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Ides of March", "Brutus Cassius", "Roman Republic crisis", "Senate assassination"], "description": "Roman dictator Julius Caesar is stabbed to death by a group of senators including Brutus and Cassius on the steps of the Senate on the Ides of March. His assassination plunges Rome into civil war and ultimately leads to the transformation of the Republic into the Roman Empire.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','augustus-first-emperor',37,'{"id": "augustus-first-emperor", "name": "Augustus Becomes First Roman Emperor", "year": -27, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Octavian Augustus", "Roman Empire begins", "Pax Romana", "Principate Rome"], "description": "Octavian, nephew of Julius Caesar, receives the title Augustus from the Roman Senate, marking the beginning of the Roman Empire and the end of the Republic. His long and stable reign inaugurates the Pax Romana, two centuries of relative peace across the vast Roman world.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','pax-romana',38,'{"id": "pax-romana", "name": "Pax Romana Begins", "year": -27, "categories": ["Politics", "Culture", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Roman peace", "Roman golden age", "Augustus peace", "empire stability"], "description": "The accession of Augustus initiates the Pax Romana, roughly two centuries of relative peace and stability across the Roman Empire during which trade, law, and culture flourish. The period sees the construction of roads, aqueducts, and monumental architecture that will shape European civilization for millennia.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','birth-of-jesus',39,'{"id": "birth-of-jesus", "name": "Birth of Jesus of Nazareth", "year": -4, "categories": ["Religion"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Jesus Christ born", "Nativity", "Bethlehem birth", "founder of Christianity"], "description": "Jesus of Nazareth is born in the Roman province of Judea, an event that marks year one of the Christian calendar and the origin point of the world''s largest religion. His teachings of love, forgiveness, and salvation would transform the spiritual and cultural landscape of human civilization.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','crucifixion-of-jesus',40,'{"id": "crucifixion-of-jesus", "name": "Crucifixion of Jesus", "year": 29, "categories": ["Religion"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Jesus crucified", "death of Jesus", "Good Friday", "Jesus of Nazareth executed", "Golgotha", "Calvary", "resurrection of Jesus"], "description": "Jesus of Nazareth is executed by crucifixion under the Roman prefect Pontius Pilate in Jerusalem, an event recorded in both Christian scripture and Roman historical sources. His followers'' belief in his subsequent resurrection becomes the central doctrine of Christianity, transforming a small Jewish sect into a religion that spreads across the Roman Empire and eventually to every corner of the world. The crucifixion and its theological interpretation remain the defining moment of the Christian faith, observed by over two billion people today.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 9}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','great-fire-of-rome',41,'{"id": "great-fire-of-rome", "name": "Great Fire of Rome", "year": 64, "categories": ["Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Rome burns", "Nero fiddles", "64 AD fire", "Nero blamed Christians", "Roman fire", "Nero Rome"], "description": "A devastating fire sweeps through Rome for six days, destroying or severely damaging ten of the city''s fourteen districts and leaving hundreds of thousands homeless. Emperor Nero, almost certainly absent when the fire began, is later accused by rumor and legend of starting it himself — a charge almost certainly false. The disaster gives Nero the opportunity to rebuild much of Rome in a grander style and leads to the first major Roman persecution of Christians, whom he scapegoats for the catastrophe.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','eruption-of-vesuvius',42,'{"id": "eruption-of-vesuvius", "name": "Eruption of Mount Vesuvius", "year": 79, "categories": ["Culture", "Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Pompeii destroyed", "Herculaneum buried", "Vesuvius erupts", "79 AD volcano", "Pliny the Younger", "Pompeii excavations"], "description": "Mount Vesuvius erupts catastrophically, burying the Roman cities of Pompeii and Herculaneum under meters of volcanic ash and pyroclastic material and killing thousands within hours. The disaster is vividly described by Pliny the Younger in letters that become the first detailed eyewitness accounts of a volcanic eruption. The remarkably preserved ruins, rediscovered and excavated from the eighteenth century onward, provide an unparalleled snapshot of daily life in the Roman world.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','paper-invented-china',43,'{"id": "paper-invented-china", "name": "Paper Invented in China", "year": 105, "categories": ["Science", "Culture"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Cai Lun", "Chinese paper", "papermaking", "invention of paper", "Han dynasty paper", "paper production"], "description": "Cai Lun, a court official of the Eastern Han dynasty, refines and standardizes the process of making paper from bark, hemp, rags, and fishing nets, presenting his improved method to the emperor. Paper rapidly replaces more expensive and cumbersome writing materials such as silk and bamboo strips. The invention spreads westward via the Silk Road over subsequent centuries, transforming record-keeping, administration, literature, and communication across Eurasia.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 8}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','hadrians-wall',44,'{"id": "hadrians-wall", "name": "Hadrian''s Wall Construction Begins", "year": 122, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Hadrian''s Wall", "Roman Britain", "northern Roman frontier", "Scotland Roman wall", "Roman fortification Britain", "Vallum Hadriani"], "description": "The Roman Emperor Hadrian orders the construction of a defensive wall stretching 117 kilometers across northern Britain, from the Solway Firth to the River Tyne, to control movement between Roman Britain and the unconquered tribes of Caledonia. The wall is the most heavily fortified frontier in the entire Roman Empire, lined with forts, milecastles, and turrets garrisoned by tens of thousands of soldiers. It remains the best-preserved Roman military structure in the world and a UNESCO World Heritage Site.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','maya-classic-period',45,'{"id": "maya-classic-period", "name": "Maya Classic Period", "year": 250, "categories": ["Culture", "Science", "Arts"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Maya civilization", "Mayan pyramids", "Mayan calendar", "Tikal Palenque", "Mesoamerica"], "description": "The Maya civilization enters its Classic Period, building monumental city-states like Tikal and Palenque with sophisticated writing, calendars, and astronomical observations. Maya mathematics independently develops the concept of zero and their calendar system achieves remarkable precision.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','christianity-roman-empire',46,'{"id": "christianity-roman-empire", "name": "Edict of Milan: Christianity Legalized", "year": 313, "categories": ["Religion", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Constantine Christianity", "Edict of Milan", "Roman Christianity", "persecution ends Christians"], "description": "Emperor Constantine issues the Edict of Milan, legalizing Christianity throughout the Roman Empire and ending decades of persecution of Christians. Constantine''s personal conversion and this decree set in motion the transformation of the Roman Empire into a Christian state.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','gupta-empire-founded',47,'{"id": "gupta-empire-founded", "name": "Gupta Empire Founded", "year": 320, "categories": ["Politics", "Culture"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Chandragupta I", "Gupta dynasty", "golden age India"], "description": "Chandragupta I establishes the Gupta Empire in northern India, inaugurating a period often called the Golden Age of India. Under Gupta rule, advances in mathematics, astronomy, literature, and the arts would flourish across the subcontinent.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','constantinople-founded',48,'{"id": "constantinople-founded", "name": "Constantinople Founded", "year": 324, "categories": ["Politics", "Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Byzantium renamed", "New Rome", "capital moved east", "Constantine''s city", "Istanbul history", "Byzantine Empire capital", "Eastern capital"], "description": "Emperor Constantine the Great dedicates his new capital at the ancient Greek city of Byzantium, renaming it Constantinople in his own honor and investing it with the institutions and architectural splendor of a new Rome. Strategically positioned at the crossroads of Europe and Asia controlling the Bosphorus strait, the city becomes the wealthiest and most powerful city in the Christian world for over a thousand years. As the capital of the Byzantine Empire, Constantinople preserves Roman law and Greek learning through the medieval period until its fall to the Ottoman Turks in 1453.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','nalanda-university-founded',49,'{"id": "nalanda-university-founded", "name": "Nalanda University Founded", "year": 427, "categories": ["Culture", "Religion", "Science"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Nalanda monastery", "ancient Indian university", "Buddhist learning center"], "description": "Nalanda is established as one of the world''s first residential universities in Bihar, attracting scholars from across Asia. At its peak, it housed thousands of students and monks studying a curriculum spanning Buddhist philosophy, logic, grammar, and medicine.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','attila-hun-invasions',50,'{"id": "attila-hun-invasions", "name": "Attila the Hun Invades Europe", "year": 450, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Attila Hun", "Scourge of God", "Hunnic Empire", "Battle of Catalaunian Plains"], "description": "Attila leads the Hunnic Empire in devastating raids into the Eastern and Western Roman Empire, earning the epithet ''Scourge of God'' for his destruction of cities and countryside. Though stopped at the Battle of the Catalaunian Plains, his invasions accelerate the fragmentation of the Western Roman Empire.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','fall-of-roman-empire-west',51,'{"id": "fall-of-roman-empire-west", "name": "Fall of the Western Roman Empire", "year": 476, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Romulus Augustulus deposed", "end of Rome", "Roman collapse", "barbarian kingdoms"], "description": "The last Western Roman Emperor, Romulus Augustulus, is deposed by the Germanic chieftain Odoacer, marking the conventional end of the Western Roman Empire and the beginning of the Middle Ages. The fall reshapes Europe into a mosaic of Germanic kingdoms with profound consequences for civilization.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','aryabhata-heliocentric',52,'{"id": "aryabhata-heliocentric", "name": "Aryabhata Proposes Earth''s Rotation", "year": 499, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Aryabhata astronomy", "Indian mathematics", "zero invention", "Aryabhatiya"], "description": "The Indian mathematician and astronomer Aryabhata publishes the Aryabhatiya, proposing that the Earth rotates on its axis and calculating the approximate value of pi. His work establishes foundational concepts in Indian mathematics and astronomy.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','birth-of-muhammad',53,'{"id": "birth-of-muhammad", "name": "Birth of Muhammad", "year": 570, "categories": ["Religion"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Prophet Muhammad born", "Islam founder born", "Mecca 570", "Prophet of Islam", "Muhammad ibn Abdullah", "birth of the Prophet"], "description": "Muhammad ibn Abdullah is born in Mecca, in the Arabian Peninsula, into the Quraysh tribe, the guardians of the Kaaba. He would receive his first divine revelation at the age of forty, beginning the delivery of the message that becomes the Quran. As the founder of Islam, Muhammad''s life and teachings shape one of the world''s largest religions and transform the political, cultural, and spiritual landscape of the Middle East, Africa, and far beyond.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 9}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','harsha-reign-begins',54,'{"id": "harsha-reign-begins", "name": "Harsha''s Reign Begins", "year": 606, "categories": ["Politics", "Culture"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Harshavardhana", "Harsha of Kannauj", "Pushyabhuti dynasty"], "description": "Harshavardhana becomes ruler of a large empire centered at Kannauj, uniting much of northern India after the fall of the Gupta Empire. His reign is noted for religious tolerance, support of Buddhist and Hindu scholarship, and diplomatic exchanges with China.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','founding-of-islam',55,'{"id": "founding-of-islam", "name": "Muhammad Receives First Revelation", "year": 610, "categories": ["Religion"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Prophet Muhammad", "Islam founded", "Quran begins", "Cave of Hira", "birth of Islam"], "description": "The Prophet Muhammad receives the first revelation of the Quran in the Cave of Hira near Mecca, which marks the beginning of Islam. Over the following decades, his preaching gives rise to a new monotheistic religion that will reshape the spiritual, political, and cultural landscape of the world.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','hijra',56,'{"id": "hijra", "name": "The Hijra: Muhammad Migrates to Medina", "year": 622, "categories": ["Religion", "Politics"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Hijra", "Muhammad flees Mecca", "Islamic calendar begins", "Medina migration", "Year One of Islam", "622 AD Islam"], "description": "Facing persecution from the Quraysh in Mecca, Muhammad and his followers migrate to the city of Medina in an event known as the Hijra. In Medina, Muhammad establishes the first Muslim community, drafts the Constitution of Medina creating a political-religious framework for governance, and begins building the mosque that becomes the model for Islamic worship. The year of the Hijra is taken as Year One of the Islamic lunar calendar, marking it as the defining moment in the founding of Islam as both a faith and a political community.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 8}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','invention-of-zero',57,'{"id": "invention-of-zero", "name": "Invention of Zero in India", "year": 628, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Brahmagupta zero", "Indian mathematics zero", "numeral system zero", "place value system"], "description": "Indian mathematician Brahmagupta formalizes the rules for arithmetic operations involving zero in his work Brahmasphutasiddhanta, treating zero as a number in its own right for the first time. This revolutionary concept, combined with the Hindu-Arabic numeral system, becomes foundational to all of modern mathematics and computing.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','arab-traders-kerala',58,'{"id": "arab-traders-kerala", "name": "Arab Traders Arrive in Kerala", "year": 629, "categories": ["Exploration", "Religion", "Culture"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Islam comes to India", "Cheraman Perumal", "Malabar Muslims", "Arab merchants India"], "description": "Arab traders establish early Muslim communities on the Malabar Coast, initiating a long history of Islamic influence in Kerala. According to tradition, the Cheraman Perumal mosque built during this period is one of the oldest mosques in Asia.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','islamic-caliphate-expands',59,'{"id": "islamic-caliphate-expands", "name": "Islamic Caliphate Expands Across Arabia", "year": 632, "categories": ["Politics", "Religion", "War"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Rashidun Caliphate", "Muslim conquests", "early Islamic empire", "Abu Bakr caliph"], "description": "Following the death of the Prophet Muhammad, Abu Bakr becomes the first caliph and launches military campaigns that rapidly expand Islamic rule across Arabia and beyond. Within a century, the Caliphate stretches from Spain to Central Asia, one of the fastest imperial expansions in history.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','moors-invade-spain',60,'{"id": "moors-invade-spain", "name": "Moors Invade Spain", "year": 711, "categories": ["War", "Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Arab invasion Spain", "Umayyad Spain", "Tariq ibn Ziyad", "Muslim conquest Iberia", "Al-Andalus", "Reconquista begins", "Gibraltar name origin"], "description": "A Muslim army under Tariq ibn Ziyad crosses the Strait of Gibraltar — a name derived from ''Jabal al-Tariq,'' or ''Rock of Tariq'' — and defeats the Visigothic King Roderic, rapidly overrunning most of the Iberian Peninsula. The resulting Muslim territory of Al-Andalus becomes a center of Islamic culture, science, and philosophy, transmitting Greek and Arabic knowledge to medieval Europe through translations in Toledo and Cordoba. The Moorish presence in Spain lasts nearly eight centuries until the final Reconquista in 1492.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','woodblock-printing-china',61,'{"id": "woodblock-printing-china", "name": "Woodblock Printing Invented in China", "year": 730, "categories": ["Science", "Culture"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["block printing", "Chinese printing Tang dynasty", "xylography", "mass communication China", "Diamond Sutra", "print technology China"], "description": "Woodblock printing is developed in Tang dynasty China, enabling text and images carved in relief on wooden blocks to be reproduced cheaply and repeatedly on paper. The technology enables the mass production of Buddhist texts, government documents, and eventually paper money, dramatically increasing access to information and accelerating literacy. Woodblock printing spreads across East Asia before Bi Sheng''s invention of movable type three centuries later further refines the process.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','battle-of-tours',62,'{"id": "battle-of-tours", "name": "Battle of Tours", "year": 732, "categories": ["War", "Religion"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Battle of Poitiers", "Charles Martel", "Muslim invasion stopped Europe", "Frankish victory"], "description": "Frankish leader Charles Martel defeats an advancing Muslim army at Tours in central France, halting the northward expansion of the Umayyad Caliphate into Western Europe. Many historians regard this battle as decisive in preserving Christianity as the dominant religion of Europe.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','islamic-golden-age',63,'{"id": "islamic-golden-age", "name": "Islamic Golden Age Begins", "year": 786, "categories": ["Science", "Culture", "Arts"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Abbasid caliphate", "House of Wisdom", "Baghdad golden age", "Arab science"], "description": "The reign of Harun al-Rashid and the establishment of the House of Wisdom in Baghdad inaugurates a golden age of Islamic science, mathematics, philosophy, and medicine. Scholars translate and extend Greek knowledge while making original contributions in algebra, optics, astronomy, and medicine.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','viking-raids-begin',64,'{"id": "viking-raids-begin", "name": "Viking Age Begins", "year": 793, "categories": ["War", "Exploration"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Norse raids", "Lindisfarne raid", "Viking expansion", "Norsemen"], "description": "Norse warriors raid the monastery of Lindisfarne on the English coast in one of the first recorded Viking attacks, inaugurating the Viking Age. Over the following centuries, Norsemen range from Newfoundland to Russia, Constantinople to North Africa, as traders, settlers, and raiders reshaping European history.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','charlemagne-crowned-emperor',65,'{"id": "charlemagne-crowned-emperor", "name": "Charlemagne Crowned Holy Roman Emperor", "year": 800, "categories": ["Politics", "Religion"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Charles the Great", "Pope Leo III", "Frankish empire", "Carolingian empire"], "description": "Pope Leo III crowns Charlemagne, King of the Franks, as Holy Roman Emperor on Christmas Day in St. Peter''s Basilica, creating a new imperial power in Western Europe. Charlemagne''s reign unites much of Western Europe, promotes literacy and education, and shapes the political and cultural identity of medieval Europe.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','gunpowder-invented',66,'{"id": "gunpowder-invented", "name": "Gunpowder Invented in China", "year": 850, "categories": ["Technology", "Science", "War"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Chinese gunpowder", "black powder", "fireworks origin", "explosive powder"], "description": "Chinese alchemists experimenting with elixirs of immortality discover the explosive properties of a mixture of sulfur, charcoal, and saltpeter, inventing gunpowder. The discovery revolutionizes warfare when it reaches Europe centuries later, making medieval fortifications obsolete and transforming military tactics worldwide.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','kievan-rus-founded',67,'{"id": "kievan-rus-founded", "name": "Founding of Kievan Rus", "year": 882, "categories": ["Politics", "Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Kiev founded", "Viking Russia", "Varangians", "Oleg of Novgorod", "origin of Russia", "East Slavic state", "Rurik dynasty"], "description": "The Varangian prince Oleg captures Kiev and makes it the capital of a new state uniting the East Slavic and Norse trading communities along the Dnieper river route connecting Scandinavia to Byzantium. Kievan Rus becomes the first major East Slavic political entity, laying the cultural, religious, and political foundations for the later nations of Russia, Ukraine, and Belarus. Its adoption of Orthodox Christianity from Byzantium in 988 shapes Eastern European civilization for centuries.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','chola-rajaraja-peak',68,'{"id": "chola-rajaraja-peak", "name": "Chola Dynasty Reaches Its Peak", "year": 985, "categories": ["Politics", "Culture"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Rajaraja Chola", "Chola empire", "Brihadeeswarar temple", "Tamil kingdoms"], "description": "Rajaraja I ascends to the Chola throne and expands the dynasty into a maritime empire dominating South India and parts of Southeast Asia. He commissions the great Brihadeeswarar temple at Thanjavur, a masterpiece of Dravidian architecture.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','viking-exploration-north-america',69,'{"id": "viking-exploration-north-america", "name": "Vikings Reach North America", "year": 1000, "categories": ["Exploration"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Leif Erikson", "Vinland", "Norse North America", "Viking discovery America"], "description": "Leif Erikson leads a Norse expedition that establishes a settlement at L''Anse aux Meadows in what is now Newfoundland, Canada, nearly five centuries before Columbus. Archaeological evidence confirms this as the first known European contact with the Americas.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','mahmud-ghazni-somnath',70,'{"id": "mahmud-ghazni-somnath", "name": "Mahmud of Ghazni Raids Somnath", "year": 1026, "categories": ["War", "Religion"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Somnath temple raid", "Ghaznavid invasion", "Mahmud Ghazni"], "description": "Sultan Mahmud of Ghazni leads one of his many raids into the Indian subcontinent, sacking the wealthy Somnath temple on the Gujarat coast. The raid becomes a defining moment in the history of Muslim-Hindu relations on the subcontinent.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','printing-movable-type-china',71,'{"id": "printing-movable-type-china", "name": "Bi Sheng Invents Movable Type in China", "year": 1040, "categories": ["Technology", "Culture"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Chinese printing", "Bi Sheng movable type", "Song dynasty printing", "ceramic movable type"], "description": "Bi Sheng of the Song dynasty invents movable type printing using ceramic characters, four centuries before Gutenberg''s press in Europe. The technology enables the mass production of books and spreads literacy and knowledge across China and East Asia.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','great-schism',72,'{"id": "great-schism", "name": "Great Schism Divides Christianity", "year": 1054, "categories": ["Religion"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["East-West Schism", "Catholic Orthodox split", "Rome Constantinople split", "papal schism 1054", "Eastern Orthodox Church founded", "Latin Greek church split"], "description": "The Pope in Rome and the Patriarch of Constantinople mutually excommunicate each other, formalizing the split of Christianity into the Roman Catholic and Eastern Orthodox churches. The division, rooted in centuries of theological disagreements over papal authority, the nature of the Holy Spirit, and the use of images in worship, proves permanent and is never healed. It reshapes the religious map of Europe and contributes to the divergent political and cultural development of Western and Eastern European civilizations.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','battle-of-hastings',73,'{"id": "battle-of-hastings", "name": "Battle of Hastings", "year": 1066, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Norman conquest England", "William the Conqueror", "Harold defeated", "Norman invasion"], "description": "William, Duke of Normandy, defeats King Harold II at the Battle of Hastings and becomes King of England, initiating the Norman Conquest. This transformative event reshapes English language, culture, and governance through the fusion of Norman French and Anglo-Saxon traditions.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','university-of-bologna-founded',74,'{"id": "university-of-bologna-founded", "name": "University of Bologna Founded", "year": 1088, "categories": ["Culture", "Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["first university", "Bologna university", "European university origins", "medieval education", "Irnerius law school", "oldest university"], "description": "The University of Bologna is established in Italy, becoming the oldest continuously operating university in the Western world, initially focused on the systematic study of Roman law. It attracts students from across Europe seeking formal legal training and establishes the model of a secular institution dedicated to higher learning with recognized degrees and faculties. The university movement rapidly spreads, with Oxford, Paris, Cambridge, and dozens of other institutions founded over the following two centuries, fundamentally reshaping European intellectual life.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','first-crusade',75,'{"id": "first-crusade", "name": "First Crusade Launched", "year": 1096, "categories": ["War", "Religion"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Pope Urban II crusade", "crusaders Jerusalem", "Holy Land conquest", "People''s Crusade"], "description": "Pope Urban II calls for a Christian military campaign to recapture Jerusalem from Muslim rule, launching the First Crusade. Armies of knights and peasants march across Europe and the Middle East, culminating in the brutal conquest of Jerusalem, and initiating two centuries of crusading warfare.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','invention-of-compass',76,'{"id": "invention-of-compass", "name": "Magnetic Compass Developed in China", "year": 1100, "categories": ["Technology", "Science", "Exploration"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Chinese compass", "navigation compass", "Song dynasty compass", "magnetic navigation"], "description": "Chinese navigators begin using magnetic compasses for maritime navigation during the Song dynasty, revolutionizing sea travel by enabling reliable orientation regardless of weather or visibility. The compass spreads to the Islamic world and Europe within centuries, enabling the Age of Exploration.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','genghis-khan-unifies-mongols',77,'{"id": "genghis-khan-unifies-mongols", "name": "Genghis Khan Unifies the Mongols", "year": 1206, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Temujin", "Mongol unification", "Great Khan", "steppe empire"], "description": "Temujin is proclaimed Genghis Khan (''Universal Ruler'') at a great assembly of Mongol chieftains after uniting the warring steppe tribes under his command. He goes on to launch the conquests that create the largest contiguous land empire in history, though at the cost of catastrophic destruction across Eurasia.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','magna-carta',78,'{"id": "magna-carta", "name": "Magna Carta Signed", "year": 1215, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["King John Magna Carta", "Great Charter", "English barons rights", "rule of law origin"], "description": "English King John is forced by rebellious barons to seal the Magna Carta at Runnymede, establishing for the first time that the king was subject to the rule of law. The document becomes a cornerstone of constitutional governance and influences legal systems around the world.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','marco-polo-china',79,'{"id": "marco-polo-china", "name": "Marco Polo Travels to China", "year": 1271, "categories": ["Exploration", "Culture"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Polo Kublai Khan", "Venice merchant China", "Silk Road traveler", "Travels of Marco Polo"], "description": "Marco Polo departs Venice on a journey that takes him to the court of Kublai Khan in China, where he spends seventeen years observing Mongol and Chinese civilization. His memoir inspires generations of European explorers, including Christopher Columbus, and sparks European fascination with the riches of Asia.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','mongol-empire-peak',80,'{"id": "mongol-empire-peak", "name": "Mongol Empire Reaches Greatest Extent", "year": 1279, "categories": ["Politics", "War", "Exploration"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Kublai Khan empire", "Genghis Khan legacy", "largest land empire", "Pax Mongolica"], "description": "Under Kublai Khan, the Mongol Empire reaches its greatest territorial extent, becoming the largest contiguous land empire in history spanning from the Pacific Ocean to Eastern Europe. The Pax Mongolica facilitates unprecedented trade and cultural exchange across Eurasia along the Silk Road.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','battle-of-bannockburn',81,'{"id": "battle-of-bannockburn", "name": "Battle of Bannockburn", "year": 1314, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Robert the Bruce", "Scottish independence", "England vs Scotland", "Stirling Castle 1314", "Scottish victory", "First War of Scottish Independence"], "description": "Scottish forces under King Robert the Bruce decisively defeat the much larger English army of Edward II near Stirling Castle, securing Scottish independence from English domination. The battle is the high point of the First War of Scottish Independence and remains the defining moment of Scottish national identity, still commemorated today. Although the formal recognition of Scottish independence required the Treaty of Edinburgh-Northampton in 1328, Bannockburn effectively ends England''s attempt to absorb Scotland.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','black-death-arrives-china',82,'{"id": "black-death-arrives-china", "name": "Black Death Spreads from Central Asia", "year": 1331, "categories": ["Disasters", "Social"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["plague China Mongol", "bubonic plague origin", "pandemic spreads east west", "Mongol plague"], "description": "Bubonic plague devastates parts of China and Central Asia under Mongol rule before spreading westward along trade routes. The disease, carried by fleas on rats, ultimately reaches Europe via Crimea and kills an estimated 75-200 million people across Eurasia.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','vijayanagara-empire-founded',83,'{"id": "vijayanagara-empire-founded", "name": "Vijayanagara Empire Founded", "year": 1336, "categories": ["Politics", "Culture"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Hampi kingdom", "Harihara Bukka", "Deccan empire", "Karnataka empire"], "description": "Harihara I and Bukka Raya I establish the Vijayanagara Empire in the Deccan, which becomes a major Hindu kingdom resisting the Sultanates of the north. The empire''s capital at Hampi grows into one of the largest cities in the world during its peak.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','hundred-years-war',84,'{"id": "hundred-years-war", "name": "Hundred Years War", "year": 1337, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["England France war", "Joan of Arc", "Agincourt", "Crécy battle"], "description": "England and France enter a prolonged series of conflicts over the French throne lasting over a century, featuring legendary battles at Crécy and Agincourt and the emergence of Joan of Arc. The war forges distinct French and English national identities and ends with England''s expulsion from France.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','black-death-europe',85,'{"id": "black-death-europe", "name": "Black Death Strikes Europe", "year": 1347, "categories": ["Disasters", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["bubonic plague Europe", "Great Plague", "Black Plague", "medieval pandemic"], "description": "The bubonic plague arrives in Sicily from Crimea and rapidly spreads across Europe, killing an estimated one-third to one-half of the European population within a few years. The catastrophic loss reshapes European society by disrupting feudal systems, labor markets, and the Church''s authority.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','ming-dynasty-founded',86,'{"id": "ming-dynasty-founded", "name": "Ming Dynasty Founded in China", "year": 1368, "categories": ["Politics", "Culture"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Zhu Yuanzhang", "Hongwu Emperor", "Mongol expulsion China", "Nanjing capital"], "description": "Zhu Yuanzhang expels the Mongol Yuan dynasty and establishes the Ming dynasty, restoring Han Chinese rule to China. The Ming period sees the rebuilding of the Great Wall, the construction of the Forbidden City, and the remarkable maritime expeditions of Zheng He across Asia and Africa.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','timur-sacks-delhi',87,'{"id": "timur-sacks-delhi", "name": "Timur Sacks Delhi", "year": 1398, "categories": ["War"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Tamerlane Delhi", "Timur Lang invasion", "Delhi sultanate destroyed", "Timurid invasion India", "1398 India", "Tamerlane conquests"], "description": "Timur, the Central Asian conqueror known in the West as Tamerlane, leads his army into the Indian subcontinent and sacks Delhi, massacring much of its population and stripping the city of its accumulated wealth. The Delhi Sultanate never fully recovers from the blow, plunging northern India into a century of fragmentation and instability. Timur''s campaign represents one of the most destructive military incursions in Indian history and reshapes the subcontinent''s political landscape, indirectly creating the conditions for the later Mughal conquest.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','renaissance-begins-florence',88,'{"id": "renaissance-begins-florence", "name": "Renaissance Begins in Florence", "year": 1401, "categories": ["Arts", "Culture", "Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Italian Renaissance", "Florence art", "Medici patronage", "rebirth classical learning"], "description": "A cultural and intellectual movement centered in Florence begins reviving interest in classical Greek and Roman art, philosophy, and science, with patronage from wealthy families like the Medici. The Renaissance produces extraordinary achievements in painting, sculpture, architecture, and literature that fundamentally reshape Western culture.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','zheng-he-voyages',89,'{"id": "zheng-he-voyages", "name": "Zheng He''s Great Maritime Voyages", "year": 1405, "categories": ["Exploration", "Politics"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Treasure Fleet China", "Zheng He admiral", "Ming maritime expeditions", "Chinese exploration"], "description": "Chinese admiral Zheng He leads the first of seven massive naval expeditions visiting Southeast Asia, India, the Persian Gulf, and the East African coast with a fleet dwarfing contemporary European ships. The voyages showcase Ming China''s power and facilitate diplomatic and trade relations across the Indian Ocean world.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','age-of-exploration-portugal',90,'{"id": "age-of-exploration-portugal", "name": "Portugal Opens African Coastal Trade", "year": 1415, "categories": ["Exploration", "Politics"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Prince Henry Navigator", "Portuguese exploration Africa", "Ceuta conquest", "maritime exploration begins"], "description": "Portugal''s conquest of Ceuta and Prince Henry the Navigator''s systematic sponsorship of African coastal exploration launches the European Age of Exploration. Portuguese navigators gradually map the West African coast, establishing trade posts and introducing European maritime expansion that will reshape global history.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','joan-of-arc-burned',91,'{"id": "joan-of-arc-burned", "name": "Joan of Arc Executed", "year": 1431, "categories": ["War", "Religion", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Maid of Orleans execution", "Joan burned at stake", "French heroine death", "Rouen execution"], "description": "Joan of Arc, the teenage peasant girl who led French armies to pivotal victories claiming divine guidance, is burned at the stake by English-allied Burgundians after being convicted of heresy. Posthumously rehabilitated and eventually canonized, she becomes France''s patron saint and a symbol of national resistance.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','gutenberg-printing-press',92,'{"id": "gutenberg-printing-press", "name": "Gutenberg Invents Printing Press", "year": 1440, "categories": ["Technology", "Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["movable type printing", "Johannes Gutenberg", "Gutenberg Bible", "printing revolution"], "description": "Johannes Gutenberg develops the movable-type printing press in Mainz, Germany, enabling the mass production of books for the first time in Europe. The invention revolutionizes the spread of knowledge, fuels the Renaissance and Reformation, and is considered one of the most transformative technologies in history.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','aztec-empire-peak',93,'{"id": "aztec-empire-peak", "name": "Aztec Empire Reaches Its Peak", "year": 1440, "categories": ["Politics", "Culture"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Tenochtitlan", "Mexica empire", "Moctezuma", "triple alliance Aztec"], "description": "Under Moctezuma I, the Aztec Triple Alliance expands rapidly to control much of Mesoamerica, extracting tribute from hundreds of subject peoples. Tenochtitlan, built on an island in Lake Texcoco, becomes one of the largest cities in the world with a population rivaling contemporary European capitals.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','fall-of-constantinople',94,'{"id": "fall-of-constantinople", "name": "Fall of Constantinople", "year": 1453, "categories": ["War", "Politics", "Religion"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Ottoman conquest Constantinople", "Mehmed II", "Byzantine Empire ends", "Istanbul"], "description": "Ottoman Sultan Mehmed II captures Constantinople after a two-month siege, ending the Byzantine Empire and marking the fall of the last vestige of the Roman Empire. The conquest transforms the city into Istanbul, the new Ottoman capital, and is often cited as the end of the Middle Ages.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','guru-nanak-born',95,'{"id": "guru-nanak-born", "name": "Guru Nanak Born", "year": 1469, "categories": ["Religion"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["founder of Sikhism", "Nanak Dev Ji", "Sikh religion founded"], "description": "Guru Nanak, the founder of Sikhism, is born in the Punjab region. His teachings emphasizing equality, monotheism, and service to humanity attract followers from both Hindu and Muslim communities and give rise to a new religious tradition.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','renaissance-da-vinci',96,'{"id": "renaissance-da-vinci", "name": "Leonardo da Vinci Active", "year": 1490, "categories": ["Arts", "Science", "Technology"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["da Vinci genius", "Vitruvian Man", "flying machines Leonardo", "Renaissance man"], "description": "Leonardo da Vinci produces his most celebrated works and notebooks during this period, combining mastery of painting with scientific investigation of anatomy, engineering, and natural phenomena. His breadth of genius — from the Last Supper to designs for flying machines — epitomizes the Renaissance ideal of the universal man.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','columbus-reaches-americas',97,'{"id": "columbus-reaches-americas", "name": "Columbus Reaches the Americas", "year": 1492, "categories": ["Exploration", "Politics"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Columbus 1492", "New World discovery", "Caribbean landing", "Columbian exchange begins"], "description": "Christopher Columbus, sailing under Spanish patronage, lands in the Bahamas, initiating sustained contact between Europe and the Americas. His voyages begin the Columbian Exchange, a massive transfer of plants, animals, diseases, and cultures that permanently transforms both hemispheres.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','vasco-da-gama-india-route',98,'{"id": "vasco-da-gama-india-route", "name": "Vasco da Gama Opens Sea Route to India", "year": 1498, "categories": ["Exploration", "Technology"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Portuguese India route", "Cape of Good Hope", "spice trade route", "Calicut landing"], "description": "Portuguese explorer Vasco da Gama completes the first direct sea voyage from Europe to India by sailing around Africa, arriving at Calicut on the Kerala coast. The discovery of this sea route breaks the Arab monopoly on Asian trade and inaugurates the Portuguese Maritime Empire.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','renaissance-michelangelo',99,'{"id": "renaissance-michelangelo", "name": "Michelangelo Paints the Sistine Chapel", "year": 1508, "categories": ["Arts", "Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Sistine Chapel ceiling", "Michelangelo Rome", "Vatican art", "Renaissance masterpiece"], "description": "Michelangelo spends four years painting the iconic ceiling of the Sistine Chapel in the Vatican, depicting scenes from Genesis in an unprecedented display of artistic mastery and physical endurance. The work, including the famous ''Creation of Adam,'' stands as one of the supreme achievements of Western art.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','protestant-reformation',100,'{"id": "protestant-reformation", "name": "Protestant Reformation Begins", "year": 1517, "categories": ["Religion", "Politics", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Martin Luther 95 theses", "Luther Wittenberg", "Church reform", "Lutheranism"], "description": "Martin Luther posts his Ninety-Five Theses on the door of a church in Wittenberg, challenging corrupt practices in the Catholic Church and igniting the Protestant Reformation. The movement permanently fractures Western Christianity, sparks religious wars, and reshapes European culture and politics.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','magellan-circumnavigation',101,'{"id": "magellan-circumnavigation", "name": "First Circumnavigation of the Globe", "year": 1519, "categories": ["Exploration", "Science"], "region": "Global", "aliases": ["Magellan circumnavigation", "Ferdinand Magellan", "round the world voyage", "Sebastian Elcano"], "description": "Ferdinand Magellan leads an expedition that becomes the first to circumnavigate the globe, though Magellan himself is killed in the Philippines. The voyage, completed by Sebastian Elcano, definitively proves the spherical nature of Earth and vastly expands European geographic knowledge.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','spanish-conquest-mexico',102,'{"id": "spanish-conquest-mexico", "name": "Spanish Conquest of the Aztec Empire", "year": 1519, "categories": ["War", "Exploration", "Politics"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Cortes conquers Aztecs", "Hernán Cortés", "fall of Tenochtitlan", "Moctezuma captured"], "description": "Hernán Cortés leads a Spanish expedition that, with the aid of indigenous allies and devastating diseases, overthrows the Aztec Empire and its emperor Moctezuma within two years. The conquest of Mexico opens the way for Spanish colonization of the Americas and the destruction of Mesoamerican civilizations.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','first-battle-of-panipat',103,'{"id": "first-battle-of-panipat", "name": "First Battle of Panipat", "year": 1526, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Babur defeats Ibrahim Lodi", "Mughal invasion", "Panipat 1526"], "description": "Babur defeats Ibrahim Lodi of the Delhi Sultanate at Panipat, using artillery to decisive effect for the first time in Indian warfare. This battle marks the end of the Delhi Sultanate and the beginning of Mughal rule over the Indian subcontinent.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','babur-founds-mughal-empire',104,'{"id": "babur-founds-mughal-empire", "name": "Babur Founds the Mughal Empire", "year": 1526, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Mughal dynasty begins", "Baburnama", "Timurid India"], "description": "Following his victory at Panipat, Babur establishes the Mughal Empire, which will eventually become one of the most powerful and culturally rich empires in Indian history. Babur is also remembered as a poet and memoirist through his autobiography, the Baburnama.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','conquest-of-peru-inca',105,'{"id": "conquest-of-peru-inca", "name": "Spanish Conquest of the Inca Empire", "year": 1532, "categories": ["War", "Exploration", "Politics"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Pizarro conquers Inca", "Francisco Pizarro", "Atahualpa captured", "fall of Cusco"], "description": "Francisco Pizarro and a small band of Spanish conquistadors capture and eventually execute the Inca emperor Atahualpa, initiating the conquest of the Inca Empire in South America. Disease and internal divisions help the Spanish rapidly dismantle one of history''s largest and most sophisticated empires.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','humayun-defeated-kanauj',106,'{"id": "humayun-defeated-kanauj", "name": "Humayun Defeated at Kanauj", "year": 1540, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Sher Shah Suri", "Battle of Kanauj", "Mughal exile", "Afghan victory India"], "description": "The Afghan chieftain Sher Shah Suri defeats Mughal emperor Humayun at the Battle of Kanauj, forcing him into a fifteen-year exile. Sher Shah''s brief reign introduces administrative and revenue reforms that would later be adopted and expanded by Akbar.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','copernicus-heliocentric',107,'{"id": "copernicus-heliocentric", "name": "Copernicus Publishes Heliocentric Theory", "year": 1543, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["De revolutionibus", "Copernican revolution", "Sun center solar system", "heliocentric model"], "description": "Nicolaus Copernicus publishes his theory that Earth and other planets orbit the Sun, directly challenging the prevailing geocentric model supported by the Church. The Copernican Revolution triggers a fundamental shift in scientific thinking and sets the stage for the broader Scientific Revolution.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','portuguese-arrive-japan',108,'{"id": "portuguese-arrive-japan", "name": "Portuguese Arrive in Japan", "year": 1543, "categories": ["Exploration", "Culture", "Technology"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Europeans Japan first contact", "guns Japan introduction", "Tanegashima firearms", "Nanban trade"], "description": "Portuguese traders shipwrecked on the island of Tanegashima introduce firearms to Japan, transforming Japanese warfare and accelerating political change. The arrival begins a period of contact that brings Christianity, new technologies, and trade goods to Japan while exposing it to European influence.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','second-battle-of-panipat',109,'{"id": "second-battle-of-panipat", "name": "Second Battle of Panipat", "year": 1556, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Akbar vs Hemu", "Bairam Khan", "Panipat 1556"], "description": "The young Mughal emperor Akbar, guided by regent Bairam Khan, defeats the Hindu general Hemu at Panipat, consolidating Mughal control over northern India. This battle ensures the survival of the Mughal Empire after the tumultuous reign of Humayun.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','shakespeare-born',110,'{"id": "shakespeare-born", "name": "William Shakespeare Born", "year": 1564, "categories": ["Arts", "Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Shakespeare", "Bard of Avon", "English playwright", "Stratford-upon-Avon", "Hamlet author", "Globe Theatre", "greatest writer English"], "description": "William Shakespeare is born in Stratford-upon-Avon, England, in the same year that Michelangelo dies, as if the torch of Renaissance genius passes between them. Over his career he writes 37 plays and 154 sonnets that explore the full range of human experience — ambition, jealousy, love, power, and mortality — with unprecedented psychological depth and linguistic brilliance. His works, from Hamlet and King Lear to A Midsummer Night''s Dream and The Tempest, remain the most performed and studied literary works in history.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','mughal-akbar-administration',111,'{"id": "mughal-akbar-administration", "name": "Akbar Establishes Mansabdari System", "year": 1571, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Akbar administration", "Mughal governance", "mansab rank system", "Fatehpur Sikri"], "description": "Emperor Akbar introduces the Mansabdari system, a unified administrative and military ranking structure that integrates Mughal and Rajput nobles into a single imperial hierarchy. This administrative innovation provides the organizational backbone of the Mughal Empire at its height.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','battle-of-haldighati',112,'{"id": "battle-of-haldighati", "name": "Battle of Haldighati", "year": 1576, "categories": ["War"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Maharana Pratap", "Akbar vs Mewar", "Rajput resistance"], "description": "Maharana Pratap of Mewar battles the Mughal forces led by Man Singh at Haldighati in a fierce but inconclusive engagement. Though Pratap''s forces are outnumbered and he retreats, he becomes a symbol of Rajput resistance to Mughal dominance.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','akbar-din-i-ilahi',113,'{"id": "akbar-din-i-ilahi", "name": "Akbar Proclaims Din-i-Ilahi", "year": 1582, "categories": ["Religion", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Akbar''s religion", "divine faith", "Mughal religious policy", "Sulh-i-kul"], "description": "Emperor Akbar establishes Din-i-Ilahi, a syncretic religious movement blending elements of Islam, Hinduism, Zoroastrianism, and other faiths. Though it attracts few followers, it exemplifies Akbar''s policy of religious tolerance and his attempt to unify his diverse empire.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','spanish-armada-defeated',114,'{"id": "spanish-armada-defeated", "name": "Spanish Armada Defeated", "year": 1588, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["England defeats Spain", "Drake Armada", "Protestant victory", "naval battle English Channel"], "description": "The English fleet and stormy weather destroy the Spanish Armada sent by King Philip II to invade England, marking a turning point in European naval dominance. The defeat weakens Spanish imperial power and accelerates England''s rise as a major maritime and colonial power.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','renaissance-shakespeare',115,'{"id": "renaissance-shakespeare", "name": "Shakespeare Writes His Greatest Works", "year": 1600, "categories": ["Arts", "Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Hamlet Macbeth Othello", "Globe Theatre", "Elizabethan drama", "English literature peak"], "description": "William Shakespeare writes his greatest tragedies including Hamlet, Othello, King Lear, and Macbeth during the height of his creative powers. His works explore the full range of human experience with unparalleled psychological depth and linguistic richness, shaping the English language and world literature.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','east-india-company-founded',116,'{"id": "east-india-company-founded", "name": "East India Company Founded", "year": 1600, "categories": ["Politics", "Exploration"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["British East India Company", "EIC", "John Company", "English East India Company", "1600 charter", "colonial trade company", "Company Raj"], "description": "Queen Elizabeth I grants a royal charter to the East India Company, giving it a monopoly on English trade with the East Indies and the power to wage war and make treaties. Initially focused on spices and textiles, the company gradually transforms into a political and military power, eventually governing large swaths of South Asia directly on behalf of the British Crown. The East India Company becomes the world''s most powerful private enterprise and the primary instrument of British colonialism in Asia, ruling India for over 250 years.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','death-of-elizabeth-i',117,'{"id": "death-of-elizabeth-i", "name": "Death of Elizabeth I", "year": 1603, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Elizabeth I dies", "end of Tudor dynasty", "Elizabethan era ends", "James I becomes king", "Tudor England ends", "Virgin Queen death"], "description": "Queen Elizabeth I of England dies at Richmond Palace after a reign of nearly 45 years, ending the Tudor dynasty that had shaped England since 1485. Her reign, celebrated as the Elizabethan era, saw England emerge as a major European power, the flourishing of literature and theatre under Shakespeare and Marlowe, and the beginnings of English overseas expansion. She is succeeded by James VI of Scotland, who unites the English and Scottish crowns as James I, beginning the Stuart era and moving England toward the constitutional conflicts of the following century.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','galileo-telescope',118,'{"id": "galileo-telescope", "name": "Galileo Turns Telescope to the Heavens", "year": 1609, "categories": ["Science", "Technology"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Galileo discoveries", "Jupiter moons", "Galileo Galilei", "astronomical revolution"], "description": "Galileo Galilei uses an improved telescope to make detailed astronomical observations including the moons of Jupiter and the phases of Venus, providing powerful evidence for the Copernican heliocentric model. His findings bring him into conflict with the Catholic Church but fundamentally advance astronomy.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','thirty-years-war',119,'{"id": "thirty-years-war", "name": "Thirty Years War Begins", "year": 1618, "categories": ["War", "Religion", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["European religious war", "Westphalia", "Habsburg conflict", "German war"], "description": "A conflict beginning with a Protestant rebellion in Bohemia draws most of Europe''s major powers into a devastating war fought primarily on German soil. The war, ending with the Peace of Westphalia in 1648, reshapes the European political order, establishes state sovereignty, and kills millions.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','pilgrims-land-plymouth',120,'{"id": "pilgrims-land-plymouth", "name": "Pilgrims Land at Plymouth", "year": 1620, "categories": ["Exploration", "Politics"], "region": "North America", "aliases": ["Mayflower", "Plymouth Colony", "Pilgrim Fathers", "Mayflower Compact", "1620 America", "Puritan settlers New England"], "description": "The Mayflower arrives at Plymouth, Massachusetts, carrying 102 passengers — mostly English Separatists seeking religious freedom from the Church of England — after a grueling ten-week voyage. Before landing, the male passengers sign the Mayflower Compact, one of the first governing documents in the New World establishing self-rule by consent of the governed. The Plymouth Colony becomes a founding symbol of American identity, democratic values, and the tradition of seeking religious freedom that draws millions of immigrants to North America.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','taj-mahal-construction-begins',121,'{"id": "taj-mahal-construction-begins", "name": "Construction of the Taj Mahal Begins", "year": 1632, "categories": ["Arts", "Culture"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Shah Jahan mausoleum", "Mumtaz Mahal", "Agra monument", "wonder of the world"], "description": "Emperor Shah Jahan commissions the Taj Mahal in Agra as a mausoleum for his beloved wife Mumtaz Mahal, who died in childbirth. The monument, completed roughly twenty years later, is considered one of the finest examples of Mughal architecture and a UNESCO World Heritage Site.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','galileo-inquisition',122,'{"id": "galileo-inquisition", "name": "Galileo Faces the Inquisition", "year": 1633, "categories": ["Science", "Religion"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Galileo trial", "heliocentric condemned", "Church science conflict", "and yet it moves"], "description": "The Roman Inquisition puts Galileo Galilei on trial for supporting the Copernican heliocentric theory in his Dialogue, forcing him to recant under threat of torture. His trial becomes the defining symbol of the conflict between religious authority and scientific inquiry.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','english-civil-war',123,'{"id": "english-civil-war", "name": "English Civil War", "year": 1642, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Cromwell Parliament", "Royalists Roundheads", "Charles I war", "Parliamentarians"], "description": "Conflict between King Charles I and Parliament erupts into civil war, with Oliver Cromwell''s New Model Army defeating royalist forces. The war leads to the execution of Charles I, the short-lived Commonwealth republic, and ultimately establishes the principle of parliamentary sovereignty in England.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','signing-of-treaty-westphalia',124,'{"id": "signing-of-treaty-westphalia", "name": "Peace of Westphalia Signed", "year": 1648, "categories": ["Politics", "Religion"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Westphalia treaty", "Thirty Years War ends", "state sovereignty established", "modern international law"], "description": "The Peace of Westphalia ends the Thirty Years War and the Eighty Years War, establishing the principle of state sovereignty and non-interference in other states'' internal affairs. The settlement is often considered the foundation of the modern international system of nation-states.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','execution-of-charles-i',125,'{"id": "execution-of-charles-i", "name": "Execution of Charles I", "year": 1649, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Charles I beheaded", "English regicide", "English Commonwealth", "Oliver Cromwell", "end of English monarchy temporarily", "Parliamentary victory Civil War"], "description": "King Charles I of England is tried for treason by a specially convened Parliamentary court and executed by beheading outside the Banqueting House in London. This unprecedented act — the public trial and execution of a reigning monarch by his own subjects — sends shockwaves across Europe and fundamentally alters the relationship between the Crown and Parliament. England briefly becomes a Commonwealth republic under Oliver Cromwell before the monarchy is restored in 1660, but the episode permanently establishes the principle that the king is not above the law.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','hobbes-leviathan',126,'{"id": "hobbes-leviathan", "name": "Hobbes Publishes Leviathan", "year": 1651, "categories": ["Culture", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Leviathan book", "Thomas Hobbes", "social contract theory", "state of nature", "political philosophy", "natural rights philosophy", "Hobbes philosophy"], "description": "Thomas Hobbes publishes Leviathan, arguing that without government human life would be ''solitary, poor, nasty, brutish, and short,'' and that people rationally surrender some freedoms to a sovereign authority in exchange for security and order. The work establishes the social contract as a foundational concept of modern political philosophy, providing a secular rather than divine basis for political authority. Hobbes''s framework, developed and challenged by Locke and Rousseau, shapes all subsequent thinking about the relationship between individuals, society, and the state.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','english-restoration',127,'{"id": "english-restoration", "name": "English Monarchy Restored", "year": 1660, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Restoration", "Charles II", "end of Commonwealth", "Cromwell era ends", "monarchy restored England", "1660 England", "Restoration era"], "description": "Charles II enters London in triumph, restoring the monarchy after eleven years of Puritan Commonwealth rule following his father''s execution. The Restoration brings a cultural renaissance in England — theaters reopen, the arts flourish, and the court becomes a center of wit and libertinism after the austerity of Cromwellian rule. The period also sees the founding of the Royal Society, cementing England''s place at the forefront of the Scientific Revolution.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','great-plague-london',128,'{"id": "great-plague-london", "name": "Great Plague of London", "year": 1665, "categories": ["Culture", "Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["London plague 1665", "bubonic plague England", "Black Death return England", "plague pits London", "Bills of Mortality", "last great plague England"], "description": "The last major outbreak of bubonic plague in England strikes London, killing an estimated 100,000 people — roughly a quarter of the city''s population — in less than eighteen months. The epidemic forces King Charles II and his court to flee the capital, disrupting trade and governance. The Great Fire of London the following year inadvertently helps end the epidemic by destroying much of the overcrowded, rat-infested housing in which the disease spread most readily.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','great-fire-london',129,'{"id": "great-fire-london", "name": "Great Fire of London", "year": 1666, "categories": ["Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["London fire 1666", "Pudding Lane fire", "St Paul''s Cathedral destroyed", "Christopher Wren rebuilds London", "London rebuilt", "1666 fire city"], "description": "A fire starting in a bakery on Pudding Lane sweeps through the medieval City of London for three days, destroying over 13,000 houses, 87 churches including the old St Paul''s Cathedral, and the city''s commercial heart. Despite the enormous destruction, few deaths are confirmed, and the fire inadvertently helps end the bubonic plague ravaging the city by destroying rat-infested slums. Architect Christopher Wren leads the rebuilding effort, creating the iconic new St Paul''s Cathedral and transforming London into a more modern, fire-resistant city.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','shivaji-crowned-chhatrapati',130,'{"id": "shivaji-crowned-chhatrapati", "name": "Shivaji Crowned as Chhatrapati", "year": 1674, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Maratha Empire", "Shivaji Maharaj", "Raigad coronation", "Maratha Confederacy"], "description": "Shivaji Bhonsale is crowned Chhatrapati at Raigad Fort, formally establishing the Maratha Kingdom as an independent sovereign state. His guerrilla warfare tactics and administrative innovations created a powerful Hindu empire that would eventually challenge Mughal dominance.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','newton-laws-of-motion',131,'{"id": "newton-laws-of-motion", "name": "Newton Publishes Laws of Motion", "year": 1687, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Principia Mathematica", "Isaac Newton", "gravity law", "classical mechanics"], "description": "Isaac Newton publishes Principia Mathematica, laying out his three laws of motion and universal law of gravitation, unifying terrestrial and celestial mechanics. This monumental work forms the foundation of classical physics and remains one of the most influential scientific texts ever written.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','glorious-revolution',132,'{"id": "glorious-revolution", "name": "Glorious Revolution in England", "year": 1688, "categories": ["Politics", "Religion"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["William of Orange", "James II deposed", "English constitutional monarchy", "Bill of Rights 1689"], "description": "King James II of England is overthrown and replaced by William of Orange in a largely bloodless coup that establishes constitutional monarchy and parliamentary supremacy. The subsequent Bill of Rights limits royal power and guarantees parliamentary privileges, shaping the British democratic tradition.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','mughal-empire-zenith-aurangzeb',133,'{"id": "mughal-empire-zenith-aurangzeb", "name": "Mughal Empire Reaches Maximum Extent", "year": 1707, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Aurangzeb Mughal", "Mughal peak territory", "Deccan campaigns", "Mughal decline begins"], "description": "Emperor Aurangzeb''s death marks both the maximum territorial extent of the Mughal Empire and the beginning of its rapid decline. His costly Deccan campaigns, religious intolerance, and the power of regional rulers exhaust the empire''s resources and trigger the fragmentation that allows the British East India Company to expand.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','act-of-union-1707',134,'{"id": "act-of-union-1707", "name": "Act of Union Creates Great Britain", "year": 1707, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Union of England and Scotland", "Kingdom of Great Britain", "Scottish Parliament dissolved", "British union 1707", "Treaty of Union", "United Kingdom origins"], "description": "The Acts of Union unite the kingdoms of England and Scotland into a single Kingdom of Great Britain with one Parliament sitting at Westminster, ending over seven centuries of separate Scottish statehood. The union, controversial in Scotland and achieved partly through political pressure and financial incentives, creates the political entity that will dominate global trade, science, and empire over the following two centuries. Great Britain''s combined resources and political stability underpin the Industrial Revolution and the expansion of a British Empire that at its height covers a quarter of the world''s land surface.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','euler-konigsberg-bridges',135,'{"id": "euler-konigsberg-bridges", "name": "Euler Solves the Königsberg Bridge Problem", "year": 1735, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Königsberg bridges", "Euler graph theory", "seven bridges problem", "graph theory founded", "topology origins", "Leonhard Euler mathematics"], "description": "The Swiss mathematician Leonhard Euler proves that it is impossible to walk through the city of Königsberg crossing each of its seven bridges exactly once, in the process founding the mathematical field of graph theory. By abstracting the city''s geography into nodes and edges, Euler creates a new framework for analyzing connectivity and networks that has no precedent. The paper is considered the first work in graph theory and topology and becomes foundational to modern network analysis, computer science, logistics, and the study of social networks.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','trans-atlantic-slave-trade-peak',136,'{"id": "trans-atlantic-slave-trade-peak", "name": "Peak of the Transatlantic Slave Trade", "year": 1750, "categories": ["Social", "Culture"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Middle Passage", "African slavery Americas", "slave ships", "triangular trade"], "description": "The transatlantic slave trade reaches its peak volume in the mid-eighteenth century, with over 80,000 Africans forcibly transported to the Americas annually. The trade, which forcibly displaced an estimated 12 million Africans across three centuries, represents one of history''s greatest human catastrophes and shapes the demographic and cultural landscape of the Americas.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','battle-of-plassey',137,'{"id": "battle-of-plassey", "name": "Battle of Plassey", "year": 1757, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Clive of India", "Robert Clive", "Siraj ud-Daulah", "British India begins", "East India Company victory"], "description": "Robert Clive of the British East India Company defeats the Nawab of Bengal, Siraj ud-Daulah, at Plassey through a combination of military force and strategic treachery. This decisive battle marks the beginning of British political control over India.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','industrial-revolution-textile',138,'{"id": "industrial-revolution-textile", "name": "Industrial Revolution Transforms Britain", "year": 1760, "categories": ["Technology", "Social", "Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["factory system Britain", "textile mills", "spinning jenny", "coal and iron", "urbanization"], "description": "Britain leads a transformation from manual craft production to machine-based manufacturing in factories, dramatically increasing industrial output and triggering mass urbanization. The Industrial Revolution creates new social classes, alters working conditions, and sets the template for modern economic development worldwide.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','east-india-company-bengal',139,'{"id": "east-india-company-bengal", "name": "East India Company Assumes Control of Bengal", "year": 1765, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Diwani rights", "British Bengal", "Company Raj", "Treaty of Allahabad"], "description": "The British East India Company receives the Diwani rights — the right to collect revenue from Bengal, Bihar, and Orissa — through the Treaty of Allahabad. This marks a decisive shift from a trading company to a governing power controlling vast territories.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','steam-engine-watt',140,'{"id": "steam-engine-watt", "name": "James Watt Improves the Steam Engine", "year": 1769, "categories": ["Technology", "Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Industrial Revolution begins", "Watt engine", "coal power", "mechanical revolution"], "description": "James Watt develops a dramatically improved steam engine with a separate condenser, greatly increasing its efficiency and making it practical for widespread industrial use. His invention becomes the driving force of the Industrial Revolution, powering factories, mines, locomotives, and ships.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','boston-tea-party',141,'{"id": "boston-tea-party", "name": "Boston Tea Party", "year": 1773, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Sons of Liberty tea", "colonial protest Britain", "no taxation representation", "American rebellion"], "description": "American colonists disguised as Mohawk warriors dump 342 chests of British East India Company tea into Boston Harbor in protest of taxation without representation. The dramatic act of defiance galvanizes colonial opposition to British rule and pushes events toward the American Revolution.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','opium-trade-china-east-india',142,'{"id": "opium-trade-china-east-india", "name": "British East India Company Begins Opium Trade", "year": 1773, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Bengal opium China", "British opium trade", "drug trade imperialism", "China opium import"], "description": "The British East India Company establishes a monopoly on opium production in Bengal and begins exporting it to China, creating a highly profitable trade that generates millions of addicts. The resulting trade imbalance and Chinese attempts to suppress the trade lead to the Opium Wars.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','american-revolution',143,'{"id": "american-revolution", "name": "American Revolution", "year": 1776, "categories": ["Politics", "War", "Social"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["American independence", "US Declaration of Independence", "13 colonies revolt", "Revolutionary War"], "description": "The thirteen American colonies declare independence from British rule and fight a revolutionary war, producing the Declaration of Independence and a new republican government. The revolution establishes the United States and becomes a model for democratic revolutions worldwide.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','american-declaration',144,'{"id": "american-declaration", "name": "Declaration of Independence Signed", "year": 1776, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["US independence", "Thomas Jefferson", "Fourth of July", "Philadelphia 1776"], "description": "The Continental Congress adopts the Declaration of Independence, drafted primarily by Thomas Jefferson, proclaiming the thirteen colonies'' separation from Britain and articulating the Enlightenment principles of natural rights and government by consent. The document becomes one of history''s most influential political texts.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','wealth-of-nations-published',145,'{"id": "wealth-of-nations-published", "name": "Adam Smith Publishes The Wealth of Nations", "year": 1776, "categories": ["Culture", "Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Wealth of Nations", "Adam Smith", "capitalism theory", "free market economics", "invisible hand", "political economy founded", "classical economics"], "description": "Scottish economist Adam Smith publishes An Inquiry into the Nature and Causes of the Wealth of Nations on the same day the American colonies declare independence, laying the foundations of modern economic theory. Smith argues that free markets, driven by individual self-interest and coordinated by the ''invisible hand'' of price signals, generate prosperity more efficiently than state direction of the economy. The book becomes the foundational text of classical economics, its ideas shaping capitalist policy from the Industrial Revolution to the present day.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 8}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','american-war-independence-ends',146,'{"id": "american-war-independence-ends", "name": "Treaty of Paris Ends American Revolution", "year": 1783, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["American independence recognized", "Britain concedes America", "Peace of Paris", "US recognized nation"], "description": "Britain signs the Treaty of Paris recognizing American independence and ceding vast territories east of the Mississippi River to the new United States. The treaty marks the successful conclusion of the American Revolution and creates the foundation for American westward expansion.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','founding-of-united-states',147,'{"id": "founding-of-united-states", "name": "United States Constitution Ratified", "year": 1788, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["US Constitution", "founding fathers", "Philadelphia convention", "federal government established"], "description": "The United States ratifies its Constitution, establishing a federal republic with separation of powers, a system of checks and balances, and protections for individual rights. The Constitution becomes one of the most influential governing documents in history, serving as a model for democratic constitutions worldwide.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','french-revolution',148,'{"id": "french-revolution", "name": "French Revolution", "year": 1789, "categories": ["Politics", "Social", "War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Bastille stormed", "Liberty Equality Fraternity", "Reign of Terror", "Louis XVI overthrown"], "description": "The French monarchy is overthrown in a sweeping revolution driven by Enlightenment ideals of liberty and equality, leading to radical political transformation, the execution of the king, and a Reign of Terror. The revolution reverberates across Europe and reshapes modern political thought around liberty, nationalism, and democracy.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','french-revolution-storming-bastille',149,'{"id": "french-revolution-storming-bastille", "name": "Storming of the Bastille", "year": 1789, "categories": ["Politics", "Social", "War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Bastille Day", "July 14 France", "French Revolution begins", "prison stormed Paris"], "description": "Parisian revolutionaries storm the Bastille prison fortress on July 14th, freeing political prisoners and seizing weapons in the opening act of the French Revolution. The storming becomes the defining symbol of the revolution and is still commemorated annually as France''s national holiday.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','french-revolution-declaration',150,'{"id": "french-revolution-declaration", "name": "Declaration of the Rights of Man", "year": 1789, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["French human rights", "Rights of Man citizen", "Enlightenment declaration", "French constitution principles"], "description": "France''s National Assembly adopts the Declaration of the Rights of Man and of the Citizen, establishing principles of individual liberty, equality before the law, and popular sovereignty. The document becomes a foundational text of modern democracy and human rights, influencing constitutions and declarations worldwide.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','haitian-revolution',151,'{"id": "haitian-revolution", "name": "Haitian Revolution", "year": 1791, "categories": ["War", "Politics", "Social"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Saint-Domingue rebellion", "Toussaint Louverture", "slave revolt Haiti", "first Black republic"], "description": "Enslaved people in the French colony of Saint-Domingue launch a massive uprising that becomes the only successful slave revolution in history, leading to the creation of Haiti as the world''s first Black republic. The revolution terrifies slaveholding nations and becomes a global symbol of Black freedom.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','abolition-slavery-france',152,'{"id": "abolition-slavery-france", "name": "France Abolishes Slavery", "year": 1794, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["French abolition", "Convention abolishes slavery", "first abolition decree", "Saint-Domingue freedom"], "description": "The French National Convention abolishes slavery in all French territories, making France the first European colonial power to do so, largely driven by the slave uprising in Saint-Domingue. The decree is later reversed by Napoleon but eventually reinstated permanently.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','first-vaccine-smallpox',153,'{"id": "first-vaccine-smallpox", "name": "Smallpox Vaccine Invented", "year": 1796, "categories": ["Medicine", "Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Edward Jenner vaccine", "cowpox vaccine", "first vaccination", "immunity against smallpox"], "description": "Edward Jenner demonstrates that inoculation with cowpox material protects against smallpox, developing the world''s first vaccine. His discovery saves hundreds of millions of lives and establishes the principle of vaccination that underlies all modern immunology.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','tipu-sultan-killed',154,'{"id": "tipu-sultan-killed", "name": "Tipu Sultan Falls at Seringapatam", "year": 1799, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Tiger of Mysore", "Fourth Anglo-Mysore War", "Seringapatam siege", "Tipu Sultan death"], "description": "Tipu Sultan, the ''Tiger of Mysore'' and one of India''s most formidable opponents of British expansion, is killed defending his capital Seringapatam. His defeat ends the Kingdom of Mysore as a significant power and opens much of southern India to British control.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','napoleonic-wars',155,'{"id": "napoleonic-wars", "name": "Napoleonic Wars Begin", "year": 1803, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Napoleon wars", "Napoleonic conquests", "Austerlitz", "Waterloo", "continental system"], "description": "Napoleon Bonaparte wages a series of military campaigns that bring most of Europe under French control and permanently reshape the continent''s political map. The wars spread revolutionary ideals across Europe, stimulate nationalism, and cause unprecedented destruction before Napoleon''s final defeat at Waterloo.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','battle-of-trafalgar',156,'{"id": "battle-of-trafalgar", "name": "Battle of Trafalgar", "year": 1805, "categories": ["War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Nelson''s victory", "Admiral Nelson dies", "Cape Trafalgar", "Napoleon''s navy defeated", "British naval supremacy", "Horatio Nelson death"], "description": "The British Royal Navy under Admiral Horatio Nelson defeats the combined French and Spanish fleets off Cape Trafalgar in southern Spain, securing British naval supremacy for over a century. Nelson is mortally wounded aboard his flagship HMS Victory at the moment of his greatest triumph, dying with the words ''Thank God I have done my duty'' and becoming one of Britain''s most celebrated national heroes. The battle ensures Napoleon can never invade Britain and establishes the maritime foundation for the British Empire''s global reach.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','abolition-slavery-britain',157,'{"id": "abolition-slavery-britain", "name": "Britain Abolishes the Slave Trade", "year": 1807, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Wilberforce abolition", "Slave Trade Act", "British anti-slavery", "transatlantic trade abolished"], "description": "The British Parliament passes the Slave Trade Act, abolishing the transatlantic slave trade in the British Empire after decades of campaigning by abolitionists led by William Wilberforce. The law marks a turning point in the global fight against slavery, though slavery itself continues in British colonies until 1833.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','latin-american-independence',158,'{"id": "latin-american-independence", "name": "Latin American Independence Movements", "year": 1810, "categories": ["Politics", "War", "Social"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Simon Bolivar", "independence Latin America", "Spanish colonies independence", "Jose de San Martin"], "description": "Inspired by the American and French revolutions and weakened Spanish imperial control, independence movements erupt across Latin America. Led by figures like Simón Bolívar and José de San Martín, most of Spanish America achieves independence over the following two decades, fundamentally redrawing the political map.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','napoleon-defeat-waterloo',159,'{"id": "napoleon-defeat-waterloo", "name": "Battle of Waterloo", "year": 1815, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Napoleon''s last battle", "Wellington vs Napoleon", "final defeat Napoleon", "Waterloo Belgium"], "description": "Napoleon Bonaparte is defeated decisively by the Duke of Wellington and Prussian forces at Waterloo in Belgium, ending his Hundred Days return to power. His final exile to Saint Helena ends the Napoleonic era and ushers in the Concert of Europe that shapes the continent for a generation.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','greek-independence',160,'{"id": "greek-independence", "name": "Greek War of Independence", "year": 1821, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Greece vs Ottoman", "Greek revolution", "Lord Byron Greece", "Hellenic independence"], "description": "Greek patriots launch a war of independence against Ottoman rule, drawing romanticist support from Europe and eventually winning international recognition for an independent Greek state. The struggle inspires nationalist movements across Europe and marks the beginning of the Ottoman Empire''s long decline.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','first-steam-railway',161,'{"id": "first-steam-railway", "name": "First Public Steam Railway Opens", "year": 1825, "categories": ["Science", "Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Stockton Darlington railway", "George Stephenson", "Locomotion No. 1", "railway age begins", "steam locomotive public", "Industrial Revolution transport"], "description": "George Stephenson''s Stockton and Darlington Railway opens in northern England, becoming the first public railway to use steam locomotives to carry passengers and freight on a regular commercial service. The success of the line launches the railway age, with networks expanding rapidly across Britain and then the world, transforming the cost and speed of overland transport beyond anything previously imaginable. Cheap, fast railways reshape economies, settlement patterns, and the conduct of warfare, accelerating the Industrial Revolution and binding global trade together.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','great-reform-act',162,'{"id": "great-reform-act", "name": "Great Reform Act Passed in Britain", "year": 1832, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Reform Act 1832", "British electoral reform", "rotten boroughs abolished", "parliamentary reform England", "Victorian democracy begins", "British suffrage history"], "description": "The Great Reform Act is passed by the British Parliament after fierce political struggle, abolishing the notorious ''rotten boroughs'' — constituencies with tiny electorates controlled by wealthy patrons — and extending the vote to a significant portion of the male middle class. Though far from establishing full democracy, the Act breaks the landed aristocracy''s monopoly on political representation and establishes the principle that Parliament should broadly reflect the population. It sets Britain on the gradual path toward universal suffrage, completed nearly a century later.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','queen-victoria-accession',163,'{"id": "queen-victoria-accession", "name": "Queen Victoria Ascends to the Throne", "year": 1837, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Victoria becomes queen", "Victorian era begins", "British Empire peak", "Queen Victoria crowned", "1837 Britain", "longest reigning monarch"], "description": "Eighteen-year-old Victoria becomes Queen of the United Kingdom following the death of her uncle William IV, beginning a reign of 63 years that makes her the longest-serving British monarch up to that point. The Victorian era sees Britain at the height of its imperial power, governing roughly a quarter of the world''s land and population, while at home rapid industrialization, social reform movements, scientific advances, and the gradual expansion of democratic rights transform British society. Victoria herself becomes a symbol of moral authority and imperial confidence across the English-speaking world.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','opium-wars-china',164,'{"id": "opium-wars-china", "name": "First Opium War", "year": 1839, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["China Britain war opium", "Canton trade conflict", "Treaty of Nanking", "unequal treaties China"], "description": "Britain goes to war against China after the Chinese government attempts to stop the lucrative British opium trade, decisively defeating the Qing forces. The resulting Treaty of Nanking forces China to cede Hong Kong and open ports to trade, beginning a century of humiliation for China.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','chinese-opium-ban',165,'{"id": "chinese-opium-ban", "name": "Lin Zexu Destroys Opium in Canton", "year": 1839, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Commissioner Lin opium", "China anti-opium", "Canton opium seized", "British merchants opium"], "description": "Imperial Commissioner Lin Zexu seizes and destroys over 20,000 chests of opium from British merchants in Canton, in a dramatic demonstration of Chinese resistance to the drug trade. Britain responds by launching the First Opium War, setting in motion China''s century of humiliation.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','first-use-of-anesthesia',166,'{"id": "first-use-of-anesthesia", "name": "First Use of Surgical Anesthesia", "year": 1844, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "North America", "aliases": ["ether anesthesia", "Horace Wells nitrous oxide", "Crawford Long ether", "painless surgery", "anesthetic invented", "surgical revolution"], "description": "American dentist Horace Wells pioneers the use of nitrous oxide for tooth extraction without pain, and within two years William Morton''s public demonstration of ether anesthesia at Massachusetts General Hospital confirms and spreads the breakthrough worldwide. The ability to render patients unconscious during operations transforms surgery from an ordeal of conscious agony — endured as briefly as possible — into a methodical, precise discipline. Anesthesia is widely regarded as one of the greatest gifts of medicine, enabling procedures that save countless millions of lives.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','revolutions-of-1848',167,'{"id": "revolutions-of-1848", "name": "Revolutions of 1848 Sweep Europe", "year": 1848, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Springtime of Nations", "1848 revolutions", "European revolutions", "Year of Revolutions", "liberal revolutions Europe", "nationalist uprisings 1848"], "description": "A wave of liberal and nationalist revolutions erupts across Europe in 1848, toppling or threatening governments in France, the German states, the Austrian Empire, Italy, and beyond in the space of weeks. Driven by demands for constitutional government, national self-determination, and economic reform, the uprisings briefly overthrow many ancien régime governments before being crushed by conservative military force. The revolutions accelerate nationalist movements across Europe, hasten the decline of the old dynastic order, and are accompanied by Marx and Engels''s Communist Manifesto, published the same year.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','crimean-war',168,'{"id": "crimean-war", "name": "Crimean War", "year": 1853, "categories": ["War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Russia vs Ottoman Empire", "Florence Nightingale", "Charge of the Light Brigade", "Crimea war", "siege of Sevastopol", "1853 war Russia Britain"], "description": "Russia goes to war with the Ottoman Empire over influence in the Holy Land and access to the Black Sea, drawing in Britain, France, and Sardinia on the Ottoman side in the first major European conflict since the Napoleonic Wars. The Crimean War becomes notable for the nursing reforms of Florence Nightingale, which lay the foundations of modern professional nursing, and for the catastrophic Charge of the Light Brigade, immortalized by Tennyson. The war ends Russian expansion toward the Mediterranean and marks the beginning of modern military logistics, journalism, and battlefield medicine.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','opium-war-second',169,'{"id": "opium-war-second", "name": "Second Opium War", "year": 1856, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Arrow War", "China Britain France war", "Peking sacked", "Summer Palace burned"], "description": "Britain and France wage a second war against China, ultimately sacking Beijing and burning the Summer Palace, forcing China to sign the Convention of Peking granting further trading concessions. The conflict deepens China''s century of humiliation and further weakens the Qing dynasty.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','indian-rebellion-1857',170,'{"id": "indian-rebellion-1857", "name": "First Indian War of Independence", "year": 1857, "categories": ["War", "Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Sepoy Mutiny", "Indian Rebellion", "1857 uprising", "Mangal Pandey", "Rani Laxmibai"], "description": "Indian soldiers in the British East India Company''s army mutiny at Meerut, sparking a widespread uprising across northern and central India against British rule. Though the rebellion is eventually suppressed, it leads to the dissolution of the East India Company and direct Crown rule over India.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','darwin-evolution',171,'{"id": "darwin-evolution", "name": "Darwin Publishes Theory of Evolution", "year": 1859, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["On the Origin of Species", "natural selection", "Charles Darwin", "evolution theory"], "description": "Charles Darwin publishes On the Origin of Species, introducing the theory of evolution by natural selection and explaining the diversity of life on Earth through common ancestry. The theory revolutionizes biology and profoundly challenges religious accounts of creation, sparking debate that continues to this day.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','first-oil-well',172,'{"id": "first-oil-well", "name": "First Commercial Oil Well Drilled", "year": 1859, "categories": ["Science", "Culture"], "region": "North America", "aliases": ["Drake oil well", "Titusville Pennsylvania", "petroleum industry begins", "Edwin Drake", "fossil fuel age begins", "oil discovery 1859"], "description": "Edwin Drake successfully drills the first commercial oil well near Titusville, Pennsylvania, striking oil at a depth of 21 meters and triggering an oil rush across the region. The discovery marks the beginning of the modern petroleum industry, enabling oil to be extracted, refined, and sold at scale for the first time. Cheap petroleum powers the second Industrial Revolution, fuels the age of automobiles and aviation, and makes oil the central commodity of the global economy and of geopolitics throughout the twentieth century.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 8}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','american-civil-war',173,'{"id": "american-civil-war", "name": "American Civil War", "year": 1861, "categories": ["War", "Politics", "Social"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Union vs Confederacy", "US Civil War", "Lincoln war", "slavery abolition war", "Confederate states"], "description": "The United States erupts into civil war when eleven Southern states secede over the issue of slavery and form the Confederate States of America. After four years of devastating conflict, the Union is preserved, slavery is abolished through the Thirteenth Amendment, and the nation''s social order is fundamentally transformed.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','emancipation-proclamation',174,'{"id": "emancipation-proclamation", "name": "Emancipation Proclamation Issued", "year": 1863, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "North America", "aliases": ["Lincoln frees slaves", "Emancipation Proclamation", "slavery abolished Civil War", "13th amendment precursor", "1863 freedom", "Confederate slaves freed"], "description": "President Abraham Lincoln issues the Emancipation Proclamation, declaring all enslaved people in states in rebellion against the Union to be free as of January 1, 1863. Though initially limited in immediate practical effect — applying only to areas not yet under Union control — the proclamation fundamentally transforms the Civil War from a conflict to preserve the Union into a war for human freedom, giving it a powerful moral dimension. It paves the way for the Thirteenth Amendment, which permanently abolished slavery throughout the United States in 1865.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 8}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','abolition-slavery-us',175,'{"id": "abolition-slavery-us", "name": "Abolition of Slavery in the United States", "year": 1865, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["13th Amendment", "Emancipation Proclamation", "Lincoln abolish slavery", "end of slavery USA"], "description": "The Thirteenth Amendment to the US Constitution is ratified, formally abolishing slavery throughout the United States at the end of the Civil War. The amendment liberates approximately four million enslaved people and begins the complex and often violent process of Reconstruction in the American South.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','lincoln-assassination',176,'{"id": "lincoln-assassination", "name": "Assassination of Abraham Lincoln", "year": 1865, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "North America", "aliases": ["Lincoln shot", "John Wilkes Booth", "Ford''s Theatre", "Lincoln killed", "presidential assassination", "Good Friday 1865", "Lincoln murder"], "description": "President Abraham Lincoln is shot by Confederate sympathizer John Wilkes Booth at Ford''s Theatre in Washington, D.C., dying the following morning just days after the Confederate surrender ends the Civil War. Lincoln''s death robs the nation of the leader best positioned to pursue a reconciliatory Reconstruction of the defeated South. The assassination leaves reunification in less capable hands, with consequences — particularly for the rights of newly freed Black Americans — that shape American society for generations.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','meiji-restoration-japan',177,'{"id": "meiji-restoration-japan", "name": "Meiji Restoration in Japan", "year": 1868, "categories": ["Politics", "Social", "Technology"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Japan modernization", "Emperor Meiji", "Tokugawa shogunate ends", "Japanese industrialization"], "description": "Emperor Meiji is restored to power, ending the feudal Tokugawa shogunate and launching Japan''s rapid modernization. Japan adopts Western technology, institutions, and military organization at an extraordinary pace, transforming from a feudal society into a modern industrial and military power within a generation.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','suez-canal-opens',178,'{"id": "suez-canal-opens", "name": "Suez Canal Opens", "year": 1869, "categories": ["Technology", "Politics", "Exploration"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Egypt canal", "Ferdinand de Lesseps", "Mediterranean Red Sea link", "maritime shortcut"], "description": "The Suez Canal, connecting the Mediterranean Sea to the Red Sea through Egypt, opens after ten years of construction, dramatically shortening sea routes between Europe and Asia. The canal becomes one of the world''s most strategically important waterways and a flashpoint of imperial rivalry.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','gandhi-born',179,'{"id": "gandhi-born", "name": "Mahatma Gandhi Born", "year": 1869, "categories": ["Social", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Mohandas Gandhi birth", "Father of Nation born", "Gujarat leader born", "satyagraha founder"], "description": "Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi is born in Porbandar, Gujarat, into a merchant-caste family. He will grow up to lead India''s independence movement through nonviolent resistance, profoundly influencing civil rights leaders worldwide including Martin Luther King Jr. and Nelson Mandela.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','unification-germany',180,'{"id": "unification-germany", "name": "German Unification", "year": 1871, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Otto von Bismarck", "Franco-Prussian War", "Second Reich", "German Empire proclaimed"], "description": "Otto von Bismarck orchestrates the unification of the German states under Prussian leadership following victory in the Franco-Prussian War, creating the German Empire. The new power fundamentally alters the balance of power in Europe and sets in motion forces that will lead to two world wars.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','telephone-invented',181,'{"id": "telephone-invented", "name": "Telephone Invented", "year": 1876, "categories": ["Technology"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Alexander Graham Bell", "first telephone call", "voice communication technology", "Bell patent"], "description": "Alexander Graham Bell makes the first successful voice telephone call, opening an era of instant long-distance communication. His invention rapidly transforms business, society, and personal relationships across the globe and lays the groundwork for all modern telecommunications.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','cricket-test-first',182,'{"id": "cricket-test-first", "name": "First Test Cricket Match", "year": 1877, "categories": ["Sports"], "region": "Oceania", "aliases": ["Australia England cricket", "cricket origins test", "first international cricket", "Melbourne cricket ground"], "description": "The first official Test cricket match is played between Australia and England at the Melbourne Cricket Ground, with Australia winning by 45 runs. Test cricket, played over five days, becomes the pinnacle of the sport and a cultural institution across the British Commonwealth.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','zulu-war',183,'{"id": "zulu-war", "name": "Anglo-Zulu War", "year": 1879, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Isandlwana battle", "Zulu victory Britain", "Rorke''s Drift", "South Africa Zulu kingdom"], "description": "British forces invade the Zulu Kingdom and suffer a catastrophic defeat at Isandlwana, one of the worst British military disasters in colonial history, before eventually defeating the Zulus. The war ends the independent Zulu Kingdom and marks Britain''s determination to consolidate control of southern Africa.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','krakatoa-erupts',184,'{"id": "krakatoa-erupts", "name": "Krakatoa Erupts", "year": 1883, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "Southeast Asia", "aliases": ["Krakatau", "volcanic eruption 1883", "Indonesia volcano", "loudest sound in history", "tsunami 1883", "volcanic winter", "Krakatoa explosion"], "description": "The volcanic island of Krakatoa in the Dutch East Indies erupts in one of the most powerful volcanic events in recorded history, generating explosions heard nearly 5,000 kilometers away and sending a tsunami that kills over 36,000 people on the coasts of Java and Sumatra. The enormous quantities of ash and sulfur dioxide ejected into the upper atmosphere lower global temperatures for several years, producing vivid crimson sunsets that inspire artists worldwide, including possibly Edvard Munch''s The Scream. Krakatoa''s eruption is the first natural disaster to be reported globally in near-real time via the telegraph network.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','colonial-africa-berlin',185,'{"id": "colonial-africa-berlin", "name": "Berlin Conference Divides Africa", "year": 1884, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Scramble for Africa", "Berlin Conference", "Africa colonization", "European partition Africa"], "description": "European powers meet at the Berlin Conference to regulate the colonization of Africa, effectively dividing the continent among themselves with little regard for existing ethnic or political boundaries. The resulting borders, drawn by European diplomats, create lasting instability and conflict that reverberates across Africa today.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','indian-national-congress-founded',186,'{"id": "indian-national-congress-founded", "name": "Indian National Congress Founded", "year": 1885, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["INC founding", "Congress party", "Dadabhai Naoroji", "A.O. Hume"], "description": "The Indian National Congress is established in Bombay as a platform for educated Indians to discuss political issues and present demands to the British government. It would evolve into the primary vehicle for the Indian independence movement under leaders like Gandhi and Nehru.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','partition-of-africa-colonial',187,'{"id": "partition-of-africa-colonial", "name": "Congo Free State Atrocities", "year": 1885, "categories": ["Social", "Politics", "Disasters"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Leopold Congo", "Belgian Congo atrocities", "rubber terror Africa", "Conrad Heart of Darkness"], "description": "King Leopold II of Belgium claims the Congo as his personal property and institutes a brutal forced labor system to harvest rubber and ivory, killing an estimated ten million Congolese. The atrocities, exposed by journalists and activists, spark one of history''s first international human rights campaigns.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','ramanujan-born',188,'{"id": "ramanujan-born", "name": "Srinivasa Ramanujan Born", "year": 1887, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Indian mathematician", "Ramanujan mathematics", "Hardy Ramanujan", "self-taught genius"], "description": "Srinivasa Ramanujan, one of history''s greatest mathematical geniuses, is born in Erode, Tamil Nadu. With almost no formal training, he would make extraordinary contributions to number theory, infinite series, and continued fractions, collaborating with G.H. Hardy at Cambridge.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','tesla-ac-electricity',189,'{"id": "tesla-ac-electricity", "name": "Tesla Demonstrates Alternating Current", "year": 1888, "categories": ["Technology", "Science"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Nikola Tesla AC", "War of currents", "Edison Tesla rivalry", "alternating current electricity"], "description": "Nikola Tesla demonstrates the practical viability of alternating current electrical systems, which can transmit power over long distances far more efficiently than Edison''s direct current. Backed by George Westinghouse, AC eventually wins the War of Currents and becomes the global standard for electrical power.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','japan-meiji-constitution',190,'{"id": "japan-meiji-constitution", "name": "Meiji Constitution Adopted in Japan", "year": 1889, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Japanese constitution Meiji", "Emperor sovereignty Japan", "Diet Japan", "modern Japan government"], "description": "Japan adopts its first modern constitution, establishing a constitutional monarchy with an elected parliament (Diet) while maintaining imperial sovereignty. The constitution formalizes Japan''s transformation into a modern state and lays the groundwork for its rise as a major world power.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','suffrage-new-zealand',191,'{"id": "suffrage-new-zealand", "name": "New Zealand Grants Women the Vote", "year": 1893, "categories": ["Social", "Politics"], "region": "Oceania", "aliases": ["first women suffrage country", "Kate Sheppard", "New Zealand women vote", "women voting rights first"], "description": "New Zealand becomes the first self-governing country in the world to grant all women the right to vote, following a petition campaign led by Kate Sheppard. The achievement provides inspiration and a model for suffrage movements in other countries worldwide.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','marconi-invents-radio',192,'{"id": "marconi-invents-radio", "name": "Marconi Demonstrates Wireless Telegraphy", "year": 1895, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["radio invented", "Marconi radio", "wireless communication", "radio telegraphy", "Guglielmo Marconi", "wireless telegraphy history"], "description": "Italian inventor Guglielmo Marconi successfully demonstrates wireless telegraphy over increasing distances, building on the theoretical foundations of Maxwell and Hertz to create the first practical radio communication system. Within years he sends signals across the Atlantic Ocean, and the technology is rapidly adopted for maritime communication, military operations, and eventually mass broadcasting. Radio transforms how information is transmitted, making possible the broadcast media that define twentieth-century public life and culture.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','x-rays-discovered',193,'{"id": "x-rays-discovered", "name": "X-Rays Discovered", "year": 1895, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Röntgen X-rays", "Wilhelm Röntgen", "X-ray discovery", "medical imaging invented", "radiation discovery 1895", "1895 physics Nobel"], "description": "German physicist Wilhelm Röntgen discovers X-rays while experimenting with cathode ray tubes, producing the first X-ray image — a photograph of his wife''s hand with her wedding ring clearly visible — and publishing his findings to astonished scientific and public audiences. The discovery spreads around the world within months and is immediately applied in hospitals for diagnosing fractures and internal conditions previously invisible to physicians. X-rays revolutionize medicine and open the field of radiation physics that leads to further discoveries including radioactivity, the atomic nucleus, and the foundations of quantum mechanics.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','modern-olympics-founded',194,'{"id": "modern-olympics-founded", "name": "Modern Olympic Games Founded", "year": 1896, "categories": ["Sports", "Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Athens Olympics", "Baron de Coubertin", "IOC founded", "first modern Olympics"], "description": "Pierre de Coubertin revives the Olympic Games in Athens with athletes from 14 nations competing in the first modern Olympiad. The Games grow from a small international competition into the world''s premier sporting event, watched by billions and imbued with ideals of international peace and friendship.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','curie-radioactivity',195,'{"id": "curie-radioactivity", "name": "Marie Curie Discovers Radioactivity Properties", "year": 1898, "categories": ["Science", "Medicine"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Curie radium polonium", "radioactivity research", "Marie Pierre Curie", "Nobel physics chemistry"], "description": "Marie Curie and her husband Pierre isolate the radioactive elements polonium and radium, pioneering the study of radioactivity and its medical applications. Marie Curie becomes the first woman to win a Nobel Prize and the only person to win it in two different sciences, transforming physics and medicine.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','south-african-boer-war',196,'{"id": "south-african-boer-war", "name": "South African Boer War", "year": 1899, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Anglo-Boer War", "British South Africa war", "concentration camps Boers", "Transvaal war"], "description": "Britain goes to war against the Boer republics of the Transvaal and Orange Free State in South Africa to secure control of the gold and diamond fields. The conflict introduces concentration camps to the modern lexicon and results in British annexation of the Boer republics, eventually leading to the Union of South Africa.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','australia-federation',197,'{"id": "australia-federation", "name": "Federation of Australia", "year": 1901, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Oceania", "aliases": ["Australian Commonwealth", "six colonies unite", "Australian constitution", "Federation Day"], "description": "Six self-governing British colonies unite to form the Commonwealth of Australia, adopting a federal constitution that balances state and national powers. Australia''s federation creates one of the world''s first democracies with universal male suffrage and establishes a stable nation on a vast continent.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','wright-brothers-flight',198,'{"id": "wright-brothers-flight", "name": "Wright Brothers Achieve Powered Flight", "year": 1903, "categories": ["Technology", "Science"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Kitty Hawk flight", "Orville Wilbur Wright", "airplane invention", "first flight"], "description": "Orville Wright pilots the Flyer for a 12-second flight at Kitty Hawk, North Carolina, achieving the world''s first powered, controlled airplane flight. The invention of the airplane revolutionizes transportation, warfare, and commerce in the twentieth century.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','suffragette-emmeline-pankhurst',199,'{"id": "suffragette-emmeline-pankhurst", "name": "Women''s Suffrage Movement Founded in Britain", "year": 1903, "categories": ["Social", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Emmeline Pankhurst WSPU", "Suffragettes Britain", "votes for women UK", "women''s suffrage movement"], "description": "Emmeline Pankhurst founds the Women''s Social and Political Union in Britain, pioneering militant tactics including hunger strikes, demonstrations, and property damage in the campaign for women''s right to vote. The movement''s pressure contributes to women over 30 gaining the vote in Britain in 1918.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','russo-japanese-war',200,'{"id": "russo-japanese-war", "name": "Russo-Japanese War", "year": 1904, "categories": ["War"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Japan defeats Russia", "Battle of Tsushima", "Port Arthur siege", "1904 Manchuria war", "Asian power defeats European", "Japanese victory 1905"], "description": "Japan launches a surprise attack on the Russian naval base at Port Arthur, beginning a war that shocks the world when Japan decisively defeats the Russian Empire on both land and sea. The Japanese victory at the Battle of Tsushima — the most decisive naval battle since Trafalgar — is the first major defeat of a European great power by an Asian nation in the modern era. The war accelerates the Russian domestic unrest that leads to the 1905 Revolution and signals Japan''s emergence as a major world power, reshaping the balance of power in Asia.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','partition-of-bengal',201,'{"id": "partition-of-bengal", "name": "Partition of Bengal", "year": 1905, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Curzon Bengal partition", "Swadeshi movement trigger", "Bengal division"], "description": "British Viceroy Lord Curzon partitions Bengal into Hindu-majority West Bengal and Muslim-majority East Bengal, ostensibly for administrative reasons. The move sparks massive protests and the Swadeshi movement, in which Indians boycott British goods, marking a new phase of nationalist resistance.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','swadeshi-movement',202,'{"id": "swadeshi-movement", "name": "Swadeshi Movement Launched", "year": 1905, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["boycott British goods", "Indian self-reliance", "homespun movement", "nationalist movement"], "description": "In response to the partition of Bengal, Indian nationalists launch the Swadeshi movement, calling for the boycott of British-made goods and the promotion of Indian-made products. The movement spreads nationalist sentiment widely and marks a turning point in the Indian independence struggle.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','einstein-relativity',203,'{"id": "einstein-relativity", "name": "Einstein Publishes Theory of Relativity", "year": 1905, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Albert Einstein", "special relativity", "E=mc2", "annus mirabilis", "space time"], "description": "Albert Einstein publishes his Special Theory of Relativity along with three other groundbreaking papers, introducing the famous equation E=mc² and revolutionizing our understanding of space, time, mass, and energy. This miracle year produces discoveries that transform physics and underpin technologies from nuclear energy to GPS.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','fall-of-qing-dynasty',204,'{"id": "fall-of-qing-dynasty", "name": "Fall of the Qing Dynasty", "year": 1911, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Chinese Revolution 1911", "Xinhai Revolution", "end of imperial China", "Republic of China proclaimed", "Sun Yat-sen", "Qing dynasty ends", "2000 years of empire ends"], "description": "The Xinhai Revolution sweeps away the Qing dynasty, ending over two thousand years of imperial rule in China and establishing the Republic of China. Led by reformists and nationalists inspired by Sun Yat-sen, the revolution abolishes the imperial examination system, the queue hairstyle enforced by the Manchu rulers, and the monarchy itself. The newly established republic is immediately beset by warlordism and political fragmentation, setting the stage for the decades of conflict between Nationalists and Communists that follow.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','tagore-nobel-prize',205,'{"id": "tagore-nobel-prize", "name": "Rabindranath Tagore Wins Nobel Prize", "year": 1913, "categories": ["Arts", "Culture"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Tagore literature Nobel", "Gitanjali", "Bengali poet Nobel", "first Asian Nobel literature"], "description": "Rabindranath Tagore becomes the first non-European to win the Nobel Prize in Literature, awarded for his collection of poems Gitanjali. The honor brings global attention to Bengali literature and to Tagore''s philosophy blending spiritual and humanist themes.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','world-war-one',206,'{"id": "world-war-one", "name": "World War One Begins", "year": 1914, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Great War", "WWI", "Archduke Franz Ferdinand", "trench warfare", "Allied powers vs Central powers"], "description": "The assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand triggers a catastrophic chain of alliances that engulfs Europe in the first truly global war. The conflict kills an estimated 17 million people, topples four empires, redraws the world map, and sets the stage for the even more destructive Second World War.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','panama-canal-opens',207,'{"id": "panama-canal-opens", "name": "Panama Canal Opens", "year": 1914, "categories": ["Technology", "Exploration"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Canal Zone Panama", "Atlantic Pacific canal", "US engineering canal", "waterway Panama"], "description": "The Panama Canal opens, connecting the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans through the Isthmus of Panama after a decade of American construction following an earlier failed French attempt. The canal revolutionizes global maritime trade by eliminating the long voyage around South America.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','russian-revolution',208,'{"id": "russian-revolution", "name": "Russian Revolution", "year": 1917, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Bolshevik revolution", "Lenin October revolution", "Tsar overthrown", "Soviet Union birth"], "description": "Lenin''s Bolshevik party seizes power in Russia in October, overthrowing the Provisional Government and establishing the world''s first communist state. The revolution leads to a brutal civil war, the murder of the Tsar''s family, and the eventual formation of the Soviet Union.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','first-world-war-ends',209,'{"id": "first-world-war-ends", "name": "World War One Armistice", "year": 1918, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["WWI ends", "Armistice Day", "November 11 peace", "Versailles treaty preparation"], "description": "At the eleventh hour of the eleventh day of the eleventh month, an armistice ends the fighting on the Western Front, concluding the First World War. The war''s end reshapes the world map through the collapse of four empires and sets conditions that lead directly to the Second World War.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','bolshevik-civil-war',210,'{"id": "bolshevik-civil-war", "name": "Russian Civil War", "year": 1918, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Reds vs Whites", "Bolshevik civil war", "Soviet consolidation", "Red Army White Army"], "description": "Following the Bolshevik Revolution, Russia erupts in a devastating civil war between the Bolshevik Red Army and the anti-Bolshevik White forces supported by foreign interventions. The Bolshevik victory consolidates communist rule and leads to the formation of the Soviet Union in 1922.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','jallianwala-bagh-massacre',211,'{"id": "jallianwala-bagh-massacre", "name": "Jallianwala Bagh Massacre", "year": 1919, "categories": ["Politics", "Social", "Disasters"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Amritsar massacre", "General Dyer", "British atrocity India", "Baisakhi massacre"], "description": "British Brigadier General Reginald Dyer orders troops to open fire on a peaceful crowd gathered at Jallianwala Bagh in Amritsar, killing hundreds of civilians. The massacre shocks the nation and world, radicalizing many Indians and galvanizing the independence movement.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','treaty-of-versailles',212,'{"id": "treaty-of-versailles", "name": "Treaty of Versailles Signed", "year": 1919, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["WWI peace treaty", "Germany war guilt", "reparations Germany", "League of Nations created"], "description": "The victorious Allied powers sign the Treaty of Versailles with Germany, imposing harsh reparations, territorial losses, and a war guilt clause that humiliates the German nation. The punitive terms generate widespread resentment in Germany and create conditions that facilitate the rise of Adolf Hitler.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','non-cooperation-movement',213,'{"id": "non-cooperation-movement", "name": "Non-Cooperation Movement", "year": 1920, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Gandhi non-cooperation", "civil disobedience India", "khilafat movement", "satyagraha"], "description": "Mahatma Gandhi launches the Non-Cooperation Movement, calling on Indians to withdraw from British institutions, return honors, and boycott British goods and courts. It marks the first mass nationalist campaign under Gandhi''s leadership and draws millions into the independence struggle.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','women-suffrage-us',214,'{"id": "women-suffrage-us", "name": "Women Gain Right to Vote in the United States", "year": 1920, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["19th Amendment", "women suffrage US", "votes for women", "suffragette victory"], "description": "The Nineteenth Amendment to the US Constitution is ratified, prohibiting the denial of the right to vote based on sex and granting women the right to vote nationwide. The achievement caps decades of suffragette activism and becomes a landmark moment in the global struggle for gender equality.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','ottoman-empire-falls',215,'{"id": "ottoman-empire-falls", "name": "Ottoman Empire Falls", "year": 1922, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Turkey republic", "Ataturk", "Sultanate abolished", "Ottoman collapse", "Mustafa Kemal"], "description": "The Ottoman Sultanate is formally abolished and Mustafa Kemal Atatürk establishes the Republic of Turkey from the empire''s Anatolian heartland. The fall of the Ottoman Empire reshapes the Middle East, creating new nations from former Ottoman territories and giving rise to conflicts that continue today.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','turkish-republic-founded',216,'{"id": "turkish-republic-founded", "name": "Turkish Republic Founded", "year": 1923, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Turkey becomes republic", "Mustafa Kemal Atatürk", "Ottoman Empire ends", "Ankara capital Turkey", "secular Turkey", "Lausanne Treaty 1923"], "description": "Mustafa Kemal Atatürk proclaims the Republic of Turkey from the ruins of the Ottoman Empire, becoming its first president and implementing one of the most sweeping modernization programs in history. Under Atatürk''s direction, Turkey adopts the Latin alphabet, separates religion from the state, grants women the right to vote, replaces Islamic law with European-inspired legal codes, and restructures education and dress along Western lines. The Turkish Republic represents one of the most rapid and radical transformations of a society in the twentieth century.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','television-invented',217,'{"id": "television-invented", "name": "Television Invented", "year": 1926, "categories": ["Science", "Culture"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["John Logie Baird", "TV invented", "first television demonstration", "mechanical television", "broadcast television history", "moving image transmission"], "description": "Scottish inventor John Logie Baird gives the first public demonstration of a working television system in London, transmitting moving images of human faces using a mechanical scanning system. Though Baird''s mechanical approach is soon superseded by all-electronic television developed by Philo Farnsworth and others, his demonstration proves the concept and launches the race to develop broadcasting. Television becomes the dominant mass medium of the twentieth century, reshaping politics, culture, advertising, and daily life across the world.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','chinese-civil-war',218,'{"id": "chinese-civil-war", "name": "Chinese Civil War", "year": 1927, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Communists Nationalists China", "KMT CCP war", "Chiang Kai-shek Mao war", "Taiwan mainland split"], "description": "Conflict between Chiang Kai-shek''s Nationalist Party and Mao''s Communist Party erupts into civil war, interrupted by Japanese invasion before resuming after World War Two. The Communist victory drives the Nationalists to Taiwan and establishes the People''s Republic of China.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','penicillin-discovered',219,'{"id": "penicillin-discovered", "name": "Penicillin Discovered", "year": 1928, "categories": ["Medicine", "Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Alexander Fleming antibiotic", "mold antibiotic", "Fleming penicillin", "antibiotics discovered"], "description": "Scottish bacteriologist Alexander Fleming observes that the mold Penicillium notatum kills bacteria on his culture plate, discovering the first antibiotic. Penicillin''s subsequent development and mass production during World War II saves millions of lives and inaugurates the antibiotic era of medicine.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','great-depression',220,'{"id": "great-depression", "name": "Great Depression Begins", "year": 1929, "categories": ["Social", "Politics"], "region": "Global", "aliases": ["Wall Street Crash", "stock market crash 1929", "economic depression", "unemployment crisis"], "description": "The New York Stock Exchange crashes in October, triggering a global economic depression that causes mass unemployment, widespread poverty, and banking failures across the world. The Great Depression reshapes economic thought, expands the role of government in economies, and creates conditions for the rise of fascism in Europe.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','gandhi-salt-march',221,'{"id": "gandhi-salt-march", "name": "Gandhi''s Salt March", "year": 1930, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Dandi March", "salt satyagraha", "civil disobedience campaign", "Gandhi Dandi"], "description": "Mahatma Gandhi leads a 240-mile march to the sea at Dandi to make salt in defiance of the British salt tax, launching the Civil Disobedience Movement. The symbolic act captures worldwide attention and inspires mass civil disobedience across India.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','first-football-world-cup',222,'{"id": "first-football-world-cup", "name": "First FIFA World Cup", "year": 1930, "categories": ["Sports", "Culture"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Uruguay World Cup", "FIFA inaugural tournament", "football world championship", "Jules Rimet trophy"], "description": "Uruguay hosts and wins the inaugural FIFA World Cup, defeating Argentina in the final in Montevideo with thirteen nations participating. The tournament grows into the world''s most watched sporting event, with the final drawing television audiences exceeding one billion people.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','japanese-empire-manchuria',223,'{"id": "japanese-empire-manchuria", "name": "Japan Invades Manchuria", "year": 1931, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Manchurian incident", "Mukden incident", "Japanese imperialism Asia", "Manchukuo"], "description": "Japan''s Kwantung Army seizes Manchuria in northeastern China following a staged incident, establishing the puppet state of Manchukuo. The invasion exposes the League of Nations'' inability to stop aggression and marks the beginning of Japan''s expansionist campaign across Asia.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','hitler-rise-chancellor',224,'{"id": "hitler-rise-chancellor", "name": "Hitler Appointed Chancellor of Germany", "year": 1933, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Nazi rise to power", "Third Reich begins", "Weimar Republic ends", "Adolf Hitler chancellor"], "description": "Adolf Hitler is appointed Chancellor of Germany by President Hindenburg, enabling the Nazi Party to rapidly consolidate power through emergency decrees and the elimination of political opposition. Within months, Hitler transforms Germany''s democratic republic into a totalitarian fascist state.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','long-march-china',225,'{"id": "long-march-china", "name": "The Long March", "year": 1934, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Mao Long March", "Chinese Communist retreat", "Red Army march", "Yan''an"], "description": "The Chinese Communist Red Army embarks on a strategic retreat of over 6,000 miles through mountainous terrain to escape Nationalist forces, with Mao Zedong emerging as the dominant leader. The Long March becomes a foundational myth of the Chinese Communist Party and a symbol of revolutionary endurance.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','rise-of-nazism',226,'{"id": "rise-of-nazism", "name": "Nazi Party Seizes Control of Germany", "year": 1934, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Night of Long Knives", "Hitler becomes Fuhrer", "Third Reich consolidated", "Hindenburg death"], "description": "Following President Hindenburg''s death, Hitler merges the offices of Chancellor and President to become absolute ruler, or Fuhrer, of Germany, completing the Nazi seizure of power. The consolidation of totalitarian control enables the subsequent persecution of Jews, political opponents, and minorities.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','spanish-civil-war',227,'{"id": "spanish-civil-war", "name": "Spanish Civil War", "year": 1936, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Franco Spain", "Republicans Nationalists", "Guernica bombing", "International Brigades"], "description": "General Francisco Franco leads a military uprising against the elected Republican government of Spain, triggering a brutal three-year civil war that draws foreign intervention from Nazi Germany, Fascist Italy, and the Soviet Union. Franco''s victory establishes a fascist dictatorship and the conflict becomes a rehearsal for World War Two.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','world-war-two',228,'{"id": "world-war-two", "name": "World War Two Begins", "year": 1939, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Global", "aliases": ["WWII", "Nazi Germany invasion Poland", "Hitler war", "Allies vs Axis", "Second World War"], "description": "Nazi Germany invades Poland, prompting Britain and France to declare war and beginning the most destructive conflict in human history. The war ultimately involves most of the world''s nations, kills an estimated 70-85 million people, and transforms the global political order.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','battle-of-britain',229,'{"id": "battle-of-britain", "name": "Battle of Britain", "year": 1940, "categories": ["War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["RAF vs Luftwaffe", "Blitz Britain", "Churchill finest hour", "air war England"], "description": "The Royal Air Force fights off a sustained German Luftwaffe campaign to achieve air superiority over Britain, in the first major campaign fought entirely by air forces. Britain''s victory prevents a German invasion and represents a turning point in World War Two, inspiring Churchill''s famous tribute to ''The Few.''", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','holocaust',230,'{"id": "holocaust", "name": "Holocaust", "year": 1941, "categories": ["Social", "Politics", "War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Nazi genocide", "Final Solution", "Auschwitz", "Jewish genocide", "Shoah"], "description": "Nazi Germany implements the systematic genocide of six million Jews and millions of others including Roma, disabled people, and political opponents across occupied Europe. The Holocaust becomes the defining atrocity of the modern era, leading to the Nuremberg trials, the Genocide Convention, and the founding of Israel.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','japanese-pearl-harbor',231,'{"id": "japanese-pearl-harbor", "name": "Attack on Pearl Harbor", "year": 1941, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Hawaii bombing", "Japan attacks US", "Pacific War begins", "day of infamy"], "description": "Japanese naval aircraft launch a surprise attack on the US naval base at Pearl Harbor, Hawaii, sinking or damaging much of the Pacific Fleet. The attack forces the United States to enter World War Two, dramatically altering the global conflict''s outcome.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','quit-india-movement',232,'{"id": "quit-india-movement", "name": "Quit India Movement", "year": 1942, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Do or Die Gandhi", "August Kranti", "British leave India movement", "Quit India resolution"], "description": "Mahatma Gandhi launches the Quit India Movement, demanding an immediate end to British rule during World War II with his rallying cry of ''Do or Die.'' The British arrest Gandhi and thousands of Congress leaders, but the movement signifies the final mass push for independence.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','manhattan-project',233,'{"id": "manhattan-project", "name": "Manhattan Project Develops Atomic Bomb", "year": 1942, "categories": ["Science", "Technology", "War"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["nuclear weapon development", "Oppenheimer bomb", "Trinity test", "Los Alamos"], "description": "The United States launches the Manhattan Project, a massive secret scientific and engineering effort employing over 130,000 people to develop the world''s first nuclear weapons. Led by J. Robert Oppenheimer, the project produces the bombs dropped on Hiroshima and Nagasaki and fundamentally changes warfare and geopolitics.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','d-day-normandy',234,'{"id": "d-day-normandy", "name": "D-Day Normandy Landings", "year": 1944, "categories": ["War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Operation Overlord", "Normandy invasion", "Allied landing France", "June sixth landing"], "description": "Allied forces launch the largest seaborne invasion in history on the beaches of Normandy, France, opening the long-awaited Western Front against Nazi Germany. The success of Operation Overlord turns the tide of war in Western Europe and ultimately leads to Germany''s defeat.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','atomic-bomb-hiroshima',235,'{"id": "atomic-bomb-hiroshima", "name": "Atomic Bomb Dropped on Hiroshima", "year": 1945, "categories": ["War", "Technology", "Science"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["nuclear bomb Japan", "Manhattan Project", "Enola Gay", "Little Boy bomb", "nuclear warfare"], "description": "The United States drops an atomic bomb on Hiroshima, Japan, instantly killing tens of thousands and exposing hundreds of thousands more to deadly radiation. The use of the weapon — followed days later by a second bomb on Nagasaki — ends World War II and inaugurates the nuclear age.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','united-nations-founded',236,'{"id": "united-nations-founded", "name": "United Nations Founded", "year": 1945, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Global", "aliases": ["UN charter", "international organization", "post-war order", "San Francisco conference"], "description": "Representatives from fifty nations sign the UN Charter in San Francisco, establishing the United Nations as the primary international organization for maintaining peace and cooperation. The UN creates a framework for international law, human rights, and collective security that shapes global governance to this day.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','end-world-war-two',237,'{"id": "end-world-war-two", "name": "World War Two Ends", "year": 1945, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Global", "aliases": ["VE Day VJ Day", "Japan surrenders", "Germany surrenders", "WWII victory", "postwar era begins"], "description": "World War Two concludes with Germany''s unconditional surrender in May and Japan''s surrender in September following the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki. The war''s end reshapes the global order, establishing the United States and Soviet Union as superpowers and laying the groundwork for the Cold War.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','nuremberg-trials',238,'{"id": "nuremberg-trials", "name": "Nuremberg Trials", "year": 1945, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Nazi war crimes trial", "international military tribunal", "crimes against humanity", "war crimes court"], "description": "Allied powers conduct the Nuremberg Trials, prosecuting Nazi leaders for war crimes, crimes against humanity, and crimes against peace, establishing that individuals can be held accountable under international law. The trials create the legal precedent for subsequent international criminal tribunals and the concept of universal human rights.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','japan-world-war-two-defeat',239,'{"id": "japan-world-war-two-defeat", "name": "Japan''s Surrender Ends the Pacific War", "year": 1945, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["VJ Day", "Japan surrenders", "Emperor Hirohito surrender", "MacArthur Tokyo Bay"], "description": "Emperor Hirohito announces Japan''s unconditional surrender following the atomic bombings and Soviet declaration of war, ending World War Two in the Pacific. The surrender ceremony aboard the USS Missouri in Tokyo Bay marks the beginning of the American occupation that transforms Japan into a democratic nation.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','indian-independence',240,'{"id": "indian-independence", "name": "Indian Independence", "year": 1947, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["India free", "15 August independence", "Nehru tryst with destiny", "end of British Raj"], "description": "India gains independence from British rule at midnight on August 15th, with Jawaharlal Nehru delivering his iconic ''Tryst with Destiny'' speech. The moment ends nearly two centuries of colonial rule and creates the world''s largest democracy.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','partition-india-pakistan',241,'{"id": "partition-india-pakistan", "name": "Partition of India and Pakistan", "year": 1947, "categories": ["Politics", "Social", "Disasters"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["India Pakistan partition", "Radcliffe Line", "refugee crisis partition", "Punjab Bengal partition"], "description": "The Indian subcontinent is partitioned into two independent nations — India and Pakistan — along religious lines, accompanied by one of the largest mass migrations in history. An estimated one to two million people die in sectarian violence and over ten million are displaced.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','cold-war-begins',242,'{"id": "cold-war-begins", "name": "Cold War Begins", "year": 1947, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Global", "aliases": ["Iron Curtain", "Truman Doctrine", "Marshall Plan", "US Soviet rivalry", "superpower competition"], "description": "Increasing tensions between the United States and Soviet Union harden into the Cold War, with President Truman articulating the policy of containment to prevent Soviet expansion. The ideological and geopolitical rivalry between the two superpowers dominates world politics for the next four decades.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','apartheid-south-africa',243,'{"id": "apartheid-south-africa", "name": "Apartheid Established in South Africa", "year": 1948, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["South Africa segregation", "National Party apartheid", "racial segregation", "South Africa racism"], "description": "The Afrikaner National Party wins elections in South Africa and implements apartheid, a rigid system of racial segregation that strips Black South Africans of political rights and enforces severe discrimination in all aspects of life. The system provokes international condemnation and a powerful internal resistance movement.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','mahatma-gandhi-assassinated',244,'{"id": "mahatma-gandhi-assassinated", "name": "Mahatma Gandhi Assassinated", "year": 1948, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Gandhi killed", "Nathuram Godse", "Father of the Nation death", "Gandhi murder"], "description": "Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi, the leader of India''s independence movement and prophet of nonviolent resistance, is shot and killed by Hindu nationalist Nathuram Godse in New Delhi. His assassination shocks the world and threatens to destabilize the newly independent nation.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','palestine-israel-state',245,'{"id": "palestine-israel-state", "name": "State of Israel Established", "year": 1948, "categories": ["Politics", "Religion", "War"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Israel independence", "Israeli state founded", "David Ben-Gurion", "Arab-Israeli conflict begins", "Nakba"], "description": "David Ben-Gurion proclaims the establishment of the State of Israel in British Mandatory Palestine, immediately triggering a war with neighboring Arab states. The founding of Israel and the displacement of hundreds of thousands of Palestinians creates a conflict that remains unresolved and deeply consequential to this day.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','chinese-communist-revolution',246,'{"id": "chinese-communist-revolution", "name": "Chinese Communist Revolution", "year": 1949, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Mao Zedong China", "People''s Republic of China", "Chiang Kai-shek defeated", "Long March outcome"], "description": "Mao Zedong proclaims the establishment of the People''s Republic of China after the Communist Party defeats Nationalist forces in the civil war. The revolution transforms the world''s most populous nation, creating a communist state that becomes a major power and reshapes global geopolitics.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','nato-founded',247,'{"id": "nato-founded", "name": "NATO Founded", "year": 1949, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["North Atlantic Treaty Organization", "Western military alliance", "collective defense pact", "Cold War alliance"], "description": "The North Atlantic Treaty Organization is established by the United States, Canada, and ten Western European nations as a collective defense alliance against Soviet expansion. NATO''s mutual defense commitment shapes the Cold War''s military balance and remains the world''s most powerful military alliance.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','indian-constitution-adopted',248,'{"id": "indian-constitution-adopted", "name": "Indian Constitution Adopted", "year": 1950, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Republic of India", "B.R. Ambedkar constitution", "Indian republic", "January 26 constitution"], "description": "India adopts its constitution on January 26th, becoming a republic and the world''s largest democracy, with B.R. Ambedkar as its chief architect. The constitution enshrines fundamental rights, abolishes untouchability, and establishes a federal democratic framework.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','korean-war',249,'{"id": "korean-war", "name": "Korean War", "year": 1950, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["North Korea South Korea war", "UN forces Korea", "forgotten war", "Korean peninsula conflict"], "description": "North Korea invades South Korea, drawing in US-led UN forces and later Chinese troops in a conflict that kills millions and ends in a stalemate along the original border. The Korean War establishes the enduring division of the peninsula and becomes the first hot war of the Cold War era.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','dna-structure-discovered',250,'{"id": "dna-structure-discovered", "name": "DNA Double Helix Structure Discovered", "year": 1953, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Watson Crick DNA", "double helix", "genetics revolution", "Rosalind Franklin", "molecular biology"], "description": "James Watson and Francis Crick, using X-ray crystallography data from Rosalind Franklin and others, determine the double helix structure of DNA. The discovery reveals the molecular basis of heredity and sparks the genomic revolution in biology and medicine.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','death-of-stalin',251,'{"id": "death-of-stalin", "name": "Death of Joseph Stalin", "year": 1953, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Stalin dies", "Soviet Union post-Stalin", "Khrushchev succeeds Stalin", "de-Stalinization", "Soviet thaw begins", "Stalin death March 1953"], "description": "Joseph Stalin, the Soviet dictator who transformed the USSR through forced collectivization, industrial crash programs, the Gulag labor camp system, and purges that killed millions, dies of a stroke after nearly three decades in power. His death triggers a power struggle within the Soviet leadership eventually won by Nikita Khrushchev, who denounces Stalin''s crimes in his 1956 ''Secret Speech'' and initiates a cautious political ''thaw.'' Stalin''s death marks a significant shift in the Cold War, reducing the acute tensions of his final paranoid years and beginning a gradual, halting reassessment of Soviet policy.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','everest-first-ascent',252,'{"id": "everest-first-ascent", "name": "First Ascent of Mount Everest", "year": 1953, "categories": ["Exploration"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Hillary and Tenzing", "Edmund Hillary", "Tenzing Norgay", "Everest summit 1953", "highest mountain climbed", "top of the world"], "description": "New Zealander Edmund Hillary and Nepali Sherpa Tenzing Norgay become the first people confirmed to stand on the summit of Mount Everest, the world''s highest peak at 8,849 meters, on May 29. The achievement, announced to the world on the morning of Queen Elizabeth II''s coronation, is celebrated across the British Commonwealth as a triumph of human endurance and teamwork. The ascent transforms mountaineering from an elite pursuit into a global aspiration and makes Everest a symbol of the limits of human ambition.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','vietnam-partition',253,'{"id": "vietnam-partition", "name": "Vietnam Partitioned at the Seventeenth Parallel", "year": 1954, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Geneva Accords Vietnam", "North South Vietnam", "Ho Chi Minh North", "Dien Bien Phu aftermath"], "description": "Following the decisive French defeat at Dien Bien Phu, the Geneva Accords divide Vietnam at the seventeenth parallel into the communist North and the Western-backed South, pending elections that never occur. The partition plants the seeds of the Vietnam War.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','french-colonial-algeria',254,'{"id": "french-colonial-algeria", "name": "Algerian War of Independence", "year": 1954, "categories": ["War", "Politics", "Social"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Algeria vs France", "FLN independence", "French Algeria war", "Algerian revolution"], "description": "The Algerian National Liberation Front launches an armed insurgency against French colonial rule, beginning an eight-year war that costs an estimated 300,000-1.5 million Algerian lives. Algeria''s independence in 1962 becomes a landmark moment in the global anti-colonial struggle.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','suez-crisis',255,'{"id": "suez-crisis", "name": "Suez Crisis", "year": 1956, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Egypt nationalizes canal", "Nasser Suez", "Anglo-French invasion Egypt", "Sinai war"], "description": "Egypt''s President Nasser nationalizes the Suez Canal, provoking a military intervention by Britain, France, and Israel that is quickly reversed under US and Soviet pressure. The crisis marks a decisive end to British and French imperial power and signals the rise of Arab nationalism in the Middle East.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','sputnik-launch',256,'{"id": "sputnik-launch", "name": "Sputnik Launched", "year": 1957, "categories": ["Technology", "Science", "Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["first satellite", "Soviet space", "Space Race begins", "Sputnik 1"], "description": "The Soviet Union launches Sputnik 1, the world''s first artificial satellite, into orbit around Earth, shocking the United States and inaugurating the Space Race. Sputnik''s beeping radio signal, audible to amateur radio operators worldwide, demonstrates Soviet technological capability and triggers massive investment in science and education.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','ghana-independence',257,'{"id": "ghana-independence", "name": "Ghana Gains Independence", "year": 1957, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Gold Coast independence", "Kwame Nkrumah", "first African independence", "Ghana Gold Coast"], "description": "Ghana becomes the first sub-Saharan African country to gain independence from European colonial rule, with Kwame Nkrumah becoming its first Prime Minister. Ghana''s independence inspires independence movements across the continent and marks the beginning of the end of European colonialism in Africa.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','mao-great-leap-forward',258,'{"id": "mao-great-leap-forward", "name": "Great Leap Forward in China", "year": 1958, "categories": ["Politics", "Social", "Disasters"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Mao industrialization", "China famine", "Steel furnaces China", "collective farming China"], "description": "Mao Zedong launches the Great Leap Forward, a disastrous campaign to rapidly transform China into a communist industrial state through forced collectivization and backyard steel production. The resulting famine kills between 15 and 55 million people, making it the deadliest famine in history.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','decolonization-africa',259,'{"id": "decolonization-africa", "name": "African Decolonization Wave", "year": 1960, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Year of Africa", "African independence", "colonialism ends Africa", "17 nations independence"], "description": "Seventeen African nations gain independence from European colonial powers in a single year, accelerating a broader wave of decolonization across the continent. The independence movements reshape the global political order, giving voice to newly sovereign nations in international forums like the United Nations.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','apartheid-sharpeville-massacre',260,'{"id": "apartheid-sharpeville-massacre", "name": "Sharpeville Massacre", "year": 1960, "categories": ["Politics", "Social", "Disasters"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["South Africa protest massacre", "pass laws protest", "anti-apartheid South Africa", "Sharpeville"], "description": "South African police open fire on a crowd of Black protesters demonstrating against the pass laws in Sharpeville, killing 69 people and wounding nearly 200. The massacre shocks the world, leads to international sanctions against South Africa, and transforms the anti-apartheid movement.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','contraceptive-pill-approved',261,'{"id": "contraceptive-pill-approved", "name": "Oral Contraceptive Pill Approved", "year": 1960, "categories": ["Science", "Social"], "region": "North America", "aliases": ["the Pill", "birth control pill", "contraceptive pill approved", "Enovid approved", "women''s liberation medicine", "sexual revolution begins"], "description": "The US Food and Drug Administration approves Enovid, the first oral contraceptive pill, developed from the research of Carl Djerassi and others, for contraceptive use. The Pill gives women unprecedented control over their reproductive choices, separating sex from reproduction in a way that transforms gender roles, family planning, and sexual norms across the developed world. It is widely regarded as one of the most socially transformative innovations of the twentieth century, directly enabling the women''s liberation movement of the 1960s.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 8}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','space-race-yuri-gagarin',262,'{"id": "space-race-yuri-gagarin", "name": "Yuri Gagarin Becomes First Human in Space", "year": 1961, "categories": ["Science", "Technology", "Exploration"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["first cosmonaut", "Soviet space triumph", "Vostok 1", "gagarin orbit"], "description": "Soviet cosmonaut Yuri Gagarin completes one orbit of Earth aboard Vostok 1, becoming the first human to travel into space. His flight shocks the United States, accelerates the Space Race, and makes Gagarin an international hero.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','india-china-war',263,'{"id": "india-china-war", "name": "India-China Border War", "year": 1962, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Sino-Indian War", "Himalayan war", "McMahon Line conflict", "China India war"], "description": "China launches a large-scale military offensive against India along their disputed Himalayan border, inflicting a humiliating defeat on Indian forces within a month before declaring a unilateral ceasefire. The conflict reshapes Indian defence policy and sours Sino-Indian relations for decades.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','cuban-missile-crisis',264,'{"id": "cuban-missile-crisis", "name": "Cuban Missile Crisis", "year": 1962, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["nuclear standoff Cuba", "Kennedy Khrushchev", "Soviet missiles Cuba", "nuclear war averted"], "description": "The United States discovers Soviet nuclear missiles in Cuba, leading to a tense thirteen-day standoff between President Kennedy and Premier Khrushchev that brings the world closer to nuclear war than at any other point. The crisis ends with Soviet withdrawal of missiles and becomes the defining moment of Cold War brinkmanship.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','south-korea-economic-miracle',265,'{"id": "south-korea-economic-miracle", "name": "South Korean Economic Miracle", "year": 1962, "categories": ["Politics", "Technology", "Social"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Han River miracle", "Korean industrialization", "chaebols South Korea", "Park Chung-hee development"], "description": "South Korea launches its first Five-Year Economic Development Plan under President Park Chung-hee, beginning a remarkable transformation from one of the world''s poorest countries into a major industrial power within a generation. The ''Miracle on the Han River'' becomes a model for rapid export-led development.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','martin-luther-king-speech',266,'{"id": "martin-luther-king-speech", "name": "Martin Luther King''s March on Washington", "year": 1963, "categories": ["Social", "Politics"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["I Have a Dream speech", "MLK Washington march", "civil rights march", "Lincoln Memorial speech"], "description": "Martin Luther King Jr. delivers his iconic ''I Have a Dream'' speech to 250,000 people at the Lincoln Memorial during the March on Washington for Jobs and Freedom. The speech becomes one of history''s most celebrated orations and galvanizes support for the Civil Rights Act.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','jfk-assassination',267,'{"id": "jfk-assassination", "name": "Assassination of President Kennedy", "year": 1963, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "North America", "aliases": ["JFK shot", "Kennedy assassination", "Dallas 1963", "Lee Harvey Oswald", "Dealey Plaza", "November 22 1963", "Camelot ends"], "description": "President John F. Kennedy is shot and killed while riding in a motorcade through Dealey Plaza in Dallas, Texas, on November 22. The Warren Commission concludes that Lee Harvey Oswald acted alone, though the assassination generates enduring conspiracy theories that have never fully been resolved. Kennedy''s death shocks the world and marks the end of a period of post-war American optimism, transforming American political culture and leaving an indelible mark on the collective memory of a generation.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 8}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','civil-rights-act-us',268,'{"id": "civil-rights-act-us", "name": "US Civil Rights Act", "year": 1964, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Martin Luther King", "racial equality US", "segregation ended", "Lyndon Johnson civil rights"], "description": "President Lyndon B. Johnson signs the Civil Rights Act into law, prohibiting discrimination based on race, color, religion, sex, or national origin in the United States. The landmark legislation, championed by the civil rights movement led by Martin Luther King Jr., dismantles the legal infrastructure of racial segregation.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','green-revolution-india',269,'{"id": "green-revolution-india", "name": "Green Revolution in India", "year": 1965, "categories": ["Science", "Technology", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["M.S. Swaminathan", "wheat revolution India", "food self-sufficiency India", "high-yield crops"], "description": "India undertakes the Green Revolution, introducing high-yielding crop varieties, chemical fertilizers, and irrigation technology that dramatically increases agricultural output. Led by scientists like M.S. Swaminathan, the program transforms India from a food-deficient nation to one capable of feeding itself.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','vietnam-war',270,'{"id": "vietnam-war", "name": "Vietnam War", "year": 1965, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["US Vietnam conflict", "Ho Chi Minh", "Gulf of Tonkin", "anti-war movement", "Tet Offensive"], "description": "The United States escalates military involvement in Vietnam to prevent a communist takeover of South Vietnam, committing ground troops in a conflict that lasts a decade. The war kills millions of Vietnamese and over 58,000 Americans, divides American society, and ends with the fall of Saigon and communist reunification of Vietnam.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','indo-pak-1965-war',271,'{"id": "indo-pak-1965-war", "name": "India-Pakistan War over Kashmir", "year": 1965, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Second Kashmir War", "Operation Gibraltar", "Tashkent Agreement", "India Pakistan 1965"], "description": "Pakistan launches Operation Gibraltar to infiltrate Jammu and Kashmir, triggering a full-scale war with India that ends in a stalemate and the Tashkent Declaration mediated by the Soviet Union. The war deepens the Kashmir dispute without resolving it.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','us-civil-rights-march-selma',272,'{"id": "us-civil-rights-march-selma", "name": "Selma to Montgomery Marches", "year": 1965, "categories": ["Social", "Politics"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Bloody Sunday Selma", "voting rights marches", "Edmund Pettus Bridge", "civil rights Alabama"], "description": "Civil rights marchers attempting to walk from Selma to Montgomery, Alabama, are violently beaten by police on the Edmund Pettus Bridge on Bloody Sunday, shocking the nation. The marches contribute directly to the passage of the Voting Rights Act, a cornerstone of American civil rights legislation.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','chinese-cultural-revolution',273,'{"id": "chinese-cultural-revolution", "name": "Chinese Cultural Revolution", "year": 1966, "categories": ["Politics", "Social", "Culture"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Mao Cultural Revolution", "Red Guards China", "Great Proletarian Cultural Revolution", "Chinese upheaval"], "description": "Mao Zedong launches the Cultural Revolution to reassert ideological purity and his personal authority, unleashing Red Guards who attack intellectuals, destroy cultural heritage, and purge party officials. The decade-long upheaval causes immense suffering and economic disruption, killing hundreds of thousands and sending millions to labor camps.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','six-day-war',274,'{"id": "six-day-war", "name": "Six-Day War", "year": 1967, "categories": ["War"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Arab-Israeli War 1967", "Israel captures West Bank", "June War", "Third Arab-Israeli War", "Sinai Golan Heights captured", "1967 Middle East war"], "description": "Israel launches preemptive air strikes against Egypt, Jordan, and Syria, destroying their air forces on the ground before seizing the Sinai Peninsula, Gaza Strip, West Bank, and Golan Heights in just six days of fighting. The swift and decisive Israeli victory reshapes the map of the Middle East, creating the territorial situation that defines the Israeli-Palestinian conflict to the present day. The war fundamentally alters the regional balance of power, deepens American and Soviet proxy rivalry in the Middle East, and makes the question of Palestinian statehood a central issue of international politics.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 8}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','moon-landing',275,'{"id": "moon-landing", "name": "Moon Landing", "year": 1969, "categories": ["Science", "Technology", "Exploration"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Apollo 11", "Neil Armstrong Moon", "one small step", "lunar landing", "NASA Moon mission"], "description": "NASA astronauts Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin become the first humans to walk on the Moon during the Apollo 11 mission, with Armstrong''s words ''one small step for man'' broadcast to a global audience. The achievement represents the culmination of the Space Race and a triumph of human exploration.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','bangladesh-liberation-war',276,'{"id": "bangladesh-liberation-war", "name": "Bangladesh Liberation War", "year": 1971, "categories": ["War", "Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Bangladesh independence", "Indo-Pakistan war 1971", "East Pakistan", "Mukti Bahini"], "description": "East Pakistan, supported by India, fights for and wins independence from Pakistan following a brutal military crackdown by the Pakistani army. The conflict results in massive atrocities, a refugee crisis, and the birth of Bangladesh as a new nation.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','world-wide-web-invention',277,'{"id": "world-wide-web-invention", "name": "First Email Sent", "year": 1971, "categories": ["Technology"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Ray Tomlinson email", "ARPANET email", "first electronic mail", "@ symbol email"], "description": "Ray Tomlinson sends the first networked email between two computers on ARPANET, using the @ symbol to distinguish the user from the host machine. This invention creates one of the world''s most widely used forms of communication, transforming business, personal communication, and the flow of information.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','oil-crisis-1973',278,'{"id": "oil-crisis-1973", "name": "Oil Crisis of the Middle East", "year": 1973, "categories": ["Politics", "Social", "Technology"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["OPEC oil embargo", "Arab oil embargo", "1973 energy crisis", "oil shock"], "description": "Arab members of OPEC impose an oil embargo on countries supporting Israel in the Yom Kippur War, causing oil prices to quadruple and triggering a global economic crisis. The shock reveals Western economies'' vulnerability to Middle Eastern oil and permanently accelerates interest in energy conservation and alternatives.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','khmer-rouge-cambodia',279,'{"id": "khmer-rouge-cambodia", "name": "Khmer Rouge Takes Power in Cambodia", "year": 1975, "categories": ["Politics", "War", "Social"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Pol Pot genocide", "Cambodian genocide", "Year Zero Cambodia", "killing fields"], "description": "The Khmer Rouge led by Pol Pot seizes power in Cambodia and launches a radical agrarian revolution, emptying cities and executing intellectuals, ethnic minorities, and perceived enemies. The resulting genocide kills an estimated 1.5 to 2 million people, roughly a quarter of Cambodia''s population.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','death-of-mao',280,'{"id": "death-of-mao", "name": "Death of Mao Zedong", "year": 1976, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Mao dies", "Mao Zedong death", "Gang of Four arrested", "post-Mao China", "Deng Xiaoping rise", "China after Mao", "end of Maoism"], "description": "Mao Zedong, the founder and supreme leader of the People''s Republic of China since 1949, dies after three decades of rule that included the Great Leap Forward, the Cultural Revolution, and China''s emergence as a nuclear power. His death triggers a brief power struggle ending in the arrest of the radical Gang of Four and the gradual rise of pragmatist Deng Xiaoping. Mao''s death is pivotal in world history, marking the beginning of China''s transformation from Maoist ideology toward the market-oriented reforms that make it the economic superpower of the twenty-first century.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 8}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','viking-1-mars',281,'{"id": "viking-1-mars", "name": "Viking 1 Lands on Mars", "year": 1976, "categories": ["Science", "Exploration"], "region": "World", "aliases": ["Mars landing 1976", "NASA Mars probe", "Viking Mars lander", "first Mars surface images", "search for life Mars", "Chryse Planitia landing"], "description": "NASA''s Viking 1 spacecraft successfully lands on the Chryse Planitia plain of Mars and transmits the first photographs taken from the surface of another planet, showing a rocky, reddish desert landscape under a salmon-colored sky. The lander conducts biological experiments designed to detect signs of microbial life in the Martian soil, producing ambiguous results that scientists continue to debate. Operating for over six years — far beyond its planned mission — Viking 1 represents humanity''s first sustained robotic presence on another world.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','tiananmen-one',282,'{"id": "tiananmen-one", "name": "Chinese Economic Reforms Begin", "year": 1978, "categories": ["Politics", "Social", "Technology"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Deng Xiaoping reforms", "socialist market economy", "China opens up", "Four Modernizations"], "description": "Deng Xiaoping consolidates power and launches sweeping economic reforms opening China to foreign investment and market forces while maintaining Communist Party political control. The reforms launch China''s extraordinary economic transformation from a poor agricultural nation into the world''s second-largest economy.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','iran-islamic-revolution',283,'{"id": "iran-islamic-revolution", "name": "Iranian Islamic Revolution", "year": 1979, "categories": ["Politics", "Religion", "Social"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Khomeini revolution", "Shah overthrown Iran", "Islamic Republic Iran", "Iranian revolution"], "description": "Ayatollah Khomeini leads a popular revolution that overthrows the US-backed Shah of Iran and establishes an Islamic Republic. The revolution reshapes Middle Eastern politics, triggers the Iran-Iraq War, and fundamentally alters US-Iran relations with repercussions that extend into the present day.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','thatcher-becomes-pm',284,'{"id": "thatcher-becomes-pm", "name": "Margaret Thatcher Becomes Prime Minister", "year": 1979, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Iron Lady", "first female PM Britain", "Thatcher government", "Thatcherism", "Conservative revolution 1979", "UK election 1979"], "description": "Margaret Thatcher becomes the United Kingdom''s first female Prime Minister following a decisive Conservative Party victory in the general election, beginning an eleven-year tenure that transforms British politics and economics. Thatcher dismantles much of Britain''s post-war consensus, privatizing state industries, curbing trade union power, and promoting free-market economic policies under the banner of Thatcherism. Her ideological alignment with Ronald Reagan''s parallel program in the United States defines the political economy of the English-speaking world in the 1980s and shifts the center of gravity of Western politics.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','smallpox-eradicated',285,'{"id": "smallpox-eradicated", "name": "Smallpox Eradicated Globally", "year": 1980, "categories": ["Medicine", "Science"], "region": "Global", "aliases": ["WHO smallpox", "disease eradication", "vaccination success", "variola defeated"], "description": "The World Health Organization officially declares smallpox eradicated, making it the first and to date only human infectious disease to be eliminated through a deliberate global vaccination campaign. The achievement represents one of public health''s greatest triumphs and saves millions of lives annually.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','iran-iraq-war',286,'{"id": "iran-iraq-war", "name": "Iran-Iraq War Begins", "year": 1980, "categories": ["War"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Gulf War first", "Saddam Hussein vs Iran", "Iraq invades Iran", "eight-year war Middle East", "1980 Persian Gulf", "chemical weapons war"], "description": "Iraq, led by Saddam Hussein, invades Iran in a dispute over the Shatt al-Arab waterway and in an attempt to exploit the instability created by Iran''s Islamic Revolution. The resulting war lasts eight years, kills between 500,000 and one million people, and ends in a stalemate with no significant territorial change for either side. The conflict devastates both economies, sees chemical weapons used on a large scale for the first time since World War One, and deepens the Sunni-Shia sectarian fault lines that define Middle Eastern geopolitics.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','aids-epidemic',287,'{"id": "aids-epidemic", "name": "AIDS Epidemic Identified", "year": 1981, "categories": ["Medicine", "Social", "Disasters"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["HIV AIDS crisis", "gay plague", "AIDS pandemic", "immune deficiency disease"], "description": "The US Centers for Disease Control identifies a mysterious immune deficiency syndrome among gay men, marking the official recognition of the AIDS epidemic. The disease goes on to kill over 35 million people worldwide and transforms global public health, sexuality politics, and medical research.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','falklands-war',288,'{"id": "falklands-war", "name": "Falklands War", "year": 1982, "categories": ["War"], "region": "South America", "aliases": ["Falklands conflict", "Argentina invades Falklands", "Malvinas War", "British Task Force South Atlantic", "Thatcher war Falklands", "1982 South Atlantic"], "description": "Argentina invades the British-controlled Falkland Islands in the South Atlantic, prompting Britain under Margaret Thatcher to dispatch a naval task force 13,000 kilometers to retake the remote archipelago. The brief but intense conflict ends in a decisive British military victory after ten weeks of fighting, costing over 900 lives on both sides. The war dramatically boosts Thatcher''s domestic political fortunes, contributes to the collapse of Argentina''s military junta, and reinforces the principle that territorial disputes should not be resolved by force.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','india-wins-cricket-world-cup',289,'{"id": "india-wins-cricket-world-cup", "name": "India Wins the Cricket World Cup", "year": 1983, "categories": ["Sports"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Kapil Dev World Cup", "Lords 1983", "West Indies vs India final", "India cricket champion"], "description": "Captained by Kapil Dev, India defeats the dominant West Indies in the Cricket World Cup final at Lord''s in one of the greatest sporting upsets ever. The victory sparks a revolution in Indian cricket and transforms the sport into the nation''s dominant cultural obsession.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','operation-blue-star',290,'{"id": "operation-blue-star", "name": "Operation Blue Star", "year": 1984, "categories": ["Politics", "War", "Religion"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Golden Temple operation", "Amritsar operation", "Punjab militancy", "Bhindranwale"], "description": "Indian military forces storm the Golden Temple in Amritsar to flush out Sikh militants led by Jarnail Singh Bhindranwale, causing heavy casualties among militants, soldiers, and civilians. The operation deeply wounds Sikh sentiments and has far-reaching political consequences.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','indira-gandhi-assassination',291,'{"id": "indira-gandhi-assassination", "name": "Assassination of Indira Gandhi", "year": 1984, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Indira Gandhi killed", "Sikh bodyguards assassination", "anti-Sikh riots", "PM assassination India"], "description": "Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi is assassinated by her own Sikh bodyguards in retaliation for Operation Blue Star. Her death triggers widespread anti-Sikh riots across India in which thousands of Sikhs are killed.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','bhopal-gas-tragedy',292,'{"id": "bhopal-gas-tragedy", "name": "Bhopal Gas Tragedy", "year": 1984, "categories": ["Disasters", "Technology"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Union Carbide disaster", "Bhopal chemical leak", "MIC gas leak", "worst industrial disaster"], "description": "A catastrophic leak of methyl isocyanate gas from a Union Carbide pesticide plant in Bhopal kills thousands of people immediately and leaves hundreds of thousands with lasting health effects. It remains the world''s worst industrial disaster and a landmark case in corporate accountability.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','ethiopian-famine',293,'{"id": "ethiopian-famine", "name": "Ethiopian Famine", "year": 1984, "categories": ["Disasters", "Social"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Africa famine 1984", "Band Aid", "Live Aid concert", "Ethiopia hunger crisis"], "description": "A catastrophic famine kills an estimated one million people in Ethiopia amid civil war and drought, shocking the world through television images and inspiring the Band Aid charity record and Live Aid concerts. The crisis raises awareness of African poverty and stimulates unprecedented international humanitarian aid.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','gorbachev-becomes-leader',294,'{"id": "gorbachev-becomes-leader", "name": "Gorbachev Becomes Soviet Leader", "year": 1985, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Gorbachev", "glasnost perestroika", "Soviet reform begins", "Chernenko dies Gorbachev", "USSR reform", "Cold War thaw 1985"], "description": "Mikhail Gorbachev becomes General Secretary of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union following the death of Konstantin Chernenko, becoming at 54 the youngest Soviet leader since Stalin. His policies of glasnost (openness) and perestroika (restructuring) are intended to revitalize the stagnating Soviet system but instead unleash forces far beyond his control, leading to the fall of communist governments across Eastern Europe in 1989 and ultimately the dissolution of the Soviet Union itself in 1991. Gorbachev''s accession is one of the pivotal moments of the Cold War.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 8}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','chernobyl-disaster',295,'{"id": "chernobyl-disaster", "name": "Chernobyl Nuclear Disaster", "year": 1986, "categories": ["Disasters", "Technology"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Chernobyl explosion", "Soviet nuclear accident", "Ukraine reactor", "nuclear meltdown"], "description": "A reactor at the Chernobyl nuclear power plant in Soviet Ukraine explodes and catches fire, releasing radioactive contamination across much of Europe in the worst nuclear accident in history. The disaster kills dozens directly and exposes millions to radiation, accelerates the decline of the Soviet Union, and reshapes global attitudes toward nuclear power.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','sachin-tendulkar-debut',296,'{"id": "sachin-tendulkar-debut", "name": "Sachin Tendulkar''s International Debut", "year": 1989, "categories": ["Sports"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Little Master debut", "Tendulkar cricket", "youngest India cricketer", "God of cricket begins"], "description": "A sixteen-year-old Sachin Tendulkar makes his Test cricket debut against Pakistan, showing remarkable composure in facing fearsome bowling. He goes on to become the highest run-scorer in both Test and One Day International cricket and is widely regarded as the greatest batsman of his era.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','berlin-wall-falls',297,'{"id": "berlin-wall-falls", "name": "Berlin Wall Falls", "year": 1989, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["German reunification", "Cold War ends", "East West Berlin", "Mauerfall"], "description": "The East German government opens its borders, leading jubilant crowds to tear down the Berlin Wall that has divided the city since 1961. The event symbolizes the collapse of communism in Eastern Europe and leads directly to German reunification and the end of the Cold War.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','tiananmen-square',298,'{"id": "tiananmen-square", "name": "Tiananmen Square Protests", "year": 1989, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Beijing student protests", "Tank Man", "June Fourth Incident", "China democracy movement"], "description": "Pro-democracy protesters gather in Tiananmen Square in Beijing for weeks before the Chinese government declares martial law and sends in the military, killing hundreds or possibly thousands in a violent crackdown. The image of a lone man standing before a column of tanks becomes one of the most iconic photographs of the modern era.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','mandela-freed',299,'{"id": "mandela-freed", "name": "Nelson Mandela Released from Prison", "year": 1990, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Mandela release", "Robben Island", "ANC leader freed", "end apartheid begins"], "description": "Nelson Mandela is released from Robben Island prison after twenty-seven years of incarceration for his anti-apartheid activism, greeted by massive global celebrations. His release marks the beginning of negotiations to end apartheid and ultimately leads to South Africa''s first fully democratic elections in 1994.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','economic-liberalization-india',300,'{"id": "economic-liberalization-india", "name": "Economic Liberalization of India", "year": 1991, "categories": ["Politics", "Social", "Technology"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["LPG reforms India", "Manmohan Singh reforms", "India opens economy", "1991 crisis reforms"], "description": "Facing a severe balance-of-payments crisis, Finance Minister Manmohan Singh introduces sweeping economic reforms that liberalize, privatize, and globalize the Indian economy. The reforms dismantle the ''License Raj'' and launch India onto a path of rapid economic growth.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','rajiv-gandhi-assassination',301,'{"id": "rajiv-gandhi-assassination", "name": "Assassination of Rajiv Gandhi", "year": 1991, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Rajiv Gandhi killed", "LTTE assassination", "Tamil Tigers India PM", "suicide bombing India"], "description": "Former Indian Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi is assassinated by a suicide bomber linked to the Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam during an election campaign rally in Tamil Nadu. His killing is motivated by India''s military intervention in Sri Lanka''s civil war.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','dissolution-soviet-union',302,'{"id": "dissolution-soviet-union", "name": "Dissolution of the Soviet Union", "year": 1991, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["USSR collapse", "Soviet Union breaks up", "Gorbachev resign", "Cold War end", "15 republics independence"], "description": "The Soviet Union formally dissolves into fifteen independent republics on December 25th, with Mikhail Gorbachev resigning as president. The collapse ends the Cold War and fundamentally reshapes the global political order, leaving the United States as the world''s sole superpower.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','internet-invented',303,'{"id": "internet-invented", "name": "World Wide Web Invented", "year": 1991, "categories": ["Technology", "Culture", "Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["Tim Berners-Lee web", "HTTP HTML", "CERN internet", "WWW created"], "description": "Tim Berners-Lee at CERN makes the World Wide Web publicly available, creating the system of linked hypertext documents that makes the internet accessible to ordinary users. The web transforms commerce, communication, entertainment, and virtually every aspect of modern civilization.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','babri-masjid-demolition',304,'{"id": "babri-masjid-demolition", "name": "Demolition of the Babri Masjid", "year": 1992, "categories": ["Religion", "Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Ayodhya dispute", "Ram Janmabhoomi", "Hindu Muslim riot", "kar sevaks"], "description": "A crowd of Hindu activists demolishes the Babri Masjid mosque in Ayodhya, claiming the site as the birthplace of Lord Ram. The event triggers widespread Hindu-Muslim riots across India, killing thousands, and sets off a decades-long legal battle culminating in a Supreme Court verdict.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','rwandan-genocide',305,'{"id": "rwandan-genocide", "name": "Rwandan Genocide", "year": 1994, "categories": ["War", "Social", "Politics"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Tutsi genocide", "Hutu Tutsi conflict", "100 days genocide", "Rwanda massacre"], "description": "Hutu extremists in Rwanda systematically murder an estimated 500,000 to 800,000 Tutsi and moderate Hutu in approximately 100 days, one of history''s fastest genocides. The international community''s failure to intervene becomes a defining moral failure and leads to reforms in international humanitarian law.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','independence-south-africa',306,'{"id": "independence-south-africa", "name": "Nelson Mandela Becomes South Africa''s President", "year": 1994, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["South Africa democracy", "ANC election victory", "end of apartheid", "Rainbow Nation", "first Black president SA"], "description": "Nelson Mandela is elected the first Black President of South Africa in the country''s first fully democratic election, marking the official end of the apartheid system. His presidency symbolizes reconciliation and moral leadership, inspiring people around the world in the struggle against racial injustice.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','collapse-apartheid-negotiations',307,'{"id": "collapse-apartheid-negotiations", "name": "South Africa''s First Democratic Election", "year": 1994, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Africa", "aliases": ["Mandela elected", "ANC wins", "end apartheid vote", "multiracial election South Africa"], "description": "South Africa holds its first fully democratic election in which all races can vote, resulting in a historic victory for Nelson Mandela and the African National Congress. The peaceful transition from apartheid to democracy becomes a model for conflict resolution and national reconciliation.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','amazon-founded',308,'{"id": "amazon-founded", "name": "Amazon Founded", "year": 1994, "categories": ["Technology", "Culture"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Jeff Bezos Amazon", "online bookstore", "e-commerce revolution", "internet retail"], "description": "Jeff Bezos founds Amazon as an online bookstore from his garage in Seattle, launching what will become the world''s largest online retailer and cloud computing provider. Amazon transforms global retail, logistics, and cloud computing while making Bezos one of the wealthiest individuals in history.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','wto-founded',309,'{"id": "wto-founded", "name": "World Trade Organization Founded", "year": 1995, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "World", "aliases": ["WTO", "World Trade Organization", "GATT successor", "global trade rules", "free trade institution", "1995 globalization"], "description": "The World Trade Organization comes into being on January 1, replacing the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade with a permanent institution equipped with binding dispute settlement mechanisms and a mandate to negotiate further trade liberalization. With 123 founding members, the WTO creates the legal framework governing the majority of world trade and becomes the central institution of economic globalization. Its establishment marks the high point of the post-Cold War liberal international order, though it subsequently becomes a focal point of protests against inequality and a target of nationalist backlash.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','dolly-sheep-cloned',310,'{"id": "dolly-sheep-cloned", "name": "Dolly the Sheep Cloned", "year": 1996, "categories": ["Science"], "region": "Europe", "aliases": ["first mammal cloned", "Dolly cloning", "Roslin Institute", "somatic cell nuclear transfer", "cloning breakthrough 1996", "Ian Wilmut sheep"], "description": "Scientists at the Roslin Institute in Edinburgh successfully clone Dolly the sheep from a single adult mammary cell, making her the first mammal ever cloned from an adult somatic cell rather than an embryo. The achievement overturns decades of biological assumptions about cell differentiation and demonstrates that the DNA of a fully specialized adult cell retains the information needed to produce a complete organism. Dolly''s creation ignites intense ethical debate about human cloning and accelerates research into stem cells, regenerative medicine, and the fundamental mechanisms of genetics.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','taliban-capture-kabul',311,'{"id": "taliban-capture-kabul", "name": "Taliban Capture Kabul", "year": 1996, "categories": ["Politics", "War"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Taliban Afghanistan", "Afghan civil war Taliban", "Islamic Emirate of Afghanistan", "Najibullah executed", "Kabul falls 1996", "Afghanistan Taliban rule"], "description": "The Taliban, a fundamentalist Islamist movement that emerged from the Afghan refugee camps of Pakistan, captures the Afghan capital Kabul, executing the former communist president Najibullah and imposing a strict interpretation of Islamic law across the territory they control. Under Taliban rule, women are barred from education and employment, and cultural sites are destroyed, drawing international condemnation. The Taliban government harbors al-Qaeda, setting the conditions for the September 11 attacks and the subsequent US-led invasion of Afghanistan in 2001.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 6}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','hong-kong-handover',312,'{"id": "hong-kong-handover", "name": "Hong Kong Handed Back to China", "year": 1997, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "East Asia", "aliases": ["Hong Kong 1997", "British Hong Kong ends", "one country two systems", "handover ceremony July 1997", "Chris Patten last governor", "Deng Xiaoping Hong Kong deal"], "description": "The United Kingdom transfers sovereignty over Hong Kong to the People''s Republic of China on July 1, ending 156 years of British colonial rule over the territory. Under the principle of ''one country, two systems'' negotiated by Deng Xiaoping and Margaret Thatcher, Hong Kong is to retain its capitalist economy, independent judiciary, and civil liberties for fifty years. The handover marks the symbolic end of the British Empire''s presence in Asia and is a defining moment in China''s national narrative of recovering territories lost during what it calls the ''century of humiliation.''", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 7}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','pokhran-nuclear-tests',313,'{"id": "pokhran-nuclear-tests", "name": "Pokhran Nuclear Tests", "year": 1998, "categories": ["Technology", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Operation Shakti", "India nuclear bomb", "Vajpayee nuclear test", "India joins nuclear club"], "description": "India conducts a series of nuclear tests in the Pokhran desert in Rajasthan, declaring itself a nuclear weapon state. The tests, code-named Operation Shakti, trigger international sanctions but mark India''s entry into the exclusive club of declared nuclear powers.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','google-founded',314,'{"id": "google-founded", "name": "Google Founded", "year": 1998, "categories": ["Technology"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Page Brin Google", "search engine Google", "internet company", "Silicon Valley startup"], "description": "Larry Page and Sergey Brin found Google, launching a search engine that organizes the world''s information through its revolutionary PageRank algorithm. Google grows into one of the most powerful technology companies in history, transforming advertising, information access, and the digital economy.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','space-station-iss',315,'{"id": "space-station-iss", "name": "International Space Station Construction Begins", "year": 1998, "categories": ["Science", "Technology"], "region": "Global", "aliases": ["ISS construction", "orbital station", "space station assembly", "international cooperation space"], "description": "The first module of the International Space Station is launched, beginning the construction of the largest human-made structure ever placed in orbit. A symbol of post-Cold War cooperation, the ISS involves the US, Russia, Europe, Japan, and Canada in continuous human presence in space.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','kargil-war',316,'{"id": "kargil-war", "name": "Kargil War", "year": 1999, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["India Pakistan Kargil", "Operation Vijay", "Line of Control conflict", "Kargil conflict"], "description": "Pakistani soldiers and militants infiltrate the Kargil sector of Jammu and Kashmir, leading to intense high-altitude combat between Indian and Pakistani forces. India successfully recaptures most positions in Operation Vijay, and the conflict remains the only direct war between two nuclear-armed states.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','gujarat-earthquake',317,'{"id": "gujarat-earthquake", "name": "Gujarat Earthquake", "year": 2001, "categories": ["Disasters"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Bhuj earthquake", "India earthquake 2001", "Gujarat quake", "Kutch earthquake"], "description": "A powerful earthquake measuring 7.7 magnitude strikes the Bhuj region of Gujarat on Republic Day, killing around 20,000 people and injuring 167,000. It is one of the deadliest earthquakes in India''s recorded history and causes widespread destruction across the Kutch region.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','september-11-attacks',318,'{"id": "september-11-attacks", "name": "September Eleventh Attacks", "year": 2001, "categories": ["War", "Politics", "Disasters"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["9/11", "Twin Towers attack", "Al-Qaeda attacks", "Pentagon attack", "World Trade Center"], "description": "Al-Qaeda terrorists hijack four commercial aircraft, flying two into the World Trade Center in New York, one into the Pentagon, and one crashes in Pennsylvania, killing nearly 3,000 people. The attacks trigger the US War on Terror, reshape global security policy, and fundamentally alter geopolitics.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','brahmos-missile-india',319,'{"id": "brahmos-missile-india", "name": "BrahMos Missile Developed", "year": 2001, "categories": ["Technology", "War"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["India Russia missile", "supersonic cruise missile", "BrahMos joint venture", "Indian defense technology"], "description": "India and Russia jointly develop and deploy the BrahMos, the world''s fastest supersonic cruise missile, representing a landmark in India''s defense technology capabilities. The missile, named after the Brahmaputra and Moskva rivers, becomes a cornerstone of Indian military modernization.", "difficulty": "hard", "importance": 2}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','human-genome-project',320,'{"id": "human-genome-project", "name": "Human Genome Project Completed", "year": 2003, "categories": ["Science", "Medicine", "Technology"], "region": "Global", "aliases": ["genome sequencing", "DNA mapping human", "genomics revolution", "HGP completion"], "description": "An international consortium completes the mapping of the entire human genome, identifying the approximately 20,000-25,000 genes that make up human DNA. The achievement revolutionizes medicine, enabling new approaches to disease diagnosis, treatment, and prevention based on genetic information.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','space-shuttle-columbia',321,'{"id": "space-shuttle-columbia", "name": "Space Shuttle Columbia Disaster", "year": 2003, "categories": ["Disasters", "Technology", "Science"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Columbia accident", "shuttle disintegration", "NASA tragedy", "foam strike disaster"], "description": "The Space Shuttle Columbia disintegrates upon reentry into Earth''s atmosphere, killing all seven crew members including India-born astronaut Kalpana Chawla. The accident grounds the shuttle fleet and leads to a comprehensive review of NASA''s safety culture and the eventual retirement of the shuttle program.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','indian-ocean-tsunami-india',322,'{"id": "indian-ocean-tsunami-india", "name": "Indian Ocean Tsunami Strikes India", "year": 2004, "categories": ["Disasters"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["2004 tsunami India", "Boxing Day tsunami", "Tamil Nadu tsunami", "Andaman tsunami"], "description": "A massive undersea earthquake off Sumatra triggers a devastating tsunami that strikes Indian coastal regions, killing over 10,000 people in Tamil Nadu, Andhra Pradesh, Kerala, and the Andaman Islands. The disaster prompts major improvements in early warning systems across the Indian Ocean.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','iphone-launched',323,'{"id": "iphone-launched", "name": "iPhone Launched", "year": 2007, "categories": ["Technology", "Culture"], "region": "Americas", "aliases": ["Steve Jobs iPhone", "Apple smartphone", "touchscreen phone", "mobile revolution"], "description": "Apple''s Steve Jobs unveils the iPhone, a revolutionary device combining a phone, music player, and internet communicator in a touchscreen package. The smartphone fundamentally transforms communication, commerce, entertainment, and social interaction, spawning a new era of mobile computing.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','chandrayaan-1-launched',324,'{"id": "chandrayaan-1-launched", "name": "Chandrayaan-1 Launched", "year": 2008, "categories": ["Science", "Technology"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["India Moon mission", "ISRO lunar probe", "Moon Impact Probe", "water on Moon India"], "description": "India launches Chandrayaan-1, its first lunar probe, marking a major milestone in the nation''s space program. The mission discovers evidence of water molecules on the lunar surface, a significant scientific finding that reshapes understanding of the Moon.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','mumbai-terrorist-attacks',325,'{"id": "mumbai-terrorist-attacks", "name": "Mumbai Terrorist Attacks", "year": 2008, "categories": ["War", "Politics", "Disasters"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["26/11 attacks", "Taj Hotel attack", "Lashkar-e-Taiba Mumbai", "Ajmal Kasab"], "description": "Pakistani Lashkar-e-Taiba militants carry out a series of coordinated terrorist attacks across Mumbai, targeting the Taj Mahal Palace Hotel, Chhatrapati Shivaji Terminus, and other locations. The three-day siege kills over 160 people and severely strains India-Pakistan relations.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','global-financial-crisis',326,'{"id": "global-financial-crisis", "name": "Global Financial Crisis", "year": 2008, "categories": ["Social", "Politics", "Technology"], "region": "Global", "aliases": ["Lehman Brothers collapse", "2008 recession", "subprime mortgage crisis", "Wall Street crash 2008"], "description": "The collapse of investment bank Lehman Brothers triggers a global financial crisis that causes the worst economic recession since the Great Depression, wiping out trillions in wealth and causing widespread unemployment worldwide. The crisis reshapes global regulation, exposes deep systemic risks in financial markets, and fuels political populism.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','arab-spring',327,'{"id": "arab-spring", "name": "Arab Spring", "year": 2011, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["Arab revolution", "Tunisia revolution", "Egypt uprising", "Mohamed Bouazizi", "Jasmine Revolution"], "description": "A wave of pro-democracy protests and uprisings sweeps across the Arab world, beginning in Tunisia and spreading to Egypt, Libya, Syria, Bahrain, and Yemen. While some countries experience democratic transitions, others descend into civil war, and the movement''s legacy remains deeply contested.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','osama-bin-laden-killed',328,'{"id": "osama-bin-laden-killed", "name": "Osama bin Laden Killed", "year": 2011, "categories": ["War", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["bin Laden death", "US Navy SEALs Pakistan", "Abbottabad raid", "Operation Neptune Spear"], "description": "US Navy SEALs kill Osama bin Laden in a raid on his compound in Abbottabad, Pakistan, a decade after the September 11 attacks. His death is a symbolic milestone in the US War on Terror though it does not end global jihadist terrorism.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','nirbhaya-case-protests',329,'{"id": "nirbhaya-case-protests", "name": "Nirbhaya Rape Case and Protests", "year": 2012, "categories": ["Social", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Delhi gang rape protests", "December 2012 protests", "India rape protest", "women safety India"], "description": "The brutal gang rape and murder of a young woman on a Delhi bus sparks massive nationwide protests against sexual violence and demands for stronger laws protecting women. The case leads to significant reforms in Indian rape law and raises global awareness about gender-based violence in India.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','mangalyaan-mars-mission',330,'{"id": "mangalyaan-mars-mission", "name": "Mangalyaan Mars Mission", "year": 2013, "categories": ["Science", "Technology"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Mars Orbiter Mission", "ISRO Mars", "India Mars mission", "MOM spacecraft"], "description": "India launches the Mars Orbiter Mission, making it the first Asian nation to reach Mars and the first in the world to do so on its maiden attempt. The mission is completed at a remarkably low cost, demonstrating ISRO''s capability for frugal and efficient space exploration.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','modi-elected-pm',331,'{"id": "modi-elected-pm", "name": "Narendra Modi Elected as Prime Minister", "year": 2014, "categories": ["Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["BJP landslide 2014", "NDA government", "Modi government", "Hindu nationalism politics"], "description": "Narendra Modi of the Bharatiya Janata Party wins a sweeping parliamentary majority, becoming Prime Minister of India with the largest mandate in thirty years. His election is seen as a major shift in Indian politics toward Hindu nationalist governance and pro-business economic reforms.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','islamic-state-rise',332,'{"id": "islamic-state-rise", "name": "Islamic State Declares Caliphate", "year": 2014, "categories": ["War", "Religion", "Politics"], "region": "Middle East", "aliases": ["ISIS caliphate", "ISIL declaration", "Abu Bakr al-Baghdadi", "Syria Iraq ISIS"], "description": "The Islamic State (ISIS) declares a caliphate spanning territory across Iraq and Syria, controlling millions of people and shocking the world with its extreme violence and sophisticated propaganda. The group''s rise triggers an international military coalition and a refugee crisis affecting millions.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','malala-nobel-peace-prize',333,'{"id": "malala-nobel-peace-prize", "name": "Malala Yousafzai Wins Nobel Peace Prize", "year": 2014, "categories": ["Social", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Malala Nobel", "Pakistan girl education", "Taliban shooting survivor", "youngest Nobel laureate"], "description": "Pakistani activist Malala Yousafzai, who survived a Taliban assassination attempt for her advocacy of girls'' education, becomes the youngest person ever to receive the Nobel Peace Prize. Her story inspires global attention to gender disparities in education in conflict zones.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','paris-climate-agreement',334,'{"id": "paris-climate-agreement", "name": "Paris Climate Agreement Signed", "year": 2015, "categories": ["Politics", "Science"], "region": "Global", "aliases": ["COP21 Paris", "climate accord", "global warming treaty", "carbon reduction agreement"], "description": "Nearly every nation signs the Paris Agreement committing to limit global warming to well below 2°C above pre-industrial levels and pursue efforts to limit warming to 1.5°C. The landmark accord represents the first universal commitment to addressing climate change but faces implementation challenges.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','demonetization-india',335,'{"id": "demonetization-india", "name": "Demonetization in India", "year": 2016, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["note ban India", "500 1000 rupee notes banned", "Modi demonetization", "cashless economy India"], "description": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi announces the sudden withdrawal of all 500 and 1000 rupee banknotes, declaring them invalid overnight in a move aimed at curbing black money and corruption. The decision causes widespread disruption and long queues at banks while remaining highly controversial in its economic impact.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','gst-implemented-india',336,'{"id": "gst-implemented-india", "name": "GST Implemented in India", "year": 2017, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["Goods and Services Tax India", "one nation one tax", "Indian tax reform", "GST rollout"], "description": "India replaces a complex web of central and state taxes with a unified Goods and Services Tax, the most ambitious tax reform since independence. The GST aims to create a single national market and reduce tax evasion, though its implementation causes initial disruption for businesses.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','chandrayaan-2-launched',337,'{"id": "chandrayaan-2-launched", "name": "Chandrayaan-2 Launched", "year": 2019, "categories": ["Science", "Technology"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["India Moon mission 2", "Vikram lander", "Pragyan rover", "ISRO lunar mission"], "description": "India launches Chandrayaan-2 with an orbiter, lander, and rover aimed at the lunar south pole. Though the Vikram lander crashes during descent, the orbiter continues to function and provides valuable data, keeping alive India''s ambitions for a soft lunar landing.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','caa-protests-india',338,'{"id": "caa-protests-india", "name": "Citizenship Amendment Act Protests", "year": 2019, "categories": ["Politics", "Social"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["CAA protests", "NRC protests India", "Shaheen Bagh", "anti-CAA movement"], "description": "India passes the Citizenship Amendment Act granting citizenship to non-Muslim refugees from three neighboring countries, sparking widespread protests over fears of religious discrimination. The demonstrations, including the prolonged Shaheen Bagh sit-in led by Muslim women, become the largest civil protest movement in years.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 3}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','black-holes-confirmed',339,'{"id": "black-holes-confirmed", "name": "First Black Hole Image Captured", "year": 2019, "categories": ["Science", "Technology"], "region": "Global", "aliases": ["Event Horizon Telescope", "M87 black hole", "black hole photograph", "astrophysics breakthrough"], "description": "The Event Horizon Telescope Collaboration releases the first direct image of a black hole''s event horizon in galaxy M87, providing visual confirmation of one of physics'' most extraordinary theoretical predictions. The image, produced by linking radio telescopes across the globe, marks a triumph of international scientific cooperation.", "difficulty": "medium", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','covid-lockdown-india',340,'{"id": "covid-lockdown-india", "name": "COVID Lockdown in India", "year": 2020, "categories": ["Disasters", "Social", "Politics"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["India COVID lockdown", "coronavirus India", "pandemic lockdown India", "migrant crisis COVID"], "description": "Prime Minister Modi announces a sudden nationwide lockdown within hours notice to contain the COVID-19 pandemic, triggering a massive humanitarian crisis as millions of migrant workers attempt to walk home to their villages. India endures one of the world''s strictest lockdowns while managing the economic and public health fallout.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 4}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','covid-19-pandemic',341,'{"id": "covid-19-pandemic", "name": "COVID-19 Global Pandemic", "year": 2020, "categories": ["Disasters", "Medicine", "Science"], "region": "Global", "aliases": ["coronavirus pandemic", "COVID pandemic", "SARS-CoV-2", "pandemic lockdown", "vaccine rollout"], "description": "A novel coronavirus identified in Wuhan, China spreads globally to become a devastating pandemic that kills millions, halts economies, and transforms daily life worldwide. The crisis accelerates vaccine development using mRNA technology and triggers profound debates about public health, inequality, and global preparedness.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
INSERT INTO "import_records" VALUES('events.json','chandrayaan-3-lunar-landing',342,'{"id": "chandrayaan-3-lunar-landing", "name": "Chandrayaan-3 Lunar Landing", "year": 2023, "categories": ["Science", "Technology"], "region": "South Asia", "aliases": ["India Moon landing", "Vikram lander 2023", "Pragyan rover 2023", "ISRO south pole landing"], "description": "India''s Chandrayaan-3 successfully lands near the lunar south pole, making India the fourth country to achieve a soft lunar landing and the first to land near the south pole. The mission discovers evidence of sulfur and other elements in the lunar soil, generating major scientific interest.", "difficulty": "easy", "importance": 5}');
