INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(1,1,0,'Five years after the Revolution: The French Revolution begins in 1789 with the Storming of the Bastille. The slogan Liberté, égalité, fraternité was proclaimed — and five years later, in 1794, the National Convention extended it to enslaved populations in French territories.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(2,1,1,'Haitian Revolution trigger: The major slave revolt in Saint-Domingue began in 1791. It took 3 years of intense fighting on the island before Paris formally ratified full emancipation in 1794. The sequence: 1789 → 1791 → 1794.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(3,2,0,'1794 is the height of the Reign of Terror — Robespierre is executed that same July. The National Convention was in its most radical phase, the same political energy that pushed through abolition.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(4,2,1,'Toussaint Louverture, the future leader of Haiti, was already a rising military commander in Saint-Domingue by 1794 — the same year France''s decree legally caught up to the revolution already underway on the ground.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(5,3,0,'Napoleon reverses the decree in 1802 — just eight years later. A short-lived window of legal freedom under French law: 1794 to 1802.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(6,3,1,'Haiti declares full independence in 1804, ten years after France''s abolition decree — a straight line from legal emancipation to the colony''s break from France.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(7,3,2,'France was the first major European colonial power to abolish slavery in 1794. Britain followed: subtract 13 years to reach the abolition of the British slave trade in 1807, or 40 years to reach Britain''s full abolition of slavery in 1834.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(8,4,0,'Count forward from Hertz: Heinrich Hertz proved electromagnetic waves exist in 1887–88. Marconi turns that pure theory into a practical device about 7-8 years later, in 1895.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(9,4,1,'Sequential Tech Link: Hertz (1887) → Marconi (1895). Eight years from ''waves exist'' to ''send a message with them.''','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(10,5,0,'1895 was the birth year of two mass-communication technologies: wireless radio (Marconi) and cinema (Lumière brothers). Both born the same year.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(11,5,1,'The ''1-8-9-5'' bridge trick: Röntgen also discovered X-rays in 1895. Pair ''invisible waves'' (X-rays) with ''invisible signals'' (radio) — both in 1895.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(12,6,0,'Turn of the Century Anchor: 1895 = exactly 5 years before 1900. A late-Victorian invention, not a 1930s one.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(13,6,1,'Marconi → Atlantic → 1901: 1895 = local demo. Six years later, 1901 = transatlantic signal.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(14,6,2,'Titanic anchor: Wireless saved survivors in 1912. Subtract ~17 years → 1895, when the technology was first demonstrated.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(15,7,0,'Northern Kingdom anchor: The Kingdom of Israel (the North) fell to the Assyrians in 722 BCE. Judah (the South) survived for another 134 years before Jerusalem fell to Nebuchadnezzar II in 588–586 BCE.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(16,7,1,'Nebuchadnezzar II becomes king of Babylon in 605 BCE, the same year he crushes Egypt at Carchemish. Jerusalem''s conquest follows about 17 years into his reign, in 588 BCE.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(17,7,2,'Count forward from the first deportation: Babylon exiles King Jehoiachin and part of Jerusalem''s elite in 597 BCE. The final conquest and the Temple''s destruction come about nine years later, in 588 BCE.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(18,8,0,'588 BCE comes just one generation after Babylon itself broke free of Assyrian rule in 626 BCE — the new Babylonian Empire wasted little time turning to conquer its neighbors.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(19,8,1,'Greek philosopher Thales of Miletus predicts a solar eclipse around 585 BCE, just three years after Jerusalem''s fall — a useful cross-check if you know early Greek science dates.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(20,9,0,'Cyrus the Great conquers Babylon in 539 BCE, ending the exile. Subtract 49 years from that to land on 588 BCE, when the exile began.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(21,9,1,'Second Temple bookend: Solomon''s First Temple was destroyed by Babylon in 588/586 BCE. The Second Temple was destroyed by the Romans in 70 CE — over 650 years later.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(22,10,0,'Count forward from the English Civil War: fighting between King Charles I and Parliament breaks out in 1642. Seven years of war and political maneuvering later, the king is tried and executed in 1649. Think: seven years from civil war to regicide.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(23,10,1,'The Mayflower sails for the New World in 1620. Charles I is executed 29 years later, in 1649 — roughly one generation after the Pilgrims left England.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(24,11,0,'1649 falls almost exactly at the midpoint of the 17th century — a king beheaded just one year shy of the century''s halfway mark.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(25,11,1,'England abolishes the monarchy and declares itself a Commonwealth in the same year, 1649 — the execution and the birth of the republic happen together.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(26,12,0,'Restoration anchor: Charles I was executed in 1649, and the monarchy returned just 11 years later in 1660 when Charles II was restored to the throne. Think: ''Charles dies → 11 years → Charles returns.''','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(27,12,1,'The Glorious Revolution came 39 years after Charles I''s execution, in 1688. The long struggle over the power of Crown and Parliament continued from 1649 toward the constitutional settlement of 1688.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(28,12,2,'French Revolution comparison: The execution of Charles I in 1649 predates the execution of Louis XVI of France in 1793 by 144 years — England set the precedent for regicide long before France followed.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(29,13,0,'1642 — Charles I raises his standard at Nottingham; the English Civil War begins','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(30,13,1,'1645 — New Model Army formed; decisive Parliamentarian victory at the Battle of Naseby breaks Royalist power','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(31,13,2,'1646 — Charles surrenders to the Scottish army, who hand him to Parliament the following year','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(32,13,3,'1648 — Second Civil War; Pride''s Purge removes moderate MPs, leaving the ''Rump Parliament'' that will try the king','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(33,13,4,'Jan 30, 1649 — Charles I tried, convicted of treason, and beheaded outside the Banqueting House in London','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(34,14,0,'Magna Carta anchor: Magna Carta was sealed in 1215. Bannockburn came 99 years later, in 1314 — almost exactly a century from Magna Carta to Scotland''s great victory over England.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(35,14,1,'William Wallace wins the Battle of Stirling Bridge in 1297, near the same ground. Bannockburn comes 17 years later, in 1314, finishing what Wallace started.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(36,14,2,'Edward I, the ''Hammer of the Scots,'' dies in 1307. Just seven years after his death, his son Edward II suffers the humiliating defeat at Bannockburn in 1314.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(37,15,0,'The Knights Templar are dissolved and their last Grand Master burned at the stake in 1314 — the same year, on the other side of Europe, Robert the Bruce was securing Scotland''s independence.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(38,15,1,'1314 sits early in the fourteenth century, a full generation before the Black Death reaches Europe in 1347 — a useful anchor if you know the plague date.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(39,16,0,'Declaration of Arbroath anchor: Scotland sent the famous Declaration of Arbroath to the Pope asserting independence in 1320 — just 6 years after the military triumph at Bannockburn in 1314.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(40,16,1,'Treaty of Edinburgh-Northampton anchor: England formally recognized Scottish independence in 1328, 14 years after Bannockburn. Subtract 14 from 1328 to land on 1314.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(41,16,2,'The Hundred Years'' War between England and France breaks out in 1337, just 23 years after Bannockburn — England was still nursing its Scottish defeat when it turned to fight France next.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(42,17,0,'The Bay of Pigs invasion fails in 1961 — a botched US attempt to overthrow Castro. Just one year later, in 1962, Soviet missiles show up in Cuba, a direct consequence of Castro turning to Moscow for protection after the invasion.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(43,17,1,'The Berlin Wall goes up in August 1961. About a year later, in October 1962, Cold War tension peaks again with missiles in Cuba — two back-to-back Cold War flashpoints.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(44,18,0,'John Glenn becomes the first American to orbit Earth in February 1962, the same year the Cuban Missile Crisis unfolds in October — space-race triumph and nuclear near-disaster in the same year.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(45,18,1,'The crisis lasted thirteen days in October 1962. The number 13 helps lock in the year: thirteen tense days in ''62.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(46,19,0,'Kennedy was assassinated in November 1963, just over a year after the crisis. Think: 1962 = missiles; 1963 = Dallas.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(47,19,1,'The Nuclear Test Ban Treaty is signed in 1963, one year after the crisis — a direct result of both superpowers stepping back from the brink they reached in 1962.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(48,20,0,'Oct 16, 1962 — Kennedy briefed on U-2 spy photos showing Soviet missile sites under construction in Cuba','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(49,20,1,'Oct 22, 1962 — Kennedy''s televised address reveals the crisis; US naval blockade of Cuba begins','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(50,20,2,'Oct 24, 1962 — Soviet cargo ships approach the blockade line, then stop and turn back','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(51,20,3,'Oct 27, 1962 — ''Black Saturday'': a U-2 is shot down over Cuba; another strays into Soviet airspace; war feels imminent','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(52,20,4,'Oct 28, 1962 — Khrushchev announces Soviet missiles will be withdrawn; crisis ends','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(53,21,0,'World War II ends in 1945. Just three years later, in 1948, Israel is established — the Holocaust''s aftermath directly accelerated international support for a Jewish state.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(54,21,1,'The Balfour Declaration, Britain''s pledge of support for a Jewish homeland in Palestine, comes in 1917. Israel''s founding follows 31 years later, in 1948 — roughly a generation from promise to statehood.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(55,22,0,'Mahatma Gandhi is assassinated in India in January 1948, and Israel declares independence in May 1948. Pair ''Gandhi dies'' with ''Israel founded'' to make the year 1948 stick.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(56,22,1,'The Universal Declaration of Human Rights is adopted by the UN in December 1948, the same year Israel is established — two major postwar milestones in international order, months apart.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(57,23,0,'Suez Crisis bridge: Israel''s founding in 1948 was followed by its next major conflict, the Suez Crisis, 8 years later in 1956.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(58,23,1,'Six-Day War anchor: The Six-Day War happens in 1967, 19 years after Israel''s founding. Subtract 19 from 1967 to land on 1948.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(59,23,2,'Camp David Accords anchor: Israel and Egypt sign the Camp David Accords in 1978, 30 years after Israel''s establishment — three decades from founding to its first peace treaty with an Arab neighbor.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(60,24,0,'The Spanish Armada is defeated in 1588, one of Elizabeth''s greatest triumphs. Fifteen years later, in 1603, she dies, having outlived her most famous victory by over a decade.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(61,24,1,'Elizabeth I becomes queen in 1558. She dies 45 years later, in 1603, after one of the longest reigns in English history up to that point.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(62,25,0,'1603 marks a major royal transition: Elizabeth I dies and James VI of Scotland becomes James I of England, beginning the Stuart dynasty. Think ''Elizabeth ends → James begins'' in 1603.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(63,25,1,'1603 sits between two famous landmarks: Elizabeth I dies in 1603, and the Gunpowder Plot to blow up Parliament is uncovered just two years later, in 1605.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(64,26,0,'The Gunpowder Plot is uncovered in 1605, just two years after Elizabeth''s death. Think 1603 → Elizabeth dies; 1605 → Guy Fawkes and the failed plot to blow up Parliament.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(65,26,1,'The English Civil War begins in 1642, 39 years after Elizabeth''s death. The Tudor age ended in 1603; within four decades, England would be fighting a civil war and eventually executing a king.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(66,27,0,'The first Olympic Games are traditionally dated to 776 BCE, just 23 years before Rome''s legendary founding in 753 BCE — two foundational myths of the ancient Mediterranean world, born within a generation of each other.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(67,27,1,'Roman writers linked their city''s origins back to the fall of Troy, traditionally placed around 1184 BCE — over 400 years before Rome''s own legendary founding date.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(68,28,0,'A useful number trick: ''seven-five-three'' — Rome''s traditional story begins in 753 BCE.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(69,28,1,'753 BCE is a purely legendary date, calculated centuries later by the Roman scholar Varro — less a historical fact than a founding myth, similar to how other ancient cultures gave their cities a symbolic origin story.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(70,29,0,'The Roman Republic traditionally began in 509 BCE, 244 years after the founding of Rome. Think 753 BCE → kings; 509 BCE → Republic.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(71,29,1,'Julius Caesar was assassinated in 44 BCE. From Rome''s traditional founding in 753 BCE to Caesar''s death is just over 700 years — a useful reminder of how long the Roman story lasted.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(72,30,0,'Spain becomes a republic in 1931, five years before civil war breaks out in 1936, as tensions between left and right factions build toward open conflict.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(73,30,1,'Hitler comes to power in Germany in 1933. Three years later, in 1936, the Spanish Civil War begins, with Nazi Germany and Fascist Italy supporting Franco''s Nationalists.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(74,31,0,'1936 is also the year Hitler hosts the Berlin Olympics and remilitarizes the Rhineland — the same year fascist and authoritarian forces are testing their strength across Europe, Spain included.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(75,31,1,'The Spanish Civil War begins in 1936, just three years before World War II erupts in 1939. It is often called a dress rehearsal for the larger war soon to follow.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(76,32,0,'World War II begins in 1939, three years after the Spanish Civil War starts. Subtract 3 from 1939 to land on 1936.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(77,32,1,'Franco rules Spain as dictator until his death in 1975, 39 years after the war began in 1936 — the conflict''s winner held power for nearly four decades afterward.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(78,33,0,'Edwin Drake begins drilling near Titusville, Pennsylvania in 1858, using a steam engine borrowed from salt-well drilling techniques. He strikes oil the following year, in 1859.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(79,33,1,'Darwin anchor: Charles Darwin published On the Origin of Species in 1859. Pair ''oil underground'' with ''evolution'' — two revolutionary developments in the same year.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(80,34,0,'1859 is also the year Charles Darwin publishes On the Origin of Species — the same year one discovery reshaped biology while another, quietly in Pennsylvania, was about to reshape energy and industry.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(81,34,1,'1859 sits right before the outbreak of the American Civil War in 1861 — Drake''s well strikes oil just two years before the war that would soon demand more fuel and industry than ever.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(82,35,0,'John D. Rockefeller founds Standard Oil in 1870, eleven years after Drake''s well. Subtract 11 from 1870 to land on 1859.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(83,35,1,'Karl Benz patents the first commercial gasoline automobile in 1886 — add 27 years to Drake''s 1859 discovery to reach the moment oil found its defining new purpose.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(84,36,0,'India''s Chandrayaan-2 attempted a lunar landing in 2019 but its lander crashed during the final descent. Four years later, Chandrayaan-3 achieved the landing in 2023.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(85,36,1,'The first human Moon landing was Apollo 11 in 1969. Chandrayaan-3 came 54 years later, in 2023 — more than half a century after humans first walked on the Moon.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(86,37,0,'2023 is also the year Russia''s Luna-25 mission crashed attempting the same south-pole landing, just days before Chandrayaan-3 succeeded — a striking same-year contrast between failure and success.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(87,37,1,'ChatGPT''s public release caused a massive AI boom starting in late 2022 and through 2023 — the same year India made its own historic technological leap, on the Moon rather than in software.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(88,38,0,'China lands its Chang''e-6 mission on the Moon''s far side in 2024, one year after Chandrayaan-3 — back-to-back lunar milestones from Asian space programs.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(89,38,1,'India plans a crewed Moon landing by 2040. Chandrayaan-3 in 2023 marks the first major stepping stone toward that goal — 17 years before the target.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(90,39,0,'The Seven Years'' War ends in 1763, reshaping global trade and colonial economics. Thirteen years later, in 1776, Smith publishes his landmark critique of mercantilism.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(91,39,1,'The American Revolution began in 1775. One year later, in 1776, Adam Smith published The Wealth of Nations on the very same day the colonies declared independence.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(92,40,0,'1776 is one of the most memorable years in history: the American Declaration of Independence and The Wealth of Nations were both published the same year. Pair ''political freedom'' with ''economic freedom'' — both in 1776.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(93,40,1,'Think 1776 = Jefferson and Adam Smith. The colonies were challenging political authority while Smith was questioning how economies should be organised.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(94,41,0,'The French Revolution begins in 1789, 13 years after Smith''s book, partly fueled by the economic grievances he analyzed. Subtract 13 from 1789 to land on 1776.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(95,41,1,'Smith dies in 1790, just fourteen years after publishing his masterwork — long enough to see it become the foundational text of classical economics.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(96,42,0,'Alexander Fleming started working on bacteriology and antiseptics during World War I. About a decade after the war ends in 1918, his famous accidental discovery in the lab follows from that background — landing in 1928.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(97,42,1,'Charles Lindbergh made the first solo nonstop transatlantic flight in 1927. One year later, in 1928, Fleming discovered penicillin.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(98,43,0,'1928 is also the year Amelia Earhart becomes the first woman to fly across the Atlantic — two very different breakthroughs, one in the sky and one in a petri dish, the same year.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(99,43,1,'1928 is the year of the first Academy Awards ceremony and the signing of the Kellogg-Briand Pact — think ''1928 = penicillin and the beginning of the Hollywood awards era.''','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(100,44,0,'The stock market crashes in 1929, just one year after Fleming discovered penicillin. Think 1928 → penicillin; 1929 → Wall Street crashes.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(101,44,1,'Penicillin isn''t mass-produced until World War II, around 1943 — 15 years after its discovery. Subtract 15 from 1943 to land on 1928.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(102,44,2,'Fleming shares the Nobel Prize in Medicine in 1945, 17 years after his original discovery — it took nearly two decades for the finding to be fully recognized and put to wide use.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(103,45,0,'1928 — Fleming notices a mold (Penicillium notatum) has killed bacteria on a culture plate left near an open window','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(104,45,1,'1929 — Fleming publishes his findings; few scientists take notice, and he cannot isolate the active compound','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(105,45,2,'1939–40 — Howard Florey and Ernst Chain at Oxford purify penicillin and run the first animal tests','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(106,45,3,'1942 — First human patient successfully treated; US and UK governments fund mass production for the war effort','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(107,45,4,'1945 — Fleming, Florey, and Chain share the Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(108,46,0,'Philip II of Macedon is assassinated in 336 BCE, two years before Alexander crosses into Asia in 334 BCE — the young king moves fast, securing Greece and launching his invasion within two years of taking the throne.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(109,46,1,'The Persian Wars, when Greece repelled Persian invasions at Marathon (490 BCE) and Salamis (480 BCE), end more than 140 years before Alexander goes on the offensive in 334 BCE — he''s finally turning the tables on the old invader.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(110,47,0,'334 BCE falls in the same century as Aristotle''s peak teaching years — Aristotle personally tutored Alexander as a boy, and just a few years later his student is crossing into Asia to conquer an empire.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(111,47,1,'334 BCE sits almost exactly 290 years before Julius Caesar''s assassination in 44 BCE — a useful bridge if you know Caesar''s date well.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(112,48,0,'Alexander dies in 323 BCE, just 11 years after beginning his conquests in 334 BCE — one of history''s shortest windows between a campaign''s start and an empire''s peak.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(113,48,1,'The decisive Battle of Gaugamela, which breaks Persian resistance for good, happens in 331 BCE, three years after the campaign begins. Subtract 3 from 331 to land on 334 BCE.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(114,49,0,'336 BCE — Philip II of Macedon is assassinated; Alexander, aged 20, inherits the throne','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(115,49,1,'334 BCE — Alexander crosses the Hellespont into Asia Minor and wins his first major battle against the Persians at the Granicus River','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(116,49,2,'333 BCE — Alexander defeats Darius III at the Battle of Issus, forcing the Persian king to flee','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(117,49,3,'332 BCE — Alexander conquers Egypt without resistance and founds the city of Alexandria','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(118,49,4,'331 BCE — Decisive victory over Darius III at Gaugamela effectively ends the Persian Empire''s resistance','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(119,50,0,'Charles II is restored to the throne in 1660, 28 years before the Glorious Revolution in 1688 — the Stuart monarchy that had been briefly abolished under Cromwell gets deposed again, this time for good, less than three decades later.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(120,50,1,'James II becomes king in 1685, just three years before Parliament invites William of Orange to invade in 1688 — a remarkably short reign before his own subjects push him out.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(121,51,0,'1688 sits almost exactly a century before the French Revolution begins in 1789 — England settles its power struggle between Crown and Parliament peacefully, roughly 100 years before France does it violently.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(122,51,1,'1688 falls 39 years after the execution of Charles I in 1649 — father beheaded by Parliament, son restored and later deposed by it, all within one Stuart family saga.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(123,52,0,'The English Bill of Rights is passed in 1689, one year after William and Mary take the throne. Subtract 1 from 1689 to land on 1688.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(124,52,1,'The Act of Union merges England and Scotland into Great Britain in 1707, 19 years after the Glorious Revolution — the new constitutional settlement of 1688 held firm long enough to absorb an even bigger political change two decades later.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(125,53,0,'1685 — James II, a Catholic, becomes king, alarming a largely Protestant Parliament','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(126,53,1,'June 1688 — James II''s son is born, raising fears of a Catholic dynasty; Parliament invites William of Orange to intervene','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(127,53,2,'Nov 1688 — William lands at Torbay with an invasion force; James II''s support collapses almost immediately','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(128,53,3,'Dec 1688 — James II flees to France without a major battle being fought','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(129,53,4,'Feb 1689 — William and Mary are jointly declared king and queen after accepting the Bill of Rights','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(130,54,0,'Bartolomeu Dias rounds the Cape of Good Hope in 1488, proving Africa''s southern tip could be sailed around. Ten years later, in 1498, da Gama finishes the job and reaches India.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(131,54,1,'Columbus sails west and reaches the Americas in 1492, still believing he''d found a route to Asia. Six years later, in 1498, da Gama actually gets there, by sailing the opposite direction around Africa.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(132,55,0,'1498 falls just six years after Columbus''s famous 1492 voyage — two competing routes to Asia, one west and one around Africa, discovered within a single decade.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(133,55,1,'1498 is only four years after the Treaty of Tordesillas in 1494, when Spain and Portugal carved up the unexplored world between them — da Gama''s voyage delivers on Portugal''s half of that bargain.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(134,56,0,'The Portuguese establish their trading colony at Goa in India in 1510, 12 years after da Gama''s voyage. Subtract 12 from 1510 to land on 1498.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(135,56,1,'Magellan''s expedition completes the first circumnavigation of the globe in 1522, 24 years after da Gama''s sea route to India — the Age of Exploration''s early breakthrough leads to its ultimate proof that the world could be sailed around entirely.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(136,57,0,'1497 — Vasco da Gama departs Lisbon with four ships, tasked with finding a sea route to India','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(137,57,1,'Nov 1497 — Da Gama rounds the Cape of Good Hope, following the path Dias had charted a decade earlier','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(138,57,2,'Apr 1498 — With the help of a local pilot, da Gama''s fleet crosses the Indian Ocean from East Africa','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(139,57,3,'May 1498 — Da Gama arrives at Calicut on India''s southwest coast, completing the first all-sea route from Europe to Asia','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(140,57,4,'1499 — Da Gama returns to Portugal, having lost half his crew and two of his four ships, but proving the route was viable','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(141,58,0,'The Wall Street Crash hits in 1929, four years before Hitler takes power in 1933. Mass unemployment and economic collapse in Germany during those years fuel the Nazi Party''s rapid rise.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(142,58,1,'Hitler''s failed Beer Hall Putsch happens in 1923, exactly ten years before he''s legally appointed Chancellor in 1933 — he goes from attempting a coup and landing in prison to reaching power through the ballot box a decade later.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(143,59,0,'1933 is also the year Franklin D. Roosevelt takes office as US President and launches the New Deal — two very different responses to the same Great Depression, on opposite sides of the Atlantic, the same year.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(144,59,1,'1933 falls 15 years after the end of World War I in 1918 — the harsh terms of that war''s peace treaty are still fueling German resentment when Hitler takes power a generation later.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(145,60,0,'Germany invades Poland in 1939, six years after Hitler becomes Chancellor, starting World War II. Subtract 6 from 1939 to land on 1933.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(146,60,1,'Hitler dies by suicide in 1945, 12 years after taking power, as the Nazi regime collapses — a twelve-year span from appointment to total defeat.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(147,61,0,'1929 — The Great Depression begins, devastating the German economy and boosting support for extremist parties','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(148,61,1,'Jul 1932 — The Nazi Party becomes the largest party in the Reichstag, though still short of a majority','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(149,61,2,'Jan 30, 1933 — President Hindenburg appoints Hitler as Chancellor, believing conservative politicians could control him','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(150,61,3,'Feb 1933 — The Reichstag Fire is used as a pretext to suspend civil liberties and arrest political opponents','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(151,61,4,'Mar 1933 — The Enabling Act passes, granting Hitler dictatorial powers and effectively ending German democracy','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(152,62,0,'Indian National Congress anchor: The INC is founded in 1885, giving Indian nationalism its first organized political voice. Twenty years later, in 1905, Curzon''s partition transforms Congress from a moderate group into a mass nationalist movement.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(153,62,1,'Queen Victoria dies in 1901. Just four years into the new Edwardian era, in 1905, the Partition of Bengal ignites the Swadeshi movement — an early crack in British authority.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(154,63,0,'1905 is also the year of the Russian Revolution of 1905, when workers and peasants rise against the Tsar — the same year colonial subjects in Bengal rise against British rule, half a world apart.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(155,63,1,'Einstein publishes his special theory of relativity in 1905, his ''miracle year.'' The same year, a very different kind of upheaval — political rather than scientific — reshapes Bengal.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(156,64,0,'The All-India Muslim League is founded just one year later, in 1906 in Dhaka — the Partition of Bengal directly catalyzed the communal politics that would shape the subcontinent for decades.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(157,64,1,'The partition is reversed in 1911, six years later, under massive public pressure — a rare colonial reversal. The same year, the British shift their imperial capital from Calcutta to Delhi. Subtract 6 from 1911 to land on 1905.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(158,64,2,'Gandhi returns to India in 1915, ten years after the partition, and later builds directly on the Swadeshi boycott tactics pioneered in 1905 for his own independence campaigns.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(159,65,0,'America''s centennial gift: The telephone is invented in 1876 — exactly 100 years after the Declaration of Independence in 1776. The United States turns 100 and gets the telephone. Now the president can make calls.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(160,65,1,'Telegraph came first — subtract 32 years: Morse demonstrated the electric telegraph in 1844. Bell patents the telephone 32 years later in 1876, turning dots and dashes into a real human voice.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(161,66,0,'The Centennial Exhibition: The 1876 World''s Fair in Philadelphia was held specifically to celebrate the USA''s 100th birthday — and Bell demonstrated the telephone there. The invention and the anniversary were literally at the same party.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(162,67,0,'Edison''s phonograph one year later: Bell patents the telephone in 1876; Edison records sound on the phonograph in 1877. Two consecutive years, two ways of capturing the human voice.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(163,67,1,'Marconi''s wireless radio in 1895 — 19 years later: telephone (wired voice, 1876) → radio (wireless signal, 1895). Add roughly 20 years to get from Bell to wireless.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(164,68,0,'1633 is too early — that''s the growth phase, not the peak: The first enslaved Africans arrive in British Virginia in 1619, and the trade expands steadily through the 1600s. But the massive sugar, tobacco, and rice plantation economies of the Caribbean and American South don''t reach full scale until the mid-1700s. 1633 is near the start of the ramp-up, not the top.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(165,68,1,'The sugar boom drives the peak: Caribbean sugar plantations explode in scale from the late 1600s onward. By 1750, Britain, France, and Portugal are all running plantation systems at maximum capacity — that''s what pushes the trade to 80,000+ Africans transported per year.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(166,69,0,'Midpoint of the 18th century: 1750 is exactly halfway through the 1700s — the century the trade will be abolished in. The trade peaks at the precise midpoint of the century that ends it.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(167,69,1,'Enlightenment irony: Montesquieu criticises slavery in 1748, just two years before the trade reaches its highest volume. The Age of Reason and the peak of the slave trade occupy the exact same moment.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(168,70,0,'American Revolution 26 years later: The Declaration of Independence proclaims ''all men are created equal'' in 1776 — just 26 years after the trade peaks. The same plantation economy that drives the 1750 peak funds much of the colonial wealth that makes the revolution possible.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(169,70,1,'British abolition in 1807 — 57 years later: Peak (1750) → ban (1807). The abolitionist movement builds for half a century before Parliament acts. Subtract 57 years from 1807 to land on the peak.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(170,71,0,'Don''t confuse 588 and 550: Babylon destroyed Jerusalem''s Temple in 588 BCE — 38 years before Cyrus founds the Persian Empire. The sequence runs 588 → 550 → 539: Babylon crushes Jerusalem, then Cyrus builds Persia, then Cyrus conquers Babylon and frees those same exiles.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(171,71,1,'Axial Age cluster: Confucius was born in 551 BCE — almost the exact moment Cyrus launches the Persian Empire in 550 BCE. Buddha was born around 563 BCE. Three world-changers all appear within a single decade in the 550s–560s BCE.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(172,72,0,'Midpoint anchor: 550 BCE is exactly halfway between 600 BCE and 500 BCE — the precise midpoint of the 6th century BCE. Put Cyrus in the dead centre of the 500s BCE.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(173,72,1,'Double-nickel: 5-5-0. The Persian Empire starts at a double-nickel date, not a round 500 or 600.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(174,73,0,'Edict of Cyrus — 11 years later: Cyrus founds Persia in 550 BCE, conquers Babylon in 539 BCE (11 years later), and immediately frees the Jewish exiles. Short chain: 550 → 539 → end of the exile.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(175,73,1,'Marathon anchor: The Battle of Marathon is 490 BCE. Subtract exactly 60 years → 550 BCE. The empire Cyrus builds in 550 is the same one that invades Greece 60 years later.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(176,74,0,'Same-digits trick: the Olympics begin in 776 BCE. Flip to 776 CE, then add 1,000 years → 1776, the American Declaration of Independence. Put a 1 in front of 776 and you land on a date you already know.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(177,74,1,'Rome anchor: Rome''s legendary founding is 753 BCE. The first Olympics came 23 years earlier, in 776 BCE, so Greece was already holding games before Rome existed.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(178,75,0,'Older idea, safer trick: inoculating people with real smallpox (variolation) reached England in 1721, brought by Lady Mary Wortley Montagu from the Ottoman Empire. Jenner''s 1796 breakthrough was swapping in harmless cowpox, 75 years later.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(179,75,1,'Revolution anchor: Declaration of Independence 1776 → add 20 years → 1796. Smallpox was the great killer of that era: in 1777 George Washington had his army inoculated the old, risky way, with real smallpox. Jenner''s safe cowpox version arrived 19 years later.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(180,76,0,'George Washington gives his Farewell Address in 1796, the same year Jenner vaccinates 8-year-old James Phipps. Think founding-fathers era, not Victorian.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(181,76,1,'Seven years after the Bastille (1789), a young Napoleon launches his Italian campaign in 1796. Vaccination is born in the age of revolutions.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(182,77,0,'Why it feels too early: Jenner had no idea what germs were. Pasteur''s germ theory came in the 1860s and viruses weren''t discovered until the 1890s. The vaccine came first; the science explaining it came 70–100 years later.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(183,77,1,'Smallpox was declared eradicated in 1980. Subtract 184 years → 1796. Less than two centuries from the first vaccine to wiping out the disease.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(184,77,2,'Pasteur''s rabies vaccine (1885) came 89 years after Jenner. Pasteur named all such treatments vaccines in Jenner''s honor, from vacca, Latin for cow.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(185,78,0,'Challenger exploded on launch in January 1986. Add 17 years → 2003, when Columbia broke up on reentry. Two shuttles lost, one on the way up and one on the way down.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(186,78,1,'Columbia was the very first shuttle to reach space, in April 1981. It flew for 22 years before it was lost in February 2003, on its 28th mission.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(187,79,0,'The US-led invasion of Iraq began in March 2003, about seven weeks after Columbia was lost on February 1. Both happened early in George W. Bush''s first term, in the shadow of 9/11 (2001).','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(188,79,1,'Space race flip: in October 2003, eight months after Columbia, China flew its first astronaut, Yang Liwei. One country''s shuttles were grounded the same year another sent its first person into orbit.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(189,79,2,'Concorde, the supersonic airliner, made its last commercial flight in October 2003. Two icons of 1970s flying machines faded out in the same year.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(190,80,0,'The shuttle program ended in July 2011 with Atlantis. Subtract 8 years → 2003. Columbia''s loss was the beginning of the end for the shuttle.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(191,80,1,'The shuttles returned to flight with Discovery in July 2005, after about two and a half years on the ground. Count back from 2005 → early 2003.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(192,81,0,'Crowns first, Parliaments later: when Elizabeth I died in 1603, James VI of Scotland also became James I of England. One king, two countries. Add 104 years → 1707, when the two Parliaments finally merged too.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(193,81,1,'Shakespeare''s era to Newton''s: Shakespeare wrote for James I after the 1603 crown union, and Newton published the Principia in 1687. Add 20 years to the Principia → 1707. Great Britain was born in Newton''s lifetime.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(194,82,0,'Two great scientists were born in 1707: Carl Linnaeus, who gave living things their two-part Latin names, and the mathematician Leonhard Euler. The year Great Britain was born, so were the men who named nature and wrote much of modern math.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(195,82,1,'The Mughal emperor Aurangzeb died in 1707 and his empire began to break apart. That same year Britain unites. One empire starts to fade as the island that would later rule India comes together.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(196,83,0,'Declaration of Independence 1776 → subtract 69 years → 1707. The American colonists broke away from a Great Britain that was less than 70 years old.','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(197,83,1,'Ireland joins in 1801 to make the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland. Subtract 94 years → 1707. First Great Britain (1707), then the United Kingdom (1801).','imported');
INSERT INTO "learning_content_items" VALUES(198,83,2,'Scotland voted on leaving the union in 2014 and stayed. Subtract 307 years → 1707. The union was just past its 300th birthday.','imported');
